/api.github.com/users/willgriffin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/commits/d0c297d0d89acaf0f503f5fdb2d175551af547cf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T03:12:42Z","email":"willgriffin@gmail.com","name":"Will Griffin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T03:12:42Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(cli): serialize concurrent db:migrate runs with a PostgreSQL advisory lock (#3640)\n\n* fix(cli): serialize concurrent db:migrate runs with a PostgreSQL advisory lock\n\nTwo processes running `smrt db:migrate` against one database (two\nworkloads gating startup on the migration, a rolling restart, a Job beside\nrunning pods) both compared the live schema, planned the same batch, and\nthe loser failed with 42701/42P07 \"already exists\" or a 40P01 deadlock.\n\nA non-dry-run db:migrate on PostgreSQL now takes a session advisory lock\n(core acquireMigrationLock) on a pinned connection before system-table\nbootstrap and schema comparison and holds it until the run ends. A\nconcurrent run waits (logged, bounded by\nmigrations.postgres.migrationLockTimeout, default 15min), then compares a\ncurrent schema and applies nothing. The lock dies with its connection, so\na killed migrator never strands it.\n\nFixes #3634\n\n* fix(cli): stop db:migrate when its migration lock is lost mid-run\n\nReview of #3634: if the pinned lock connection dies (failover, an\nidle-connection reaper, a terminated backend) PostgreSQL frees the lock\nwhile the run keeps applying on its pool, so a second migrator could race\nit again with no signal. MigrationLock.assertHeld() probes pg_locks on the\npinned session; db:migrate calls it before applying and before the\npost-apply contract check and fails with MigrationLockLostError. The lock\nsession also exempts itself from idle_session_timeout (PostgreSQL 14+).\n\nRefs #3634","tree":{"sha":"16d1175134185861d73f58e3084da082412b3060","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/git/trees/16d1175134185861d73f58e3084da082412b3060"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/git/commits/d0c297d0d89acaf0f503f5fdb2d175551af547cf","verification":{"payload":"tree 16d1175134185861d73f58e3084da082412b3060\nparent c0fed7f30b25e9d03da0cf88211c558c37dbf7ad\nauthor Will Griffin <willgriffin@gmail.com> 1791342762 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791342762 +0000\n\nfix(cli): serialize concurrent db:migrate runs with a PostgreSQL advisory lock (#3640)\n\n* fix(cli): serialize concurrent db:migrate runs with a PostgreSQL advisory lock\n\nTwo processes running `smrt db:migrate` against one database (two\nworkloads gating startup on the migration, a rolling restart, a Job beside\nrunning pods) both compared the live schema, planned the same batch, and\nthe loser failed with 42701/42P07 \"already exists\" or a 40P01 deadlock.\n\nA non-dry-run db:migrate on PostgreSQL now takes a session advisory lock\n(core acquireMigrationLock) on a pinned connection before system-table\nbootstrap and schema comparison and holds it until the run ends. A\nconcurrent run waits (logged, bounded by\nmigrations.postgres.migrationLockTimeout, default 15min), then compares a\ncurrent schema and applies nothing. The lock dies with its connection, so\na killed migrator never strands it.\n\nFixes #3634\n\n* fix(cli): stop db:migrate when its migration lock is lost mid-run\n\nReview of #3634: if the pinned lock connection dies (failover, an\nidle-connection reaper, a terminated backend) PostgreSQL frees the lock\nwhile the run keeps applying on its pool, so a second migrator could race\nit again with no signal. MigrationLock.assertHeld() probes pg_locks on the\npinned session; db:migrate calls it before applying and before the\npost-apply contract check and fails with MigrationLockLostError. The lock\nsession also exempts itself from idle_session_timeout (PostgreSQL 14+).\n\nRefs #3634","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxbi7CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAcVwQAFDnwZ8G/Q/DKCn8F/GvPuVo\nPGapc0NSGohFwi7v/AFXud+me3nhOCX7xbW3LFbVgZjmfmW6VL8ADt6d3SgGAQ4M\n7Zuns+Fyhc1M1cvbKpzWN3mNi1eZ1WFsbVeQyccR8AWO+zngfwXK3UOLX4qaQJRW\nlUhrfXvufScF4o0HaQsjIzIlqs1RLpgSOIC6N/A2k0W9oktTHU7c+AXSACA/knOM\nBAYEPRDiG4Yq2+EfSCF/pLsQgavn7pYdqj6CBy1fI8QZrjIpNBBWWLiX4YjRBNd5\ndKQTL7pGEBUCrw1BXvOWDiC05WyWTtvEaBfCAaUC1z7anrlRixUCxxKk3jrEa8xj\nmR0rCZgnNb7VRODC9xNhvy34+yxEuwUY6qwUtxTGSoTKIEVSa7MM2BKm6y8Z0PTY\nfYdKKNaXel+7OyZHy4hyvud57quC8M/V5zSfbhULFeu3WrBY/d0W2d2H+9M2xcXI\nU4cTcnpu9cST+J8BFSy5KVdSmdjcQrE7XBy8y/qcF9tw/c1PQaw2FLuPdjSAuNJf\nFB5gP1KAoVybnvOAtN9bLm50881iusStHOdAbp3f4qWAjBetLyAxiRTR5eT19WL4\n5o4N21HvVXlB0XQtKxpOV5N0bu/TaZFuQJfKoHBX8PWRWpXiGTWKi5KApOzQYGYv\nCVFT8EZyItIxZafgk7PK\n=zPNu\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T03:12:59Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/happyvertical/smrt/commit/d0c297d0d89acaf0f503f5fdb2d175551af547cf","node_id"