wDOQDruXtoAKDQ4NzY0NWRkZWQ2MGIwYjc0YWRmZTI3NzRmNDBkODFmZjllNDY0MjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/happyvertical/smrt/commit/9cfc044607523a643787d8b6b8126045e1cf42f8","sha":"9cfc044607523a643787d8b6b8126045e1cf42f8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/commits/9cfc044607523a643787d8b6b8126045e1cf42f8"}],"sha":"487645dded60b0b74adfe2774f40d81ff9e46420","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/commits/487645dded60b0b74adfe2774f40d81ff9e46420"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/590602?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/willgriffin","id":590602,"login":"willgriffin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU5MDYwMg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/commits/9cfc044607523a643787d8b6b8126045e1cf42f8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T22:57:05Z","email":"willgriffin@gmail.com","name":"Will Griffin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T22:57:05Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(core): user-facing help for SmrtRecipe (#3597)\n\n* feat(core): add SmrtRecipe, declared units of app functionality\n\nA recipe is a SmrtRecipe subclass with static id, label, summary,\nsynonyms, models, nav, requires, and options. The scanner matches the\nimport binding (aliases and namespaces included), reads the statics\nstructurally, resolves model class references to qualified names, and\nvalidates the set at build time. Recipes are emitted as a top-level\nrecipes array in manifest.json and smrt-knowledge.json.\n\nCloses #3590\n\n* feat(commerce): declare customers, vendors, sales, purchases recipes\n\nFour minimal recipes (headers only): commerce.customers,\ncommerce.vendors, commerce.sales (requires customers), and\ncommerce.purchases (requires vendors).\n\nRefs #3590\n\n* feat(commerce): hide and lock the discriminator in sales and purchases\n\nSales and purchases recipes now carry options that hide and lock the\ncontractType discriminator and the other party''s id, and label and\norder the party field, matching the shape smrt-planner consumes.\n\nRefs #3590\n\n* fix(core): reject indirect recipes, typo''d excludes, prefix specifiers\n\nReview findings on the recipe matcher: report a recipe that extends\nanother recipe or is declared as a class expression instead of\ndropping it; require exposure excludes to be non-empty and name a CRUD\nverb or a model method; match the smrt-core specifier exactly.\n\nRefs #3590\n\n* fix(core): accept inherited methods in recipe exposure excludes\n\nRecipe exposure excludes now resolve public instance methods across the\nmodel''s inheritance chain, and the docs state that cross-file recipe\nsubclasses are not detected.\n\nRefs #3590\n\n* fix(core): validate recipe option fields against the merged manifest\n\nField names in recipe options are now checked after inherited fields\nmerge, so STI-merged, tenant, and framework-base fields such as\nparentId are accepted. Outside-glob recipe discovery no longer depends\non the agentSurface option and reports unreadable files.\n\nRefs #3590\n\n* docs(core): reattach orphaned manifest-generator doc blocks\n\nTwo JSDoc blocks (FRAMEWORK_ABSTRACT_BASE_NAMES, assertQualifiedNameAliases)\nwere separated from their declarations by the #3590 recipe additions.\n\n* feat(core): user-facing help for SmrtRecipe\n\nA recipe may declare `static help = ''./x.recipe.md''`. The scanner reads the\nfile at build time and emits `help: { markdown, fieldRefs }` on the recipe in\nthe manifest and knowledge artifact; fieldRefs is derived, never authored.\nManifest generation fails on references to undeclared fields and on a\nfieldRefs list that disagrees with the Markdown. Knowledge fields now carry\ntheir @field description.\n\ncore ships a browser-safe renderer (renderHelp, helpToMarkdown, validateHelp)\nthat resolves {field:x} to effective labels, drops blocks tied to hidden,\ndisabled or advanced fields, prunes emptied headings, builds the glossary\nand a collapsed \"Connect other tools\" section. Output is an AST of text\nnodes, never HTML.\n\nRefs #3591\n\n* feat(commerce): help and field descriptions for the commerce recipes\n\nAdd user-facing help (customers, vendors, sales, purchases .recipe.md) and\n@field descriptions for the fields those recipes show, upstreamed from the\nsmrt-planner prose and adjusted to the real enums and statuses.\n\nCloses #3591\n\n* fix(core): reject help references to sensitive fields\n\nReview of #3591 found that help naming a sensitive field passes the build\nbut names a field the knowledge artifact excludes, so a host building its\nfield list from it silently drops that step. Reject such references at\nmanifest generation, reword the two commerce steps, include both lists in\nthe fieldRefs mismatch error, neutralise the Contract descriptions inherited\nby every STI subtype, and document that help files are not rescanned.\n\nRefs #3591\n\n* fix(core): keep universal fields out of recipe help references\n\nUniversal fields (id, slug, ...) are not manifest fields, so they never reach\nthe knowledge artifact and a host building its field list from it would drop\na step that names one. Validate help references against declared fields only.\n\nRefs #3591","tree":{"sha":"07c08ea43c4d87778dab7397d35444a74177a1ba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/git/trees/07c08ea43c4d87778dab7397d35444a74177a1ba"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/git/commits/9cfc044607523a643787d8b6b8126045e1cf42f8","verification":{"payload":"tree 07c08ea43c4d87778dab7397d35444a74177a1ba\nparent d523ac298fc40a7dd729f9cad873db07f4156a74\nauthor Will Griffin <willgriffin@gmail.com> 1791327425 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791327425 +0000\n\nfeat(core): user-facing help for SmrtRecipe (#3597)\n\n* feat(core): add SmrtRecipe, declared units of app functionality\n\nA recipe is a SmrtRecipe subclass with static id, label, summary,\nsynonyms, models, nav, requires, and options. The scanner matches the\nimport binding (aliases and namespaces included), reads the statics\nstructurally, resolves model class references to qualified names, and\nvalidates the set at build time. Recipes are emitted as a top-level\nrecipes array in manifest.json and smrt-knowledge.json.\n\nCloses #3590\n\n* feat(commerce): declare customers, vendors, sales, purchases recipes\n\nFour minimal recipes (headers only): commerce.customers,\ncommerce.vendors, commerce.sales (requires customers), and\ncommerce.purchases (requires vendors).\n\nRefs #3590\n\n* feat(commerce): hide and lock the discriminator in sales and purchases\n\nSales and purchases recipes now carry options that hide and lock the\ncontractType discriminator and the other party''s id, and label and\norder the party field, matching the shape smrt-planner consumes.\n\nRefs #3590\n\n* fix(core): reject indirect recipes, typo''d excludes, prefix specifiers\n\nReview findings on the recipe matcher: report a recipe that extends\nanother recipe or is declared as a class expression instead of\ndropping it; require exposure excludes to be non-empty and name a CRUD\nverb or a model method; match the smrt-core specifier exactly.\n\nRefs #3590\n\n* fix(core): accept inherited methods in recipe exposure excludes\n\nRecipe exposure excludes now resolve public instance methods across the\nmodel''s inheritance chain, and the docs state that cross-file recipe\nsubclasses are not detected.\n\nRefs #3590\n\n* fix(core): validate recipe option fields against the merged manifest\n\nField names in recipe options are now checked after inherited fields\nmerge, so STI-merged, tenant, and framework-base fields such as\nparentId are accepted. Outside-glob recipe discovery no longer depends\non the agentSurface option and reports unreadable files.\n\nRefs #3590\n\n* docs(core): reattach orphaned manifest-generator doc blocks\n\nTwo JSDoc blocks (FRAMEWORK_ABSTRACT_BASE_NAMES, assertQualifiedNameAliases)\nwere separated from their declarations by the #3590 recipe additions.\n\n* feat(core): user-facing help for SmrtRecipe\n\nA recipe may declare `static help = ''./x.recipe.md''`. The scanner reads the\nfile at build time and emits `help: { markdown, fieldRefs }` on the recipe in\nthe manifest and knowledge artifact; fieldRefs is derived, never authored.\nManifest generation fails on references to undeclared fields and on a\nfieldRefs list that disagrees with the Markdown. Knowledge fields now carry\ntheir @field description.\n\ncore ships a browser-safe renderer (renderHelp, helpToMarkdown, validateHelp)\nthat resolves {field:x} to effective labels, drops blocks tied to hidden,\ndisabled or advanced fields, prunes emptied headings, builds the glossary\nand a collapsed \"Connect other tools\" section. Output is an AST of text\nnodes, never HTML.\n\nRefs #3591\n\n* feat(commerce): help and field descriptions for the commerce recipes\n\nAdd user-facing help (customers, vendors, sales, purchases .recipe.md) and\n@field descriptions for the fields those recipes show, upstreamed from the\nsmrt-planner prose and adjusted to the real enums and statuses.\n\nCloses #3591\n\n* fix(core): reject help references to sensitive fields\n\nReview of #3591 found that help naming a sensitive field passes the build\nbut names a field the knowledge artifact excludes, so a host building its\nfield list from it silently drops that step. Reject such references at\nmanifest generation, reword the two commerce steps, include both lists in\nthe fieldRefs mismatch error, neutralise the Contract descriptions inherited\nby every STI subtype, and document that help files are not rescanned.\n\nRefs #3591\n\n* fix(core): keep universal fields out of recipe help references\n\nUniversal fields (id, slug, ...) are not manifest fields, so they never reach\nthe knowledge artifact and a host building its field list from it would drop\na step that names one. Validate help references against declared fields only.\n\nRefs #3591","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxXzRCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAbu0QABDyEBgkJYSofnFr0dqpRD5h\nikP4BiV3XVnekEecdQeRqRV9xUK6+zxt07kaM2VKi9LY9B/2Sz1PYpp7Ia6gS+xh\nDSE2W9CTjdNVJOOPXoW1ke4bwA6pFtD+RxMC2MuUx4aSZ2PuPcJ4qHOJzgEbPifp\n6U5FEj6D4yNP8XbcjC6kV99NEj4coaqsYzAPFS30hCiyMh9LdGsdSfY+Of8pEhlS\nX/ffDmZZcWN0aq4QbwrZtxB1IGNnwvahMvrlzuxSV8/olkOLInZYTWYFPmu6BMKR\ncGgXpZ7jXox4Ae5ATO51mKsML8IWCKDoJ21vUxGm9Ac4taZcufAAreuZ95qlegJY\nqXAwRdTbYi/OAK9+qX4vWOswj5f+2ni9M2TkJba/STEUGQRYSJfWvmoIEIT83g4j\ni8bV68B4xxEDYnye1eysG4bqDtjkVFRV8PUIbyJ62uZeGoi5+cEO6xHHyJYS1xiw\nUgCgqGbeRXi9mWtMLpKae+WWHznZqtLzdU9rqJwG0CHD79CmWrFvcY/kpOzNhxUj\nCjcR4YwNaiDd20qRtO0FKIr7aI+OKGXlNBwjl5fs8jJUh/7M1SxGBXcbWxcgvNkf\n/+GkDEmrA1Ra7w2sbgSr5qEIOkghHC+KUew9RmN3WMcafbzBw8NDnUGvhkiUQjTT\nOzX/SXkHu228p5e8afMI\n=RTD3\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T22:57:21Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_ur