n/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/willgriffin","id":590602,"login":"willgriffin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU5MDYwMg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/commits/3dfbc8f703be8b78900927b770a73de939b1e576/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T20:43:27Z","email":"willgriffin@gmail.com","name":"Will Griffin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T20:43:27Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(users): publish the OIDC client landing-URL registration contract (#3570)\n\nKanidm discards a pending authorization whenever the user detours through\nits own /ui/login (e.g. \"Return to Login\" after a mistyped password) and\nthen strands the user in its apps panel. The client''s landing URL is the\nonly way back, so it must be the app''s login start route.\n\nAdd loginPath and getOidcClientRegistration() to smrt-users/sveltekit so\napps derive the redirect and landing URLs from the same options the route\nhandlers use, and document the Kanidm registration.\n\nRefs #3569","tree":{"sha":"a6b815dabb4c2c59893df4e66e7e18e750d54f32","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/git/trees/a6b815dabb4c2c59893df4e66e7e18e750d54f32"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/git/commits/3dfbc8f703be8b78900927b770a73de939b1e576","verification":{"payload":"tree a6b815dabb4c2c59893df4e66e7e18e750d54f32\nparent 5ba9e01b6e2aa0d1746fabeb7ac673893ce9c4dd\nauthor Will Griffin <willgriffin@gmail.com> 1791319407 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791319407 +0000\n\nfeat(users): publish the OIDC client landing-URL registration contract (#3570)\n\nKanidm discards a pending authorization whenever the user detours through\nits own /ui/login (e.g. \"Return to Login\" after a mistyped password) and\nthen strands the user in its apps panel. The client''s landing URL is the\nonly way back, so it must be the app''s login start route.\n\nAdd loginPath and getOidcClientRegistration() to smrt-users/sveltekit so\napps derive the redirect and landing URLs from the same options the route\nhandlers use, and document the Kanidm registration.\n\nRefs #3569","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxWEqCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA1LMQAIuoHuKt7O9NalfsTw3uoQBO\nJiNrD0K+Z11b6K3YsY7eg4lrf+4n5EqaL/khV6UHNshLEK6jTv4lV8pV9LhukE6Q\nQFiXZ2LqCYlTvdehab/RXCa1lrCIxmCvn8It1sy0CqCljYq/25m5mdGBctesGzkS\nUAKJc21SXKitaisSLbD+pHYD9SZMKO+CfxzlMY2XRuJY616+zHlcTsLRtyQiOjX7\nG2tCXChSqoCDDJ9QQuhe5tvdmzS6XnoiE6YBtiO5GO8bqRmBuz+L2iKt7jiiMT5p\nkthoDeHxMmLoA07d5JwDCEALkdTpA1c37PwlYxdp3EHHzSWZew/IwP2f57By+y6M\nPUpcstbtLT8c+g6yvKQm/NcrGUXS23E0zfUSHSydeDqubTkxH5j9o17kiEQEh8gd\nhUFVmzeB96rZQ7bkFExO+vXKDMIbjuY20XQsd/NhQ2EO8z74wykIej6/CDsRarqw\nRb7sg/LTPtyB1ux1Hj8lFT+oCELh2He8N+Kor1OD/WbAuhTFhv2B2l5KFaOhkTSe\nIKBy+9MbI6CE8aaPHau29waUwstJiqSm45isfm7aTRCKyvTgMEsGUov0xX+RTnPb\n03658msIYwa47K2mriVNT2UrCf+JY8PRZuMtzGiureDICCahB/TBmKJTXOue0SLJ\n2q5x22N3p2f+/CNaOdld\n=Cks1\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T20:59:23Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/happyvertical/smrt/commit/3dfbc8f703be8b78900927b770a73de939b1e576","node_id":"C_kwDOQDruXtoAKDNkZmJjOGY3MDNiZThiNzg5MDA5MjdiNzcwYTczZGU5MzliMWU1NzY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/happyvertical/smrt/commit/5ba9e01b6e2aa0d1746fabeb7ac673893ce9c4dd","sha":"5ba9e01b6e2aa0d1746fabeb7ac673893ce9c4dd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/commits/5ba9e01b6e2aa0d1746fabeb7ac673893ce9c4dd"}],"sha":"3dfbc8f703be8b78900927b770a73de939b1e576","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/commits/3dfbc8f703be8b78900927b770a73de939b1e576"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/590602?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/willgriffin","id":590602,"login":"willgriffin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU5MDYwMg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/commits/5ba9e01b6e2aa0d1746fabeb7ac673893ce9c4dd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T20:43:19Z","email":"willgriffin@gmail.com","name":"Will Griffin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T20:43:19Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs(adr): ADR 0003 — smrt add declarative package install (#3378) (#3565)\n\n* docs(adr): ADR 0003 — smrt add declarative package install\n\nAnswers the six design questions of #3378 from a hand-add of\n@happyvertical/smrt-content to a throwaway smrt-start copy and a working\ncatch-all mount prototype:\n\n- descriptor home: an authored smrt-package.json exported by the package,\n  with a JSON Schema (docs/adr/0003-smrt-package.schema.json) and its\n  TypeScript type; app state in smrt.config.ts (consumer.routes,\n  consumer.mount, assistant.allowedTools);\n- routes: one catch-all route rendering registered pages, checked against\n  SvelteKit 2.70.3 precedence, SSR, layouts, per-page load and actions;\n  thin route files only on eject;\n- assistant tools: suggested in the plan, granted only by name;\n- extension scaffolds, removal and drift findings, day-one coverage, the\n  plan/apply/remove CLI contract and its invariants.\n\nAdds the reference descriptor for smrt-content as an inert draft (not in\nfiles or exports, so not published) and indexes the ADR in CONTEXT-MAP.\n\nRefs #3378\n\n* docs(adr): write extension files before build and migrate in smrt add apply\n\nReview finding F1 on ADR 0003: the apply order built and migrated before\nwriting --extend/--eject files, so a reference scaffold''s table could not be\nin the manifest that migration reads and the final plan could not be empty.\nFiles now come before the build, and a resume table states what a re-run\ndoes after an interruption at each step boundary.\n\nRefs #3378\n\n* docs(adr): close the $mount value set in the package descriptor schema\n\nReview finding F2 on ADR 0003: an object such as {\"$mount\": \"routesBsae\"}\nvalidated through the unrestricted JSON branch of `props`, so the closed set\nof mount expressions was not enforced. jsonValue now rejects any object with\na `$mount` key at any depth, mountValue enumerates routesBase, navigation and\nthe href:<page id> pattern, and the ADR states the semantic rule that an\nhref target must name a page in the same descriptor.\n\nRefs #3378\n\n* docs(adr): link the filed implementation issues from ADR 0003\n\nRefs #3378","tree":{"sha":"d6e128cc502cc02c8055652f8f6a318e3e83c911","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/git/trees/d6e128cc502cc02c8055652f8f6a318e3e83c911"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/git/commits/5ba9e01b6e2aa0d1746fabeb7ac673893ce9c4dd","verification":{"payload":"tree d6e128cc502cc02c8055652f8f6a318e3e83c911\nparent a8c092613749c9abb0913cb47ee00e76bf0169a4\nauthor Will Griffin <willgriffin@gmail.com> 1791319399 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791319399 +0000\n\ndocs(adr): ADR 0003 — smrt add declarative package install (#3378) (#3565)\n\n* docs(adr): ADR 0003 — smrt add declarative package install\n\nAnswers the six design questions of #3378 from a hand-add of\n@happyvertical/smrt-content to a throwaway smrt-start copy and a working\ncatch-all mount prototype:\n\n- descriptor home: an authored smrt-package.json exported by the package,\n  with a JSON Schema (docs/adr/0003-smrt-package.schema.json) and its\n  TypeScript type; app state in smrt.config.ts (consumer.routes,\n  consumer.mount, assistant.allowedTools);\n- routes: one catch-all route rendering registered pages, checked against\n  SvelteKit 2.70.3 precedence, SSR, layouts, per-page load and actions;\n  thin route files only on eject;\n- assistant tools: suggested in the plan, granted only by name;\n- extension scaffolds, removal and drift findings, day-one coverage, the\n  plan/apply/remove CLI contract and its invariants.\n\nAdds the reference descriptor for smrt-content as an inert draft (not in\nfiles or exports, so not published) and indexes the ADR in CONTEXT-MAP.\n\nRefs #3378\n\n* docs(adr): write extension files before build and migrate in smrt add apply\n\nReview finding F1 on ADR 0003: the apply order built and migrated before\nwriting --extend/--eject files, so a reference scaffold''s table could not be\nin the manifest that migration reads and the final plan could not be empty.\nFiles now come before the build, and a resume table states what a re-run\ndoes after an interruption at each step boundary.\n\nRefs #3378\n\n* docs(adr): close the $mount value set in the package descriptor schema\n\nReview finding F2 on ADR 0003: an object such as {\"$mount\": \"routesBsae\"}\nvalidated through the unrestricted JSON branch of `props`, so the closed set\nof mount expressions was not enforced. jsonValue now rejects any object with\na `$mount` key at any depth, mountValue enumerates routesBase, navigation and\nthe href:<page id> pattern, and the ADR states the semantic rule that an\nhref target must name a page in the same descriptor.\n\nRefs #3378\n\n* docs(adr): link the filed implementation issues from ADR 0003\n\nRefs #3378","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxV13CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAiYcQAIcJEm4JpAKCGps4L2yWUj46\nKW93VkjRg6WaNL63tSfHYMQ+D5fnOzsP2kcUtLy82JgbBIqTwhh8BYLbRp56mAFR\nDk4KhuzsxMry9AtpcpPBxyD+i0iB5B4he3OZkrk7RppnWK6bBR63AZXK4ieNm3d6\nDLYSo2mnP+qxdUQslCWQZhit3UP2yuiq9Dw8Huj/ikNrYSYEhx7b/ODCGG0Dqa+Z\npi2rZinjoFQ5VcrkcbqUgm5IqWJi68w5cvyxRqh1PEXOTQCYuWIlU6aKkX34bJNb\nQZgaO355UIUhgWrBDMaW3YpB2HeHSSzGtSFAVsdKMpGhPyPqzo6Ii00ga28zbDOa\neuEHRLkRiXjvGdf7l+1zAS89am2X3RGxfl7jdUdILuRP9E9Nz1CC2wkhjwPaTeiw\n/JKKUVUEUUHbY8o3Fquug12lDO7w5/nbx20FTXxcQTqLMqkzu0JpxnV87C088Abd\nIhN2BJ7MX/ZJ9e/4wTpNy1oMC8oIk9+NG/2orqmwhKFCYq9RgWIoTE+IaG2mn9xu\nd3rA8em0uXSbpLwV7hvfcLgge0lsEk2SLsboGn4rG2/4eyhleaAZM