D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/happyvertical/smrt/commit/27b2e8becba900a81ec0f45a2d74f0a46267801c","node_id":"C_kwDOQDruXtoAKDI3YjJlOGJlY2JhOTAwYTgxZWMwZjQ1YTJkNzRmMGE0NjI2NzgwMWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/happyvertical/smrt/commit/3612749e155f8799499b24c606c6a4c19aa066e4","sha":"3612749e155f8799499b24c606c6a4c19aa066e4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/commits/3612749e155f8799499b24c606c6a4c19aa066e4"}],"sha":"27b2e8becba900a81ec0f45a2d74f0a46267801c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/commits/27b2e8becba900a81ec0f45a2d74f0a46267801c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/590602?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/willgriffin","id":590602,"login":"willgriffin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU5MDYwMg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/commits/3612749e155f8799499b24c606c6a4c19aa066e4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T19:14:31Z","email":"willgriffin@gmail.com","name":"Will Griffin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T19:14:31Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(core,cli): redact database URLs in every banner, log and error (#3587)\n\n* fix(core,cli): redact database URLs in every banner, log and error\n\nRoute the CLI connect banner, db:* headers, verbose database log and\nDatabaseError.connectionFailed through one smrt-core helper pair\n(redactDatabaseUrl / redactDatabaseUrlsInText): scheme, user, host, port\nand database at most; no password, no query string, and never the raw\nstring when it cannot be parsed. smrt-dev-mcp''s mirror (no runtime core\ndependency) gains the same secret-key predicate and always scrubs\nembedded userinfo.\n\nRefs #3527\n\n* fix(core,cli): load the redaction helpers from a dependency-free core subpath\n\nCommand tests mock the smrt-core root module; importing the helpers from\n@happyvertical/smrt-core/utils/database-url keeps them real everywhere.\n\nRefs #3527\n\n* fix(core): never let a digits-then-delimiter password parse as a port\n\nA password like owner:2024/Xy9@host parsed as host owner, port 2024 and\nkept the password in the path. Trust a direct parse only when the @ sits\ninside the authority; otherwise strip userinfo first, and never render a\npath that still holds an @.\n\nRefs #3527\n\n* fix(core): treat any stray @ outside the userinfo as unparseable\n\nowner:pa@rt#secret@host parsed with host rt, a password fragment. An @\nleft in the path, query or fragment after parsing is ambiguous, so the\ndisplay falls back to the scheme-only unparseable form.\n\nRefs #3527","tree":{"sha":"c84b3513217bb415c8b8cb253b2f8a5ac3b046b3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/git/trees/c84b3513217bb415c8b8cb253b2f8a5ac3b046b3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/git/commits/3612749e155f8799499b24c606c6a4c19aa066e4","verification":{"payload":"tree c84b3513217bb415c8b8cb253b2f8a5ac3b046b3\nparent 5df6d7cf68fd9f7d713fb7f774ea803ae9181cc2\nauthor Will Griffin <willgriffin@gmail.com> 1791314071 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791314071 +0000\n\nfix(core,cli): redact database URLs in every banner, log and error (#3587)\n\n* fix(core,cli): redact database URLs in every banner, log and error\n\nRoute the CLI connect banner, db:* headers, verbose database log and\nDatabaseError.connectionFailed through one smrt-core helper pair\n(redactDatabaseUrl / redactDatabaseUrlsInText): scheme, user, host, port\nand database at most; no password, no query string, and never the raw\nstring when it cannot be parsed. smrt-dev-mcp''s mirror (no runtime core\ndependency) gains the same secret-key predicate and always scrubs\nembedded userinfo.\n\nRefs #3527\n\n* fix(core,cli): load the redaction helpers from a dependency-free core subpath\n\nCommand tests mock the smrt-core root module; importing the helpers from\n@happyvertical/smrt-core/utils/database-url keeps them real everywhere.\n\nRefs #3527\n\n* fix(core): never let a digits-then-delimiter password parse as a port\n\nA password like owner:2024/Xy9@host parsed as host owner, port 2024 and\nkept the password in the path. Trust a direct parse only when the @ sits\ninside the authority; otherwise strip userinfo first, and never render a\npath that still holds an @.\n\nRefs #3527\n\n* fix(core): treat any stray @ outside the userinfo as unparseable\n\nowner:pa@rt#secret@host parsed with host rt, a password fragment. An @\nleft in the path, query or fragment after parsing is ambiguous, so the\ndisplay falls back to the scheme-only unparseable form.\n\nRefs #3527","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxUioCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAclAQAJgGp3kweP8nJlSX4gaKuNQw\nbNC6PTqYgosyX9tGcFDpY5pEZKEphsYStJGJ6JE0nFnT16xWdBdHDAnbHiU2Wv02\nz0VoMTVFZSCc6Ep1ElQieGnua4dM+NKuFS2NIJhggwR5F98rgK0ygmw/hOTGfTRv\nm6wm8oX/91yihzB0Oa66r2UhOKWQZ1izhJUMucZcN1RQzD2vPbM/K3IRea2oiZGJ\nFTvogFEONVSqYQ/qsstfxFN9p5e83buQX4dAN4fyYcVmBjYRAPe1fmTGbI94Ut7h\nv2kjzkN8eEiM5Feyhlk6l5j0uWyvpVH8N13Z7fn+8nbXk8trzTmuHUSxtT63/oNF\nY91aIyyHr3QBVCplQ6tcO