il":"willgriffin@gmail.com","name":"Will Griffin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T04:03:08Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(users): password credential and SvelteKit password sign-in (#3274) (#3511)\n\n* feat(users): password credential and SvelteKit password sign-in (#3274)\n\nAdds UsersPasswordCredential, its own sensitive object (one row per person,\nno generated api/mcp/cli surface, out of the change feed), and\nPasswordCredentialService:\n\n- scrypt from node:crypto with a random per-hash salt and the parameters\n  encoded in each hash; timingSafeEqual verify; a dummy-hash verify for an\n  unknown email or a user without a password; rehash under the current\n  policy after a successful sign-in through a guarded UPDATE that never\n  overwrites a rotated password.\n- Policy: minLength 10, maxLength 256 (ceiling 1024, refused before\n  hashing), NFKC normalization, a small built-in denylist plus a consumer\n  denylist and reject() hook, the person''s own email refused, no\n  composition rules.\n- signIn: emailKey normalization, LoginAttemptLimiter reservation per\n  account and per client address before any work, ACTIVE user and ACTIVE\n  tenant membership required, never creates a user, one\n  PasswordCredentialError for every refusal, SessionService.createSession\n  with authMethod ''password'', a post-mint generation re-check, and\n  revocation of the browser''s previous session.\n- setPassword (first password by the person, or an admin), changePassword\n  (current password through the sign-in budget; ends every other session),\n  resetPassword (admin, never self; ends every session; mustChange yields\n  an empty-ceiling session that can only change the password),\n  clearPassword. users.password.manage follows the PIN''s single-tenant\n  target rule; layered (PIN) sessions never manage passwords.\n- createPasswordCredentialHandlers for SvelteKit: cookie-setting sign-in\n  (JSON or form), identical 401s, 429 + Retry-After, no-store, and\n  locals-based management handlers.\n\nThe PIN''s scrypt helpers move to a shared credential-hash module, and\nSessionService.destroyAllUserSessions gains exceptSessionId, reading\nsession ids through the unbounded raw query.\n\nRefs #3274\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(users): note the emailKey backfill prerequisite for password sign-in\n\nRefs #3274\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(users): guard self-service password writes and equalize legacy-hash work (#3274)\n\nReview round 1 findings:\n\n- changePassword and a self clearPassword now write through\n  replaceIfCurrent/deleteIfCurrent, guarded on the exact credential row and\n  hash the person proved; a first self-set is insert-only. A reset that lands\n  in between is never overwritten under the old password.\n- Every write that ends sessions sweeps them before and after the\n  credential write, so a failure between the two leaves the person signed out.\n- Verification against a stored hash with weaker scrypt parameters than the\n  policy is padded with scrypt work up to the policy''s cost, so a wrong\n  password on a not-yet-upgraded account costs what an unknown account does.\n- A sign-in missing its email or password is reserved and failed through the\n  limiter instead of being refused before the reservation.\n\nRefs #3274\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(users): bound scrypt padding memory and sweep sessions on a raced admin first-set (#3274)\n\nReview round 2 findings:\n\n- scryptPaddingParams now pads in the policy''s own memory shape: whole\n  lanes as one derivation at the policy''s N and r with up to policy.p lanes,\n  the remainder as at most six single-lane derivations at the policy''s r with\n  halving N. Every generated parameter set is valid and never touches more\n  memory than one current-policy verification, including p increases.\n- An administrator''s setPassword that saw no password inserts insert-only;\n  if a first password landed meanwhile it takes the replacement path, which\n  sweeps the person''s sessions before and after the write.\n- scrypt maxmem accounts for p.\n\nRefs #3274\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5df26366668f188201f2b6cf3ee89973a14f8e16","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/git/trees/5df26366668f188201f2b6cf3ee89973a14f8e16"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/git/commits/b2ba7f3e221609c7c91ecbbb15948c5481bb071d","verification":{"payload":"tree 5df26366668f188201f2b6cf3ee89973a14f8e16\nparent 3197324f84439f4ec516828149f72857585f1693\nauthor Will Griffin <willgriffin@gmail.com> 1791172988 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791172988 +0000\n\nfeat(users): password credential and SvelteKit password sign-in (#3274) (#3511)\n\n* feat(users): password credential and SvelteKit password sign-in (#3274)\n\nAdds UsersPasswordCredential, its own sensitive object (one row per person,\nno generated api/mcp/cli surface, out of the change feed), and\nPasswordCredentialService:\n\n- scrypt from node:crypto with a random per-hash salt and the parameters\n  encoded in each hash; timingSafeEqual verify; a dummy-hash verify for an\n  unknown email or a user without a password; rehash under the current\n  policy after a successful sign-in through a guarded UPDATE that never\n  overwrites a rotated password.\n- Policy: minLength 10, maxLength 256 (ceiling 1024, refused before\n  hashing), NFKC normalization, a small built-in denylist plus a consumer\n  denylist and reject() hook, the person''s own email refused, no\n  composition rules.\n- signIn: emailKey normalization, LoginAttemptLimiter reservation per\n  account and per client address before any work, ACTIVE user and ACTIVE\n  tenant membership required, never creates a user, one\n  PasswordCredentialError for every refusal, SessionService.createSession\n  with authMethod ''password'', a post-mint generation re-check, and\n  revocation of the browser''s previous session.\n- setPassword (first password by the person, or an admin), changePassword\n  (current password through the sign-in budget; ends every other session),\n  resetPassword (admin, never self; ends every session; mustChange yields\n  an empty-ceiling session that can only change the password),\n  clearPassword. users.password.manage follows the PIN''s single-tenant\n  target rule; layered (PIN) sessions never manage passwords.\n- createPasswordCredentialHandlers for SvelteKit: cookie-setting sign-in\n  (JSON or form), identical 401s, 429 + Retry-After, no-store, and\n  locals-based management handlers.\n\nThe PIN''s scrypt helpers move to a shared credential-hash module, and\nSessionService.destroyAllUserSessions gains exceptSessionId, reading\nsession ids through the unbounded raw query.\n\nRefs #3274\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(users): note the emailKey backfill prerequisite for password sign-in\n\nRefs #3274\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(users): guard self-service password writes and equalize legacy-hash work (#3274)\n\nReview round 1 findings:\n\n- changePassword and a self clearPassword now write through\n  replaceIfCurrent/deleteIfCurrent, guarded on the exact credential row and\n  hash the person proved; a first self-set is insert-only. A reset that lands\n  in between is never overwritten under the old password.\n- Every write that ends sessions sweeps them before and after the\n  credential write, so a failure between the two leaves the person signed out.\n- Verification against a stored hash with weaker scrypt parameters than the\n  policy is padded with scrypt work up to the policy''s cost, so a wrong\n  password on a not-yet-upgraded account costs what an unknown account does.\n- A sign-in missing its email or password is reserved and failed through the\n  limiter instead of being refused before the reservation.\n\nRefs #3274\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(users): bound scrypt padding memory and sweep sessions on a raced admin first-set (#3274)\n\nReview round 2 findings:\n\n- scryptPaddingParams now pads in the policy''s own memory shape: whole\n  lanes as one derivation at the policy''s N and r with up to policy.p lanes,\n  the remainder as at most six single-lane derivations at the policy''s r with\n  halving N. Every generated parameter set is valid and never touches more\n  memory than one current-policy verification, including p increases.\n- An administrator''s setPassword that saw no password inserts insert-only;\n  if a first password landed meanwhile it takes the replacement path, which\n  sweeps the person''s sessions before and after the write.\n- scrypt maxmem accounts for p.\n\nRefs #3274\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwyGMCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAp4sQAFydk31pnoCOsEDMs/yVXw0s\ngbKcHfC8OttmMT1B6KV/y3qtNHje4hzzCDaQnCgwW+pN1+Tu0FtsWidPzrciLexm\nOaHCAbgELcnDRxNbZXUseHVIHPcoGHXHbs3HfndDPF1jbQ1I6nxQu/iVWSY5eSF5\n5GTYnId2C1Wbb2VH8A3cuAs6wK3446paydx/xkJf1o2YF/+QgqW+Jov5fVrNR1Co\njR83Cc1UmptmdFK04/FvfDpiE++DiD4KvdbYWN0de0kEBwfowMf7W31J3l5Xta4x\nTWYsGU5q0wnz8Wa7VaxlljbhD1lzVZWosQUGvpXluIUKxvBDxVXi/0C9Islvb5p9\n8KWRa7dBjTkRRrThmrllwTPTqwfStq5uv8pMhsfnJNz8SVTAEmYquM9NzvO/08dH\nn2BbwT+lLtJLiutRf4Dl5oOgTvvhwbHkkUtQE60RNLlFxg/aN8t06qdB7e9Fe/aX\n9CD8uXEsM74Dr3JeSkBNaOtiHhiK1dpmUUguxVuVJ08BTmw4IR28cccTPdUvCREL\nxTJVzTgiM8Z3wZfLxstsldFdVDUv+76FUNG1NKh124Nly4avIRE3H6AYE9oWInHb\nwjVCaPasfPZSjkZ5nLxh4SwzYSiyyXmEVd97mtvyk77WUJ0yKJj8GYXw61+WKj6o\n/RiUxGaS7vjwMD3rwDeY\n=nQgs\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-05T04:03:25Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_u