84cbec8c1dc1","sha":"f578c8890b228815f21ed8c712f984cbec8c1dc1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/commits/f578c8890b228815f21ed8c712f984cbec8c1dc1"}],"sha":"55bd09fecc6a3bac2d7f99d3551c10e821a7b6f7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/commits/55bd09fecc6a3bac2d7f99d3551c10e821a7b6f7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/590602?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/willgriffin","id":590602,"login":"willgriffin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU5MDYwMg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/commits/f578c8890b228815f21ed8c712f984cbec8c1dc1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T15:33:33Z","email":"willgriffin@gmail.com","name":"Will Griffin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T15:33:33Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(manufacturing)!: rebuild AssemblyForm on smrt-ui and drop smrt-fields (#3493)\n\n* feat(manufacturing)!: rebuild AssemblyForm on smrt-ui and drop smrt-fields\n\nAssemblyForm is now a purpose-built, props-driven form on smrt-ui /forms\ncontrols, modelled on OperationForm: assembly, onsubmit, oncancel, loading,\noperations, currency, hiddenFields and readonlyFields. The default operation\nis a picker over the active operations the host passes; a retired or unlisted\ncurrent operation stays selected, marked, and can be cleared. AssemblyList\nreads a structural policy type instead of importing smrt-fields.\n\n@happyvertical/smrt-fields is removed from the package''s dependencies.\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: AssemblyForm no longer wraps smrt-fields ObjectForm. The\nfields, policy, value, isNewRecord, disabled, showModeSwitch, actions and\nonsubmit(SubmitEvent) props are replaced; see the package README.\n\nCloses #3492\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(manufacturing): AssemblyForm passes protected fields through as stored\n\nHidden and read-only fields were re-trimmed and re-split on submit; they now\nkeep their exact initial value.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(manufacturing): AssemblyForm price follows the currency and untouched fields persist\n\nThe price is typed and checked with the currency''s minor-unit exponent, a\nnegative stored price keeps its sign, and a field the reader leaves as it was\nis returned exactly as stored (comma-containing tags, padded text).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(manufacturing): AssemblyForm re-shows the stored price when the currency changes\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0858aeefd8b2195a99646c66e33d871991a81962","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/git/trees/0858aeefd8b2195a99646c66e33d871991a81962"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/git/commits/f578c8890b228815f21ed8c712f984cbec8c1dc1","verification":{"payload":"tree 0858aeefd8b2195a99646c66e33d871991a81962\nparent ce07fa79b86a251a32ca3c2d530dbd82e1d4be8d\nauthor Will Griffin <willgriffin@gmail.com> 1791128013 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791128013 +0000\n\nfeat(manufacturing)!: rebuild AssemblyForm on smrt-ui and drop smrt-fields (#3493)\n\n* feat(manufacturing)!: rebuild AssemblyForm on smrt-ui and drop smrt-fields\n\nAssemblyForm is now a purpose-built, props-driven form on smrt-ui /forms\ncontrols, modelled on OperationForm: assembly, onsubmit, oncancel, loading,\noperations, currency, hiddenFields and readonlyFields. The default operation\nis a picker over the active operations the host passes; a retired or unlisted\ncurrent operation stays selected, marked, and can be cleared. AssemblyList\nreads a structural policy type instead of importing smrt-fields.\n\n@happyvertical/smrt-fields is removed from the package''s dependencies.\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: AssemblyForm no longer wraps smrt-fields ObjectForm. The\nfields, policy, value, isNewRecord, disabled, showModeSwitch, actions and\nonsubmit(SubmitEvent) props are replaced; see the package README.\n\nCloses #3492\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(manufacturing): AssemblyForm passes protected fields through as stored\n\nHidden and read-only fields were re-trimmed and re-split on submit; they now\nkeep their exact initial value.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(manufacturing): AssemblyForm price follows the currency and untouched fields persist\n\nThe price is typed and checked with the currency''s minor-unit exponent, a\nnegative stored price keeps its sign, and a field the reader leaves as it was\nis returned exactly as stored (comma-containing tags, padded text).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(manufacturing): AssemblyForm re-shows the stored price when the currency changes\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwnKlCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAkh4QAGuloFg7GiGRH8nrDwwkuZkh\neA6c3jzJZtXM+