ubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/happyvertical/smrt/commit/ea840768b4337b0a0fe8f9ef9bcbd6ba108d63ce","node_id":"C_kwDOQDruXtoAKGVhODQwNzY4YjQzMzdiMGEwZmU4ZjllZjliY2JkNmJhMTA4ZDYzY2U","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/happyvertical/smrt/commit/43350fcb96b0450fc8dc2b996652844e28a377fd","sha":"43350fcb96b0450fc8dc2b996652844e28a377fd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/commits/43350fcb96b0450fc8dc2b996652844e28a377fd"}],"sha":"ea840768b4337b0a0fe8f9ef9bcbd6ba108d63ce","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/commits/ea840768b4337b0a0fe8f9ef9bcbd6ba108d63ce"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/590602?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/willgriffin","id":590602,"login":"willgriffin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU5MDYwMg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/commits/43350fcb96b0450fc8dc2b996652844e28a377fd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T10:49:49Z","email":"willgriffin@gmail.com","name":"Will Griffin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T10:49:49Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(manufacturing): multi-level bills of materials and production runs (#3484)\n\n* feat(manufacturing): walk sub-assemblies and record production runs\n\nMulti-level bills: every BomService method takes { levels } (one level by\ndefault, unchanged). explode returns each line with its level, path and\nquantity, waste compounding down the levels, plus rolled-up totals;\nplanRequirements nets the walk against stock (available, short, and what\nbuilding a short sub-assembly takes) and canProduce reports shortages at\nthe level they occur. Cost and labour roll up the same walk. A loop\nalready in stored data fails with BomStructureCycleError; depth and size\nare bounded.\n\nProductionRun and ProductionRunCompletion record a build against a bill\n(target, completed, status, dated completions). ProductionRunService\nserializes concurrent completions on the run row and can consume and\nproduce stock through ProductionService in the same transaction, only\nwhen asked. ProductionRunList and RequirementsTree are the views.\n\nRefs #3444\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(manufacturing): document multi-level walks and production runs\n\nRefs #3444\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(manufacturing): walk only the top bill''s tenant''s lines\n\nA multi-level walk now reads a bill''s lines the way AssemblyService reads\na structure: the top bill''s tenant and global lines, whatever tenant\ncontext is active.\n\nRefs #3444\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(manufacturing): plan with the bill''s tenant''s stock; exact run targets\n\nplanRequirements counts only the top bill''s tenant''s stock rows and\nglobal ones, whatever tenant context is active, as the walk reads its\nstructure. Quantity comparisons on production runs (and the plan''s\nshortfall) allow only floating-point rounding, a few units in the last\nplace, instead of a relative 1e-9 that let a large run pass its target.\n\nRefs #3444\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(manufacturing): note that a plan reads the bill''s tenant''s stock\n\nRefs #3444\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(manufacturing): keep quantities to six decimals and compare exactly\n\nA tolerance that scales with the value still hid a whole unit at large\nbut exactly representable quantities. Run targets, completions and a\nplan''s shortfall are now rounded to QUANTITY_DECIMALS (6) places through\ntheir decimal representation and compared exactly, in the service and in\nthe list''s validation.\n\nRefs #3444\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(manufacturing): sum run quantities as exact millionths up to a bound\n\nRounding the sum after a binary addition could not recover a fraction\nlost against large progress. Runs now add and compare target, completed\nquantity and reports as whole millionths, exactly, and accept quantities\nup to MAX_QUANTITY (999,999,999), where every six-place value survives a\ndouble; larger ones are refused. The list''s validation matches.\n\nRefs #3444\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(manufacturing): pin runs, completions and their stock to the bill''s tenant\n\ncreateRun resolves a product''s bill in the active tenant (global bills\nonly without one) and refuses another tenant''s bill; the run takes its\nbill''s tenant, a completion the run''s, and the stock legs run in the\nrun''s tenant whatever the caller''s context. The walk shows the top\nproduct''s name only when that tenant may see it. Tests cover two tenants\nwith the same SKU codes and a run recorded without a tenant context.\n\nRefs #3444\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(manufacturing): consume only a bill''s own tenant''s lines\n\nProductionService.consumeMaterials (and so runProduction and a run''s\ncompletion) now reads a bill''s lines the way a structure is read: the\nbill''s tenant''s lines and global ones. A global run recorded without a\ntenant context no longer consumes a line another tenant wrote against\nthe bill.\n\nRefs #3444\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(manufacturing): read structures as the owner''s and global rows\n\nUnder a tenant context the interceptor hid global rows (a shared\ncomponent, a global bill, global stock); without one it showed every\ntenant''s. Walks, plans, run creation, consumption and AssemblyService''s\nexplicit-tenant reads now list through withTenantGlobalRead for the\nowning tenant and keep own-or-global rows. Without a tenant context,\ncreateRun accepts global bills only.\n\nA sub-assembly bill in another currency is no longer added to a cost or\nlabour total, and remainingQty and the list''s message are rounded to the\nsix-decimal quantity precision.\n\nRefs #3444\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(manufacturing): read routings and the top bill as owner''s and global rows\n\nA global sub-assembly''s global routing and operations were hidden under\na tenant context, so its labour counted as zero; a global top bill was\nnot found there. Both are now read through the tenant-plus-global scope.\n\nRefs #3444\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(manufacturing): read a bill''s lines as owner''s and global rows everywhere\n\nThe single-level explodeRequirements, computeMaterialCost and canProduce\nread lines in the ambient context, so a global bill found from a tenant\ncontext had no lines. They now read the bill''s own tenant''s and global\nlines, like the walks.\n\nRefs #3444\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d0429a82405a9cbb2d724a0aca0f0161456fac37","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/git/trees/d0429a82405a9cbb2d724a0aca0f0161456fac37"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/git/commits/43350fcb96b0450fc8dc2b996652844e28a377fd","verification":{"payload":"tree d0429a82405a9cbb2d724a0aca0f0161456fac37\nparent ba4eb20430d2c9e5e7a32099b045a00435c67991\nauthor Will Griffin <willgriffin@gmail.com> 1791110989 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791110989 +0000\n\nfeat(manufacturing): multi-level bills of materials and production runs (#3484)\n\n* feat(manufacturing): walk sub-assemblies and record production runs\n\nMulti-level bills: every BomService method takes { levels } (one level by\ndefault, unchanged). explode returns each line with its level, path and\nquantity, waste compounding down the levels, plus rolled-up totals;\nplanRequirements nets the walk against stock (available, short, and what\nbuilding a short sub-assembly takes) and canProduce reports shortages at\nthe level they occur. Cost and labour roll up the same walk. A loop\nalready in stored data fails with BomStructureCycleError; depth and size\nare bounded.\n\nProductionRun and ProductionRunCompletion record a build against a bill\n(target, completed, status, dated completions). ProductionRunService\nserializes concurrent completions on the run row and can consume and\nproduce stock through ProductionService in the same transaction, only\nwhen asked. ProductionRunList and RequirementsTree are the views.\n\nRefs #3444\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(manufacturing): document multi-level walks and production runs\n\nRefs #3444\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(manufacturing): walk only the top bill''s tenant''s lines\n\nA multi-level walk now reads a bill''s lines the way AssemblyService reads\na structure: the top bill''s tenant and global lines, whatever tenant\ncontext is active.\n\nRefs #3444\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(manufacturing): plan with the bill''s tenant''s stock; exact run targets\n\nplanRequirements counts only the top bill''s tenant''s stock rows and\nglobal ones, whatever tenant context is active, as the walk reads its\nstructure. Quantity comparisons on production runs (and the plan''s\nshortfall) allow only floating-point rounding, a few units in the last\nplace, instead of a relative 1e-9 that let a large run pass its target.\n\nRefs #3444\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(manufacturing): note that a plan reads the bill''s tenant''s stock\n\nRefs #3444\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(manufacturing): keep quantities to six decimals and compare exactly\n\nA tolerance that scales with the value still hid a whole unit at large\nbut exactly representable quantities. Run targets, completions and a\nplan''s shortfall are now rounded to QUANTITY_DECIMALS (6) places through\ntheir decimal representation and compared exactly, in the service and in\nthe list''s validation.\n\nRefs #3444\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(manufacturing): sum run quantities as exact millionths up to a bound\n\nRounding the sum after a binary addition could not recover a fraction\nlost against large progress. Runs now add and compare target, completed\nquantity and reports as whole millionths, exactly, and accept quantities\nup to MAX_QUANTITY (999,999,999), where every six-place value survives a\ndouble; larger ones are refused. The list''s validation matches.\n\nRefs #3444\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(manufacturing): pin runs, completions and their stock to the bill''s tenant\n\ncreateRun resolves a product''s bill in the active tenant (global bills\nonly without one) and refuses another tenant''s bill; the run takes its\nbill''s tenant, a completion the run''s, and the stock legs run in the\nrun''s tenant whatever the caller''s context. The walk shows the top\nproduct''s name only when that tenant may see it. Tests cover two tenants\nwith the same SKU codes and a run recorded without a tenant context.\n\nRefs #3444\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(manufacturing): consume only a bill''s own tenant''s lines\n\nProductionService.consumeMaterials (and so runProduction and a run''s\ncompletion) now reads a bill''s lines the way a structure is read: the\nbill''s tenant''s lines and global ones. A global run recorded without a\ntenant context no longer consumes a line another tenant wrote against\nthe bill.\n\nRefs #3444\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(manufacturing): read structures as the owner''s and global rows\n\nUnder a tenant context the interceptor hid global rows (a shared\ncomponent, a global bill, global stock); without one it showed every\ntenant''s. Walks, plans, run creation, consumption and AssemblyService''s\nexplicit-tenant reads now list through withTenantGlobalRead for the\nowning tenant and keep own-or-global rows. Without a tenant context,\ncreateRun accepts global bills only.\n\nA sub-assembly bill in another currency is no longer added to a cost or\nlabour total, and remainingQty and the list''s message are rounded to the\nsix-decimal quantity precision.\n\nRefs #3444\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(manufacturing): read routings and the top bill as owner''s and global rows\n\nA global sub-assembly''s global routing and operations were hidden under\na tenant context, so its labour counted as zero; a global top bill was\nnot found there. Both are now read through the tenant-plus-global scope.\n\nRefs #3444\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(manufacturing): read a bill''s lines as owner''s and global rows everywhere\n\nThe single-level explodeRequirements, computeMaterialCost and canProduce\nread lines in the ambient context, so a global bill found from a tenant\ncontext had no lines. They now read the bill''s own tenant''s and global\nlines, like the walks.\n\nRefs #3444\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwi9dCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAacgQACO8YMOpKBMvJIbNm9+n8uvN\nt0wVHY+tTiKnM2MAnAooU0TSM54VmLKEk5Tfz3fmCOhKjgUOz3WjGDTj0js/Q6yQ\nTjKtM7GWNvjubGeRIqmb+QyElUpMDSEiTMcoCW1FfMX45DWk3co40eWDx/HLLDK8\nadGbC9GCtgmIC5O/WXibSLPybqmkGKT4ngbYYunFj7pvX9Fayo36poq6Y7yjvlLF\np6geTli8tNXsqx8D+S4C08Jqs/xhxZJoFetmcHE6s50wjfnr+JqH3D2L+67nyxW1\nq6t9eaSYWYxsBUrqUcXQ7KhVlnyEauIa3HuTF8VYcbDjHXsXBd99UJDpIlFGD2T8\n8szJYc1/QlyLxbIgiCyKbySUhwoJMu3zy47xUgIFJTrPr7ug1W0dUc0t5UUbd6uU\nnzgCHm7R/VZ2Iua25kXC7LR5cUCJVYmez+X/trYEF2LpyG/Q4mKx5i/QrF8Gn1sP\nL9+BwL5yBgzENGkxcBRwy6TRCVxgcd8ktd5F+QGX692eJ7UFhBMG1LNtS9LxTf0/\n4A64HsflQ8BmJtxi7Ojv78Pz5h/+/6Puw71/3L9J48Ea/Sqq/Mj9KdNOo+fDHwjm\nRjKGpqXZpIK3j0o7bfNB201vUriu3bcMUCORkrubznuopnyJ0KNiJKEUY9MK1Jex\nRtLQJdAIY6lsYLlUJH9i\n=gdir\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-04T10:50:05Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/