":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/commits/ba4eb20430d2c9e5e7a32099b045a00435c67991/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T10:02:29Z","email":"41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"github-actions[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T10:02:29Z","email":"41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"github-actions[bot]"},"message":"chore(release): v0.53.5 [skip ci]","tree":{"sha":"79f3476ce09661d5e23f0238764d73fb30816a5a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/git/trees/79f3476ce09661d5e23f0238764d73fb30816a5a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/git/commits/ba4eb20430d2c9e5e7a32099b045a00435c67991","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","id":41898282,"login":"github-actions[bot]","node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/happyvertical/smrt/commit/ba4eb20430d2c9e5e7a32099b045a00435c67991","node_id":"C_kwDOQDruXtoAKGJhNGViMjA0MzBkMmM5ZTVlN2EzMjA5OWIwNDVhMDA0MzVjNjc5OTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/happyvertical/smrt/commit/fac4bd614f1566d2f3cf22d0cceb0df540d2ae7b","sha":"fac4bd614f1566d2f3cf22d0cceb0df540d2ae7b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/commits/fac4bd614f1566d2f3cf22d0cceb0df540d2ae7b"}],"sha":"ba4eb20430d2c9e5e7a32099b045a00435c67991","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/commits/ba4eb20430d2c9e5e7a32099b045a00435c67991"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/590602?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/willgriffin","id":590602,"login":"willgriffin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU5MDYwMg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/commits/fac4bd614f1566d2f3cf22d0cceb0df540d2ae7b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T09:32:07Z","email":"willgriffin@gmail.com","name":"Will Griffin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T09:32:07Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(manufacturing): add Assembly, the product that is made, with bill editor (#3482)\n\n* feat(products): add the assembly product type\n\nAssembly, the made counterpart to Material, is defined in smrt-manufacturing;\nthe discriminator value lives with the others so catalog code can filter by it.\n\nRefs #3455\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(manufacturing): add Assembly, the component resolver and cycle refusal\n\nAssembly extends smrt-products Product (STI, product type assembly) with\nestimatedLabourMinutes, defaultOperationId and partReference columns.\nAssemblyService resolves a component SKU to an assembly and its active bill,\na material, a bought item or missing, and BomLine and active\nBillOfMaterials saves refuse a loop with a BomCycleError naming the path.\n\nRefs #3455\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(manufacturing): add assembly list, form and bill editor components\n\nAssemblyList and AssemblyForm follow the consumer''s field policy (the form is\nsmrt-fields ObjectForm); BomEditor edits a bill''s lines and expands each\nsub-assembly to its own bill, read-only, through loadBill.\n\nRefs #3455\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(manufacturing): check a stored bill''s lines when an upsert activates it\n\nSaving a new active bill with an existing (productId, version, tenantId)\nupserts onto the stored bill, so the activation check now includes its lines.\n\nRefs #3455\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(manufacturing): share one database across AssemblyService collections\n\nA config object such as :memory: is now resolved once, so the SKU, product and\nbill collections read the same database.\n\nRefs #3455\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(manufacturing): reference an assembly''s default operation by foreign key\n\nOperation now lives in this package, so defaultOperationId is a nullable\n@foreignKey(''Operation'') rather than a plain string.\n\nRefs #3455\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(manufacturing): cover the assembly slots in the UI registration test\n\nThe svelte entry now registers the operation and assembly components together.\n\nRefs #3455\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(manufacturing): match the active tenant when an upsert activates a bill\n\nValidation runs before the tenancy interceptor stamps tenantId, so the stored\nbill a natural-key save will adopt is matched against the active tenant.\n\nRefs #3455\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(manufacturing): read a bill''s own tenant''s structure in the cycle walk\n\nA shared assembly''s active bill is chosen among the walking bill''s tenant''s\nbills, so writes made without a tenant context neither refuse a safe line nor\nmiss a loop because of another tenant''s higher version.\n\nRefs #3455\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(manufacturing): hide the assembly name in the list when the policy hides it\n\nRefs #3455\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(manufacturing): reference the default operation by class with RESTRICT\n\nFollows RoutingStep.operationId now that Operation is on main: operations are\nretired, never deleted.\n\nRefs #3455\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(manufacturing): report another tenant''s SKU as missing in a tenant walk\n\nWith an explicit tenantId, resolveComponent treats a SKU, product or bill line\nof another tenant as missing, so getBillStructure and cycle errors never expose\nit on writes made without a tenant context.\n\nRefs #3455\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(manufacturing): refuse a negative or fractional assembly labour estimate\n\nRefs #3455\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(manufacturing): leave other tenants'' lines out of a bill''s structure\n\ngetBillStructure and the activation check now read only the bill tenant''s (and\nglobal) lines when a write or read has no tenant context.\n\nRefs #3455\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"73ba3c03793210559aa38e7140ba0700421aa6b0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/git/trees/73ba3c03793210559aa38e7140ba0700421aa6b0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/git/commits/fac4bd614f1566d2f3cf22d0cceb0df540d2ae7b","verification":{"payload":"tree 73ba3c03793210559aa38e7140ba0700421aa6b0\nparent 432b67110c8ea2276e99ea9e007229bf08b66a79\nauthor Will Griffin <willgriffin@gmail.com> 1791106327 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791106327 +0000\n\nfeat(manufacturing): add Assembly, the product that is made, with bill editor (#3482)\n\n* feat(products): add the assembly product type\n\nAssembly, the made counterpart to Material, is defined in smrt-manufacturing;\nthe discriminator value lives with the others so catalog code can filter by it.\n\nRefs #3455\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(manufacturing): add Assembly, the component resolver and cycle refusal\n\nAssembly extends smrt-products Product (STI, product type assembly) with\nestimatedLabourMinutes, defaultOperationId and partReference columns.\nAssemblyService resolves a component SKU to an assembly and its active bill,\na material, a bought item or missing, and BomLine and active\nBillOfMaterials saves refuse a loop with a BomCycleError naming the path.\n\nRefs #3455\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(manufacturing): add assembly list, form and bill editor components\n\nAssemblyList and AssemblyForm follow the consumer''s field policy (the form is\nsmrt-fields ObjectForm); BomEditor edits a bill''s lines and expands each\nsub-assembly to its own bill, read-only, through loadBill.\n\nRefs #3455\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(manufacturing): check a stored bill''s lines when an upsert activates it\n\nSaving a new active bill with an existing (productId, version, tenantId)\nupserts onto the stored bill, so the activation check now includes its lines.\n\nRefs #3455\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(manufacturing): share one database across AssemblyService collections\n\nA config object such as :memory: is now resolved once, so the SKU, product and\nbill collections read the same database.\n\nRefs #3455\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(manufacturing): reference an assembly''s default operation by foreign key\n\nOperation now lives in this package, so defaultOperationId is a nullable\n@foreignKey(''Operation'') rather than a plain string.\n\nRefs #3455\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(manufacturing): cover the assembly slots in the UI registration test\n\nThe svelte entry now registers the operation and assembly components together.\n\nRefs #3455\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(manufacturing): match the active tenant when an upsert activates a bill\n\nValidation runs before the tenancy interceptor stamps tenantId, so the stored\nbill a natural-key save will adopt is matched against the active tenant.\n\nRefs #3455\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(manufacturing): read a bill''s own tenant''s structure in the cycle walk\n\nA shared assembly''s active bill is chosen among the walking bill''s tenant''s\nbills, so writes made without a tenant context neither refuse a safe line nor\nmiss a loop because of another tenant''s higher version.\n\nRefs #3455\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(manufacturing): hide the assembly name in the list when the policy hides it\n\nRefs #3455\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(manufacturing): reference the default operation by class with RESTRICT\n\nFollows RoutingStep.operationId now that Operation is on main: operations are\nretired, never deleted.\n\nRefs #3455\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(manufacturing): report another tenant''s SKU as missing in a tenant walk\n\nWith an explicit tenantId, resolveComponent treats a SKU, product or bill line\nof another tenant as missing, so getBillStructure and cycle errors never expose\nit on writes made without a tenant context.\n\nRefs #3455\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(manufacturing): refuse a negative or fractional assembly labour estimate\n\nRefs #3455\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(manufacturing): leave other tenants'' lines out of a bill''s structure\n\ngetBillStructure and the activation check now read only the bill tenant''s (and\nglobal) lines when a write or read has no tenant context.\n\nRefs #3455\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwh30CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQqEQAG2dMR66XUp5pbL088PBWIYP\n+IFRb3YzMlPPVnv9Vfl4M+Cmz/ZDSEEr5ECi4OdqrWFPoPBiVQeMBnDOUjhZ1jqD\nh7RAtEZJFKwxXB9I8LPM6rFOTliL4bWhgOK2RAboePRFSsWCYjhJa8GXC1s9qpY7\n8/cDb0tsDH8CllyLL+o9PDoZ4/TDZOlgxYXyLzXdtJiBaBmKgGZc5UV1ZtXfOC4F\nsz+kjlbl6ywIFdOsmuJY7+kn/EAYt