}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/happyvertical/smrt/commit/e6f4ed5fbdd8c6eb806bac9965a4c2ab4acdd27b","node_id":"C_kwDOQDruXtoAKGU2ZjRlZDVmYmRkOGM2ZWI4MDZiYWM5OTY1YTRjMmFiNGFjZGQyN2I","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/happyvertical/smrt/commit/5ad6a17b1f8a6a9fcd15205b53c017d7e7d06053","sha":"5ad6a17b1f8a6a9fcd15205b53c017d7e7d06053","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/commits/5ad6a17b1f8a6a9fcd15205b53c017d7e7d06053"}],"sha":"e6f4ed5fbdd8c6eb806bac9965a4c2ab4acdd27b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/commits/e6f4ed5fbdd8c6eb806bac9965a4c2ab4acdd27b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/590602?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/willgriffin","id":590602,"login":"willgriffin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU5MDYwMg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/commits/5ad6a17b1f8a6a9fcd15205b53c017d7e7d06053/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T07:28:38Z","email":"willgriffin@gmail.com","name":"Will Griffin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T07:28:38Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: starter-gaps loose ends — runtime parity, dev-mcp db, smrt init, Biome (#3446) (#3477)\n\n* fix(config): share one runtime-block resolver between smrt app and app-runtime\n\n`smrt app` failed closed on a present-but-falsy `runtime` block (`null`,\n`false`, `0`, `''''`) while app-runtime''s SvelteKit entry used a truthiness\ncheck and silently selected the local profile for the same config.\n\nAdd `resolveEffectiveApplicationRuntime(config)` to smrt-config: when\nneither the loaded file nor a `setConfig()` override declares `runtime`,\nthe profile is `local`; otherwise it is `resolveConfiguredApplicationRuntime()`\nover the given file config, so a present non-block value throws one\n`RuntimeProfileValidationError`. The CLI''s `resolveConfiguredRuntime` and\napp-runtime''s `loadConfiguredRuntime` both call it.\n\nRefs #3446\n\n* fix(dev-mcp): resolve the dev database with the CLI''s DATABASE_URL fallback\n\n`smrt-dev-mcp` read `packages.cli.database` directly, so a project whose\ndatabase comes from `DATABASE_URL`/`DATABASE_TYPE` (the fallback the CLI\ngained in #3410) had no runtime diagnostics.\n\nMove the CLI''s precedence into smrt-config as `resolveCliDatabaseConfig()`\n(read-only; a configured `packages.cli.database.url` wins, else\n`DATABASE_URL` with the engine from the config type, `DATABASE_TYPE`, or the\nURL scheme; an unsupported `DATABASE_TYPE` refuses the fallback). The CLI''s\n`applyDatabaseEnvironment()` now applies its result, and dev-mcp calls it\nthrough the project''s own smrt-config after `dbUrl` and `SMRT_DEV_DB_URL`;\nan older project smrt-config without it keeps the config-only read.\n\nRefs #3446\n\n* fix(cli): smrt init writes the runtime smrt.ts; migrate in-repo apps off the legacy accessors\n\n`smrt init` still generated `src/lib/server/smrt.ts` exporting\n`getCollection`/`getSmrtConfig`, the shape #3416 deprecates for one release,\nso every CLI-created app hit the deprecation warning on its first generated\nroute. The generated module now exports only `runtime`\n(`classOptions()` + `getCollection()` over DATABASE_URL/DATABASE_TYPE,\n`satisfies GeneratedCollectionRuntime`), which generated routes resolve\nthrough without the legacy path, and points at `createSmrtSvelteKitRuntime()`\nfor the full application runtime.\n\nThe assets, images and content dev apps export the same `runtime` object\nover their existing per-class configuration; content''s hand-written routes,\nhooks, seeders and route-test mocks call `runtime.getCollection()` /\n`runtime.classOptions()`.\n\nRefs #3446\n\n* fix(hooks): run the pre-commit and pre-push Biome at CI''s pinned version\n\nThe `format` (pre-commit) and `format-check` (pre-push) hooks ran a bare\n`npx biome`, which resolves the root devDependency (2.5.3), while\n`pnpm lint`, `pnpm format` and CI''s test-suite pin `@biomejs/biome@2.5.2`\n(#2710). The two disagree on at least one construct (seen in #3413), so a\ncommit could pass locally and fail CI or the reverse. Pin both hooks to the\nsame `npx --yes @biomejs/biome@2.5.2` the lint script and CI run.\n\nRefs #3446\n\n* fix(config): reject a non-block runtime override in setConfig\n\n`setConfig({ runtime: null })` was accepted and `deepMerge` dropped the\nnull, so no override was recorded and `resolveEffectiveApplicationRuntime()`\nselected the local profile — the fail-open the resolver exists to prevent.\nA declared runtime override that is not an object (`null`, `false`, `0`,\n`''''`, an array) now throws the same `RuntimeProfileValidationError`\n(`invalid_config` at `runtime`) before anything is stored.\n\nRefs #3446\n\n* fix(dev-mcp): let an explicit dbType override the DATABASE_URL engine\n\nThe DATABASE_URL path carried the CLI-resolved engine as the connection''s\ntype, and the resolver prefers that over `inferDatabaseType(url, dbType)`,\nso `DATABASE_URL=postgres://…` with `dbType: ''sqlite''` still opened\nPostgreSQL although the tool schema promises `dbType` overrides an\nenvironment connection. For the `environment` source an explicit `dbType`\nnow wins and the resolved type (DATABASE_TYPE or the URL scheme) is the\nfallback; a configured `cli.database.type` still wins over `dbType`.\n\nRefs #3446","tree":{"sha":"b7d34041071da3d31ae986022a03c0df425bff4a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/git/trees/b7d34041071da3d31ae986022a03c0df425bff4a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/git/commits/5ad6a17b1f8a6a9fcd15205b53c017d7e7d06053","verification":{"payload":"tree b7d34041071da3d31ae986022a03c0df425bff4a\nparent 1f383ab7cf7027cc717f5dbcfc953144bbc4eaea\nauthor Will Griffin <willgriffin@gmail.com> 1791098918 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791098918 +0000\n\nfix: starter-gaps loose ends — runtime parity, dev-mcp db, smrt init, Biome (#3446) (#3477)\n\n* fix(config): share one runtime-block resolver between smrt app and app-runtime\n\n`smrt app` failed closed on a present-but-falsy `runtime` block (`null`,\n`false`, `0`, `''''`) while app-runtime''s SvelteKit entry used a truthiness\ncheck and silently selected the local profile for the same config.\n\nAdd `resolveEffectiveApplicationRuntime(config)` to smrt-config: when\nneither the loaded file nor a `setConfig()` override declares `runtime`,\nthe profile is `local`; otherwise it is `resolveConfiguredApplicationRuntime()`\nover the given file config, so a present non-block value throws one\n`RuntimeProfileValidationError`. The CLI''s `resolveConfiguredRuntime` and\napp-runtime''s `loadConfiguredRuntime` both call it.\n\nRefs #3446\n\n* fix(dev-mcp): resolve the dev database with the CLI''s DATABASE_URL fallback\n\n`smrt-dev-mcp` read `packages.cli.database` directly, so a project whose\ndatabase comes from `DATABASE_URL`/`DATABASE_TYPE` (the fallback the CLI\ngained in #3410) had no runtime diagnostics.\n\nMove the CLI''s precedence into smrt-config as `resolveCliDatabaseConfig()`\n(read-only; a configured `packages.cli.database.url` wins, else\n`DATABASE_URL` with the engine from the config type, `DATABASE_TYPE`, or the\nURL scheme; an unsupported `DATABASE_TYPE` refuses the fallback). The CLI''s\n`applyDatabaseEnvironment()` now applies its result, and dev-mcp calls it\nthrough the project''s own smrt-config after `dbUrl` and `SMRT_DEV_DB_URL`;\nan older project smrt-config without it keeps the config-only read.\n\nRefs #3446\n\n* fix(cli): smrt init writes the runtime smrt.ts; migrate in-repo apps off the legacy accessors\n\n`smrt init` still generated `src/lib/server/smrt.ts` exporting\n`getCollection`/`getSmrtConfig`, the shape #3416 deprecates for one release,\nso every CLI-created app hit the deprecation warning on its first generated\nroute. The generated module now exports only `runtime`\n(`classOptions()` + `getCollection()` over DATABASE_URL/DATABASE_TYPE,\n`satisfies GeneratedCollectionRuntime`), which generated routes resolve\nthrough without the legacy path, and points at `createSmrtSvelteKitRuntime()`\nfor the full application runtime.\n\nThe assets, images and content dev apps export the same `runtime` object\nover their existing per-class configuration; content''s hand-written routes,\nhooks, seeders and route-test mocks call `runtime.getCollection()` /\n`runtime.classOptions()`.\n\nRefs #3446\n\n* fix(hooks): run the pre-commit and pre-push Biome at CI''s pinned version\n\nThe `format` (pre-commit) and `format-check` (pre-push) hooks ran a bare\n`npx biome`, which resolves the root devDependency (2.5.3), while\n`pnpm lint`, `pnpm format` and CI''s test-suite pin `@biomejs/biome@2.5.2`\n(#2710). The two disagree on at least one construct (seen in #3413), so a\ncommit could pass locally and fail CI or the reverse. Pin both hooks to the\nsame `npx --yes @biomejs/biome@2.5.2` the lint script and CI run.\n\nRefs #3446\n\n* fix(config): reject a non-block runtime override in setConfig\n\n`setConfig({ runtime: null })` was accepted and `deepMerge` dropped the\nnull, so no override was recorded and `resolveEffectiveApplicationRuntime()`\nselected the local profile — the fail-open the resolver exists to prevent.\nA declared runtime override that is not an object (`null`, `false`, `0`,\n`''''`, an array) now throws the same `RuntimeProfileValidationError`\n(`invalid_config` at `runtime`) before anything is stored.\n\nRefs #3446\n\n* fix(dev-mcp): let an explicit dbType override the DATABASE_URL engine\n\nThe DATABASE_URL path carried the CLI-resolved engine as the connection''s\ntype, and the resolver prefers that over `inferDatabaseType(url, dbType)`,\nso `DATABASE_URL=postgres://…` with `dbType: ''sqlite''` still opened\nPostgreSQL although the tool schema promises `dbType` overrides an\nenvironment connection. For the `environment` source an explicit `dbType`\nnow wins and the resolved type (DATABASE_TYPE or the URL scheme) is the\nfallback; a configured `cli.database.type` still wins over `dbType`.\n\nRefs #3446","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwgMzCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAACUoQAFwTV9kA9lIWSvBvKYjg2Q3M\nKMPbnYVUpWQZ8IX0YTycLx6dUiwjL/32vS2WSZE87OoL0BCEsox0D9gHXEYLYNGx\nzoqtxlgG2yDiGZNSNM6mru44VZJC/6V9Zf9KSfUjTmg6AJ1qVHuQJ6a9p3zziIVS\nX1N5ZfjOOG+TMVvLGTwgtYYW6hV8DLrViun6YmpYqNLFNO9Ustr/FBfByeCML9Mx\nceAStK6j+VmowjbDTR2P6Ge1zp95RoOMxtOepWJJ/KDwaLhK8RzHDG/r8LzcvPuL\naRPNYzpM4ywppWgaJg9dTURofDzV+HeBkBrlkFj9q1UZqAVba96yqOjBFWpCMZQN\n2Blokw+l2BO7CB7Hd2PnDAumbkSrtXn6RgDNeo9vacFZO4yB4jJDhwIZDNWlVrgH\n3Q+mxnQqbEcEt/6y32q16mpOF6krIHxP8LjdjHAM77uBf0jHd3QEnO8V3EZHIn9d\nUe6lJ/cn+H812M8NawUPcUgFYW1vykTu+iAnnX2/gS4g+v4Dxky5dvo+wXiUeHNo\nZ5RtiiMkzTgNkNLDBt12EjXHjBUnBRXK0hS0A/ECRAsRZQa1ZahnLougGkgDXaNv\nDA22oummL/jvOsbk0ZSH+YfBJhFjHZw7Ktha+3gCH+l3EE9ltbmINg4YhsNY0uy8\nOLN63O1KxdZeE8NA6ELk\n=g+fv\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-04T07:41:39Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/happyvertical/smrt/commit/5ad6a17b1f8a6a9fcd15205b53c017d7e7d06053","node_id":"C_kwDOQDruXtoAKDVhZDZhMTdiMWY4YTZhOWZjZDE1MjA1YjUzYzAxN2Q3ZTdkMDYwNTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/happyvertical/smrt/commit/1f383ab7cf7027cc717f5dbcfc953144bbc4eaea","sha":"1f383ab7cf7027cc717f5dbcfc953144bbc4eaea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/commits/1f383ab7cf7027cc717f5dbcfc953144bbc4eaea"}],"sha":"5ad6a17b1f8a6a9fcd15205b53c017d7e7d06053","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/commits/5ad6a17b1f8a6a9fcd15205b53c017d7e7d06053"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/590602?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/willgriffin","id":590602,"login":"willgriffin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU5MDYwMg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/commits/1f383ab7cf7027cc717f5dbcfc953144bbc4eaea/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T07:28:06Z","email":"willgriffin@gmail.com","name":"Will Griffin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T07:28:06Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(users): login rate limiter and per-person PIN on an enrolled device (#3273, #3276) (#3471)\n\n* feat(users): shared login rate limiter, session provenance, and device PIN sign-in\n\nAdds LoginAttemptLimiter (#3273): a cross-replica sign-in budget stored in\nusers_login_attempts, keyed by hashed subject and source, with exponential\nlockout and a LoginAuditSink seam whose default persists UsersLoginAuditEvent\nrows. TerminalAuthService.approveRequest now draws from it; the old\nUsersCliAuthApproveLimit classes stay exported but deprecated.\n\nSession gains authMethod and parentSessionId. loadSessionContext enforces\nparent liveness and exposes authMethod/parent (the bridge for #2944);\nswitchTenant keeps layered sessions inside the parent''s tenant; destroySession\nrevokes children. OIDC, terminal, and mobile mints set authMethod.\n\nAdds DeviceCredentialService (#3276): per-person sign-in layered on an\nenrolled device''s bearer session, with a DeviceCredentialVerifier seam and a\nscrypt PinVerifier, PIN set/reset/clear with per-person and per-device lockout\nthrough the limiter, and SvelteKit handlers.\n\nRefs #3273, #3276, #2944\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Eo95PyxMmTReUCt5sJLQzu\n\n* fix(users): repair logger call and session fixtures for the provenance columns\n\nThe limiter/PIN patch was written without a runnable toolchain. Its first\nreal build and test run found a createLogger() call with the wrong argument\nshape, a value import used only as a type, and two hand-written sessions\nDDL fixtures (OIDC SQLite helper, DuckDB UUID case) missing the new\nauth_method and parent_session_id columns.\n\nRefs #3273 #3276\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(users): person authority, device ceiling, and hand-over for device PIN sessions\n\nReconciles DeviceCredentialService with the 2026-10-03 amendment on #3276.\n\n- Device ceiling: optional deviceCeiling(device) hook, snapshotted into the\n  person session as data.permissionCeiling and intersected with the person''s\n  resolved permissions in loadSessionContext. A ceilinged session never gets\n  superAdminBypass or systemContext from withSessionPermissionContext.\n- Switching people: singleOccupant (default true) ends the device session''s\n  other children after a successful sign-in.\n- personSessionTtlSeconds/personSessionAutoExtend are replaced by\n  personIdleSeconds (sliding, stored on the session so it applies whichever\n  SessionService resolves the bearer) and optional personMaxSeconds (absolute\n  cap in data.absoluteExpiresAt, enforced by Session.isValid/extend).\n- Tests for person-vs-device authority, ceiling, occupancy, idle and absolute\n  expiry on SQLite, plus a PostgreSQL case covering the lockout-enabled\n  limiter path and the session data controls.\n\nRefs #3273 #3276\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(users): address review findings on the limiter and device PIN\n\n- Treat a malformed sign-in user id as an unknown user before it reaches a\n  native UUID predicate, keeping the non-enumerating failure and equal work.\n- Enforce mustReset server-side: a temporary-PIN session carries an empty\n  ceiling and setPin ends it.\n- Refuse a layered session whose tenant differs from its parent''s.\n- Fail a mixed-type stored permission ceiling closed.\n- Record a per-row retain_until from the limiter''s own configuration and\n  sweep by it, so retention cannot erase a custom-configured budget early.\n- Keep the raw subject id out of self-service PIN audit metadata.\n- Store parentSessionId as a native UUID column (still not a foreign key).\n- Cover the two retention tasks and the SvelteKit device handlers.\n\nRefs #3273 #3276\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(users): address deep-review findings on device PIN sessions\n\n- Mark Session.parentSessionId sensitive: it is the device''s bearer and must\n  not appear in a person session''s public serialization.\n- Limit PIN administration to active members of the administrator''s tenant.\n- Enforce a session''s permission ceiling in checkOperationPermission, and\n  ignore ambient bypass inside a ceilinged session.\n- Re-check the verified credential generation after the mint so a reset or\n  clear that completes mid sign-in cannot leave a session behind.\n- Read revocation targets with raw id queries so caller list bounds cannot\n  truncate a reset/clear sweep or a single-occupant hand-over.\n- loadPersonSession re-checks device enrollment before accepting or extending\n  the person session, and revokes it when the device is no longer enrolled.\n\nRefs #3273 #3276\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(users): address review-cycle round 1 findings\n\n- Lock a limiter key when a failure completes another maxAttempts\n  consecutive failures, not only when it exhausts a window, so pacing one\n  attempt under the budget no longer avoids the exponential lockout.\n- Apply a session''s permission ceiling in operation guards whatever tenant\n  the guarded resource is in.\n- Limit PIN administration to people whose every active membership is in the\n  administrator''s tenant: the PIN is one per person across tenants.\n- End sessions minted under the old PIN on every PIN change.\n- loadPersonSession revokes only on an explicit un-enrolment; a throwing\n  enrollment hook refuses the request without revoking.\n- Terminal approval is keyed on the approving user only again, in its own\n  limiter key namespace.\n- Count a post-mint credential-generation mismatch as a failed attempt, and\n  never return a session a concurrent hand-over already ended.\n\nRefs #3273 #3276\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(users): address review-cycle round 2 findings\n\n- A successful sign-in resets only the subject''s streak; a shared source\n  keeps its backoff and sheds it by time since its last failure\n  (last_failed_at), so one valid credential cannot clear it.\n- Tie the lock write to the streak it was computed from.\n- Terminal approval uses a prefixed subject so it never pools with the same\n  person''s PIN budget, whichever limiter instance is in use.\n- Read the target''s memberships for PIN administration outside any ambient\n  tenant filter.\n- Mint sessions in one write with the capped expiry.\n- Warn when no PIN pepper is configured; document that users.pin.manage is\n  impersonation-equivalent on enrolled devices.\n\nRefs #3273 #3276\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(users): address review-cycle round 3 nits\n\n- An idempotent terminal re-approval releases its reservation instead of\n  settling as a success, so it cannot clear the approver''s streak.\n- Drop unused limiter-default imports from retention.\n- Correct the last_failed_at comment: streak forgiveness is all-or-nothing.\n\nRefs #3273 #3276\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(users): decay a shared source''s failure streak gradually\n\nA source key (a tablet, an office address) is not reset by anyone''s\nsuccessful sign-in, so its streak previously cleared only after a full\nstreakResetSeconds with no failure at all — on a busy shared device,\nordinary typos escalated to the maximum lockout for everyone. A source now\nsheds one failure per sourceStreakDecaySeconds (default: twice the window)\nsince its last failure: spaced-out mistakes never accumulate, while a burst\nleaves no time to decay and still escalates. Subject keys are unchanged.\n\nRefs #3273 #3276\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(users): guard the source-streak decay on the last-failure time\n\nThe decay''s compare-and-set matched on the streak alone, but forgiving one\nfailure and adding one writes the same number back, so concurrent failures\non a shared source could each apply the same forgiveness and collapse into\none. The guard now also matches the last-failure time the forgiveness was\ncomputed from; when nothing is forgiven the write is the plain atomic\nincrement. Covered on SQLite and PostgreSQL.\n\nRefs #3273 #3276\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(users): lock a decayed source only when its streak crosses a boundary\n\nForgiving one failure and adding one leaves a decayed streak on the number\nit held, so a source resting on a multiple of maxAttempts re-locked on every\nspaced-out mistake. The boundary now triggers a lock only when the failure\nmoved the streak up onto it. Also mark 400/403 PIN handler responses\nno-store and note the overlapping-sign-in case in the README.\n\nRefs #3273 #3276\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(users): do not let device sign-out rewrite another session''s expiry\n\nsignOut resolved whatever bearer it was given through the auto-extending\nperson-TTL session service before checking it was a person session, so a\ndevice or browser session presented to it had its expiry rewritten to the\nperson idle timeout. It now decides without recording activity. Also mark\nthe remaining 401/500 PIN handler responses no-store.\n\nRefs #3273 #3276\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(users): never rotate a layered session; tighten person-session resolution\n\n- switchTenant no longer rotates a layered session: its only permitted\n  target is its parent''s tenant, and a replacement session would escape the\n  revocation sweeps (PIN reset/clear, hand-over) that read ids once.\n- Layers do not nest: a session whose parent is itself layered never loads.\n- loadPersonSession revokes only when the host hook reports un-enrolment,\n  not when the parent is simply not this service''s kind of device session.\n- PIN management resolves a person bearer through the enrolled-device gate.\n\nRefs #3273 #3276\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8cc0cd9c684d4ca2fc87b309bdd9cb4402946942","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/git/trees/8cc0cd9c684d4ca2fc87b309bdd9cb4402946942"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/git/commits/1f383ab7cf7027cc717f5dbcfc953144bbc4eaea","verification":{"payload":"tree 8cc0cd9c684d4ca2fc87b309bdd9cb4402946942\nparent 58684736c1e7e787c40427c5731c03b803b9f798\nauthor Will Griffin <willgriffin@gmail.com> 1791098886 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791098886 +0000\n\nfeat(users): login rate limiter and per-person PIN on an enrolled device (#3273, #3276) (#3471)\n\n* feat(users): shared login rate limiter, session provenance, and device PIN sign-in\n\nAdds Lo