,"gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/happyvertical/smrt/commit/58684736c1e7e787c40427c5731c03b803b9f798","node_id":"C_kwDOQDruXtoAKDU4Njg0NzM2YzFlN2U3ODdjNDA0MjdjNTczMWMwM2I4MDNiOWY3OTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/happyvertical/smrt/commit/5efbc7a59d3a87627726fa8e859848d3e07cb35f","sha":"5efbc7a59d3a87627726fa8e859848d3e07cb35f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/commits/5efbc7a59d3a87627726fa8e859848d3e07cb35f"}],"sha":"58684736c1e7e787c40427c5731c03b803b9f798","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/commits/58684736c1e7e787c40427c5731c03b803b9f798"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/590602?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/willgriffin","id":590602,"login":"willgriffin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU5MDYwMg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/commits/5efbc7a59d3a87627726fa8e859848d3e07cb35f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T06:52:03Z","email":"willgriffin@gmail.com","name":"Will Griffin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T06:52:03Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(human-resources): add employment and qualification records (#3470)\n\n* feat(human-resources): add employment and qualification records\n\nNew package @happyvertical/smrt-human-resources: who works for an\norganization, as what, and with what standing.\n\n- Employment: one record per tenant and profile, employee number unique\n  per tenant, dated terms (rehire adds a term to the same record), and an\n  append-only change history. EmploymentService: hire, end, rehire,\n  position and worker-type changes, leave, login link, employed-on-date\n  and active-employee checks answered from the terms\n- Qualifications: per-tenant definitions and held qualifications with\n  issue and expiry dates, person or employment scope, renewal chains.\n  QualificationService: grant, renew, suspend, reinstate, revoke, verify,\n  a check that returns the failure reason, holders, expiring-within and\n  an expiry sweep\n- Every model and collection is tenant-required, sensitive, and closed on\n  REST, MCP and CLI; writes go only through the services\n- Lifecycle events through an onEvent hook, delivered after commit\n- Svelte components: employee list, employee form, a person''s\n  qualifications, expiring-soon list\n- Tests on in-memory SQLite, component tests under jsdom, and optional\n  PostgreSQL suites\n\nCloses #3435\n\n* fix(human-resources): decide qualification and login standing by date\n\nRefs #3435\n\n* fix(human-resources): validate qualification changes by dated standing\n\nRefs #3435\n\n* test(human-resources): always cover the nested-transaction refusal\n\nThe native-adapter test skips when its optional module is missing; a stub\nhandle now covers the same branch unconditionally. AGENTS.md states that the\nexpiry sweep selects by stored status.\n\nRefs #3435\n\n* fix(human-resources): sweep lapses by date and renew up to a later grant\n\nsweepExpired records a lapse for every row that ran out in force, including\nwhile suspended or while a revocation is recorded for a later day. renew is\nno longer refused by another grant that starts on or after the renewal''s\ncutoff, so the outcome does not depend on recording order.\n\nRefs #3435\n\n* fix(human-resources): bound the expiry sweep and correct stale docs\n\nsweepExpired takes an optional since date so a scheduled run does not\nre-read every lapsed row. Doc comments now describe the renewal overlap rule\nand where the stored expired status is written.\n\nRefs #3435\n\n* fix(human-resources): refuse a renewal that ends before what it renews\n\nThe renewed row keeps answering for its own period, so a shorter renewal\nlapsed (and the sweep announced it) while check still passed. The error says\nhow to replace a qualification with a shorter one: revoke it and grant anew.\n\nRefs #3435","tree":{"sha":"d3407082b339605975862ab37189b82db7a5a875","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/git/trees/d3407082b339605975862ab37189b82db7a5a875"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/git/commits/5efbc7a59d3a87627726fa8e859848d3e07cb35f","verification":{"payload":"tree d3407082b339605975862ab37189b82db7a5a875\nparent 6c475cbb5c67f6619fef20645a64bce664076c16\nauthor Will Griffin <willgriffin@gmail.com> 1791096723 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791096723 +0000\n\nfeat(human-resources): add employment and qualification records (#3470)\n\n* feat(human-resources): add employment and qualification records\n\nNew package @happyvertical/smrt-human-resources: who works for an\norganization, as what, and with what standing.\n\n- Employment: one record per tenant and profile, employee number unique\n  per tenant, dated terms (rehire adds a term to the same record), and an\n  append-only change history. EmploymentService: hire, end, rehire,\n  position and worker-type changes, leave, login link, employed-on-date\n  and active-employee checks answered from the terms\n- Qualifications: per-tenant definitions and held qualifications with\n  issue and expiry dates, person or employment scope, renewal chains.\n  QualificationService: grant, renew, suspend, reinstate, revoke, verify,\n  a check that returns the failure reason, holders, expiring-within and\n  an expiry sweep\n- Every model and collection is tenant-required, sensitive, and closed on\n  REST, MCP and CLI; writes go only through the services\n- Lifecycle events through an onEvent hook, delivered after commit\n- Svelte components: employee list, employee form, a person''s\n  qualifications, expiring-soon list\n- Tests on in-memory SQLite, component tests under jsdom, and optional\n  PostgreSQL suites\n\nCloses #3435\n\n* fix(human-resources): decide qualification and login standing by date\n\nRefs #3435\n\n* fix(human-resources): validate qualification changes by dated standing\n\nRefs #3435\n\n* test(human-resources): always cover the nested-transaction refusal\n\nThe native-adapter test skips when its optional module is missing; a stub\nhandle now covers the same branch unconditionally. AGENTS.md states that the\nexpiry sweep selects by stored status.\n\nRefs #3435\n\n* fix(human-resources): sweep lapses by date and renew up to a later grant\n\nsweepExpired records a lapse for every row that ran out in force, including\nwhile suspended or while a revocation is recorded for a later day. renew is\nno longer refused by another grant that starts on or after the renewal''s\ncutoff, so the outcome does not depend on recording order.\n\nRefs #3435\n\n* fix(human-resources): bound the expiry sweep and correct stale docs\n\nsweepExpired takes an optional since date so a scheduled run does not\nre-read every lapsed row. Doc comments now describe the renewal overlap rule\nand where the stored expired status is written.\n\nRefs #3435\n\n* fix(human-resources): refuse a renewal that ends before what it renews\n\nThe renewed row keeps answering for its own period, so a shorter renewal\nlapsed (and the sweep announced it) while check still passed. The error says\nhow to replace a qualification with a shorter one: revoke it and grant anew.\n\nRefs #3435","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwfeiCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA1u8QAEwspM6qAfQaLPPRduDHm7r+\nxpisl+dLvLD+cowT82jOrvHIFgN0P7cFwy3sUiU5Gn2OGZciOT7v7zX6vy28icCx\nmh1oUDCFuiG6ueq/tHat3ZzZSSJtehvYQcGMFciKbONsxLgfIniBNdgM5eHCtyLW\nXVu150uB2FTbBcj9TffuXrICzx4bFN/1nrG1XhzZ/fb4yxVkdwL1lEgeF/AvsyZ4\nMTtkYOUbX1HsmMJSM7tFd2SMu3SX5qKaeekpsTT3WdLLM4hrqB8nD2xU0AMaz8ce\nPCDkkry6WZ2xCzpu/YWp33VbQI1xF2kz6WYVlP2BVWKlz4ef1AcoVn9XjDSXwCB+\nDoJ+jvm0iC6+U988ZifnSJDst1XvzkqyuKnz/NOgK7QAUTTjkMbdeTbyZmmmsO8F\n8MBaexoB8SiarJ/jsukPUmWYoplvSEXGxTJ9SnbDQsoosUrMyWGI3aAlKwhAd4nI\n6nqfjWNXooqUek9OBaXgva4Ay8K7LRytnQsRYU04cXA1spS+XD2AOsUngR+y+L8x\n+y36vYeE/6GiLyMR2DziLLanXjHUtffoS22aHzeGCSP27DwNvWWiqxOEY6C6iF/4\nG/WOf4+6P2rJRU+3KdgOMU42R7Hx4jTTtGgDy1a5isOQ/KfksczcGfap+32oHR1x\niqLc6plai3VOpBB9nx0/\n=Tfvy\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-04T06:52:19Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/happyvertical/smrt/commit/5efbc7a59d3a87627726fa8e859848d3e07cb35f","node_id":"C_kwDOQDruXtoAKDVlZmJjN2E1OWQzYTg3NjI3NzI2ZmE4ZTg1OTg0OGQzZTA3Y2IzNWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/happyvertical/smrt/commit/6c475cbb5c67f6619fef20645a64bce664076c16","sha":"6c475cbb5c67f6619fef20645a64bce664076c16","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/commits/6c475cbb5c67f6619fef20645a64bce664076c16"}],"sha":"5efbc7a59d3a87627726fa8e859848d3e07cb35f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/commits/5efbc7a59d3a87627726fa8e859848d3e07cb35f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/590602?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/willgriffin","id":590602,"login":"willgriffin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU5MDYwMg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/commits/6c475cbb5c67f6619fef20645a64bce664076c16/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T03:57:58Z","email":"willgriffin@gmail.com","name":"Will Griffin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T03:57:58Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(events): synchronize iCalendar sources by UID (#3465)\n\n* feat(events): sync iCalendar sources by UID\n\n* fix(events): scope calendar source identities\n\n* test(events): cover calendar sync boundaries\n\n* fix(events): isolate calendar series by tenant\n\n* feat(events): complete bounded calendar synchronization contract\n\nRefs #3402\n\n* fix(events): preserve authoritative calendar recurrence across windows\n\nAddress accepted recurrence selection, cross-zone RDATE and stale master findings.\n\nRefs #3402\n\n* fix(events): require bounds for retained recurring masters\n\nReject stale minimal notices without expansion after authoritative master selection.\n\nRefs #3402","tree":{"sha":"ae4b480a1a17ad3afb39af91f0113ead634a3ba6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/git/trees/ae4b480a1a17ad3afb39af91f0113ead634a3ba6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/git/commits/6c475cbb5c67f6619fef20645a64bce664076c16","verification":{"payload":"tree ae4b480a1a17ad3afb39af91f0113ead634a3ba6\nparent 5db5509e0c36a99f1c432f05ec48f1bf7a509cd0\nauthor Will Griffin <willgriffin@gmail.com> 1791086278 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791086278 +0000\n\nfeat(events): synchronize iCalendar sources by UID (#3465)\n\n* feat(events): sync iCalendar sources by UID\n\n* fix(events): scope calendar source identities\n\n* test(events): cover calendar sync boundaries\n\n* fix(events): isolate calendar series by tenant\n\n* feat(events): complete bounded calendar synchronization contract\n\nRefs #3402\n\n* fix(events): preserve authoritative calendar recurrence across windows\n\nAddress accepted recurrence selection, cross-zone RDATE and stale master findings.\n\nRefs #3402\n\n* fix(events): require bounds for retained recurring masters\n\nReject stale minimal notices without expansion after authoritative master selection.\n\nRefs #3402","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwdEGCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAtmoQADBvpT9gM/vplSRwaGbN1kZc\nyOOlz28XRGaWoRu/UkSnTuOCDiEZ/C0/SYJIZzT6pZcXte/tP3AGhE0vAmOnXJoR\nN4uGR/nlVdZJ4YsiG04pvodQV4EX5sDEW4b4pt0NMjsTqoDUUJCncnt81iCwO3nk\nf25nZNfPm4272JHQP2Vfy3S05N3gRUeYBPPleYTQJGrzWfqy7fLM70+giXzIX/2I\nVlOh2Ao4CJayR0tk5g3kw/GFryFVw/1BVIEpzKbLYTGlyyXCrPEcs+71bnB7PofR\nKbe2pD4Q93UH5xTFyd1OkbH3eeDItcvvuVFFGDo3BleVxvhAsQTjAzPrnIja/gcF\nh0+WIQI7AluyUL5HpGs95Hwdt25U0T9P8bL3JWs9NiPaE65XEglY0QmsIbOUv3UP\nSqSSU9f3pbs5/rLe3cwWE/fmsdL16U6wEzdodAn4+Mvq4PjKsrYQuyvMcCmMddt3\nSE0LhfPUvFby8uAd8LWlTxb9r08sP2Zf+QTsFZIyXb6CyDYJJEO0l93yXkzS8Syo\nLEeixwK8pHaZhtb5lMqh5IyUfFkJc0HjfZtB4ln6btnTCxO3Jsqz+N6apU9OkceJ\nXXc0EyRVZPlVklG9E8++0B5OmBpCKeEqSBfWtut07RMtgMC6OV2Wc/Zd6QcDLlXw\nRqdVdbf/dVWgM0Zfn2v2\n=PaQ5\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-04T04:07:35Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/happyvertical/smrt/commit/6c475cbb5c67f6619fef20645a64bce664076c16","node_id":"C_kwDOQDruXtoAKDZjNDc1Y2JiNWM2N2Y2NjE5ZmVmMjA2NDVhNjRiY2U2NjQwNzZjMTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/happyvertical/smrt/commit/5db5509e0c36a99f1c432f05ec48f1bf7a509cd0","sha":"5db5509e0c36a99f1c432f05ec48f1bf7a509cd0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/commits/5db5509e0c36a99f1c432f05ec48f1bf7a509cd0"}],"sha":"6c475cbb5c67f6619fef20645a64bce664076c16","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/commits/6c475cbb5c67f6619fef20645a64bce664076c16"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/590602?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/willgriffin","id":590602,"login":"willgriffin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU5MDYwMg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/commits/5db5509e0c36a99f1c432f05ec48f1bf7a509cd0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T03:39:49Z","email":"willgriffin@gmail.com","name":"Will Griffin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T03:39:49Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: starter gaps — local MCP tokens, runtime collections, assistant defaults (#3367) (#3472)\n\n* fix(web): accept the generated { items } list envelope in unwrapListResult\n\nRefs #3412\n\n* feat(svelte): AppShell passes the Provider''s DataSurfaceRegistry to the dock snippet\n\nFix the ShellDockTool icon docs example (icon takes a component).\n\nRefs #3415\n\n* feat(chat): default mountAssistantRoutes tools, db and ai\n\nmountAssistantRoutes now needs no glue for the common case:\n\n- Without `tools`, the route offers the manifest operations `allowedTools`\n  names (buildManifestToolCatalog), minus names an `extraTools` entry\n  serves. Fail-closed is unchanged: absent or empty offers nothing. A name\n  nothing provides is an error: at mount when its collection is already\n  registered, otherwise the turn answers 503 before anything is stored\n  (skipped when `actions` is set, since action tools are allow-listed too).\n  An explicit `tools` value (even []) keeps the old behaviour.\n- `db` also accepts a per-request resolver, called once per request, so a\n  `database-rls` app passes `() => runtime.databaseConfig()`. The fixed\n  form still works.\n- `ai` is optional: omitted, each turn builds the client from the\n  smrt.config `ai` block through resolveConfiguredAIProvider and\n  toAIClientOptions (loading the config file if no one has). Nothing\n  configured answers 503 and sends AIProviderNotConfiguredError, which names\n  variables and never values, to onError only. An explicitly empty `ai` is\n  still a mount error.\n\nRefs #3414\n\n* fix(chat): honour PLAYWRIGHT_CHROMIUM_EXECUTABLE_PATH in e2e config\n\nThe chat e2e config ignored the override the sibling package configs\nhonour, so test:e2e could not run where the downloaded Chromium cannot\nload (missing libgbm).\n\nRefs #3414\n\n* fix(core): fail at scan time when an app package name is unscoped\n\nAn unscoped package.json name made generation emit pkg:Class keys that\nisQualifiedName (and the isolated-manifest validator) reject, surfacing\nas CONFIG_INVALID_ISOLATED_MANIFEST at build. The @scope/ requirement is\na deliberate contract (#713), so manifest generation now throws\nCONFIG_UNSCOPED_PACKAGE_NAME with a rename hint when a package declares\nclasses. Test fixtures now use scoped names.\n\nRefs #3408\n\n* fix(app-runtime): remove onboarding hand-off files after a committed owner claim\n\ncreateOwnerSetupPage now deletes onboarding.json and onboarding-launch.html\nfrom the private state root once claimOwner resolves, so pnpm app:open stops\noffering the spent invitation. Failed claims leave them untouched;\nonOwnerClaimed still runs for extra cleanup and removeOnboardingHandoff:false\nopts out. Adds runtime.applicationStateRoot() and ONBOARDING_HANDOFF_FILES.\nThe template drops its copied onOwnerClaimed glue.\n\nRefs #3411\n\n* feat(cli): print the one-time setup URL to the operator terminal\n\nsmrt app setup and recover print the loopback /setup?token= URL through an\noptional io.operatorTerminal sink that exists only when stdout and stderr are\nTTYs; the URL never reaches stdout/stderr logs or pipes.\n\nRefs #3411\n\n* fix(app-runtime): clean up onboarding hand-off before setting the session cookie\n\nA throwing cookies.set() after the claim committed skipped the removal and left\nthe spent invitation. Removal now runs right after claimOwner resolves. Updates\nthe AGENTS.md note that still called cleanup an injected hook.\n\nRefs #3411\n\n* fix(cli): default smrt app to the local profile without a runtime block\n\nItem 1 of the #3410 patch train. smrt app setup failed \"profile must be\nlocal, self-hosted, or cloud\" for a smrt.config with no runtime block,\nwhile app-runtime''s SvelteKit entry resolves that config as local. The\nCLI resolver now applies the same rule; a present but invalid block still\nfails closed.\n\nRefs #3410\n\n* fix(cli): honour DATABASE_URL/DATABASE_TYPE as the db command fallback\n\nItem 2 of the #3410 patch train. smrt app setup and smrt app migrate\nexport DATABASE_URL/DATABASE_TYPE for the child smrt db:migrate, but every\ndb command read only packages.cli.database and failed \"Database\nconfiguration required\", so an application had to forward the variables\nin its own config.\n\nmain() now applies the environment once, after loadConfig, with an\nexplicit precedence: a config-declared packages.cli.database.url wins (a\nstray shell URL never retargets a configured project), then DATABASE_URL\nwith the engine from config type, DATABASE_TYPE, or the URL scheme, then\nthe :memory: default the schema commands refuse. URL and engine travel as\na pair; an unsupported DATABASE_TYPE disables the fallback with a warning\nthat never echoes the URL.\n\nThe template''s smrt.config.ts drops its packages.cli.database forwarding.\n\nRefs #3410\n\n* fix(cli): load .env beside a TypeScript smrt.config\n\nDrive-by on the #3410 patch train (item 2''s path). main() looks for .env\nnext to smrt.config.{js,mjs,cjs,json} only, while the config loader also\nfinds smrt.config.{ts,mts,cts} (the template default), so a direct smrt\ndb:migrate in such an app never saw DATABASE_URL from .env. The shell\nstill wins over the file.\n\nRefs #3410\n\n* fix(cli): bind smrt app dev to the loopback host the URLs name\n\nItem 3 of the #3410 patch train. smrt app dev ran vite dev with the\ncaller''s arguments only, so Vite bound its default host localhost, which\nNode resolves to [::1] first, while onboarding and app:open hand out\nhttp://127.0.0.1:<PORT>/ - connection refused until the user edited the\nURL. smrt app dev now adds --host 127.0.0.1 unless --host is given, and\n--port $PORT when PORT is set and --port is not (devServerArguments,\nexported from ./app). smrt app vite stays verbatim.\n\nThe template''s browser fixture drops its --host/--port workaround.\n\nRefs #3410\n\n* fix(cli): keep a redacted tail of a failed smrt app start''s output\n\nItem 4 of the #3410 patch train. smrt app start spawned the detached web\nprocess with stdio ''ignore'', so \"exited before becoming ready\" left no\ntrace of why. The process now writes stdout/stderr to a fresh 0600\n<state>/app.log per start (removed, then created exclusively, so a planted\nlink is never written through; a pipe would EPIPE once the CLI exits).\nA start that never proves readiness throws ApplicationStartError, and the\nenvelope gains output (the last <= 8 KiB, redacted with redactSecrets\nagainst the child environment before the cut) and logFile. Message and\nexit code are unchanged.\n\nRefs #3410\n\n* docs(cli): keep the db precedence note inside the AGENTS chain cap\n\nItem 2 of the #3410 patch train: the precedence paragraph pushed the\npackages/cli AGENTS chain 166 bytes over the 32 KB cap; the README keeps\nthe full rule.\n\nRefs #3410\n\n* fix(cli): fail closed on a present falsy runtime block\n\nItem 1 of the #3410 patch train, review finding F2. resolveConfiguredRuntime\nsent runtime: null / false / 0 / '''' down the local default branch. Only an\nabsent property (or an explicit undefined) now means \"no runtime block\";\nany other present value goes to the existing validator, which rejects it.\n\nRefs #3410\n\n* fix(cli): redact short secrets from a failed start''s captured output\n\nItem 4 of the #3410 patch train, review finding F1. The start output tail\nwent through redactSecrets, which skips secret-named environment values\nshorter than eight characters and Bearer tokens shorter than eight, so a\nchild printing a six-character key leaked it under\nsecretValuesIncluded: false.\n\nredactSecrets gains an opt-in { strict: true } that redacts every\nnon-empty secret-named value and every Bearer token whatever its length;\nthe capture path (and the envelope''s second pass over it) uses it. The\ndefault is unchanged: its floor keeps short flag values from erasing\nordinary characters in operator messages, and strict never redacts less.\n\nRefs #3410\n\n* fix(cli): run strict redaction after the credential patterns\n\nItem 4 of the #3410 patch train, review finding F1 (follow-up). The strict\npass replaced short secret-named values before the URL-userinfo pattern\nran; a value that is URL syntax (Vite''s BASE_URL=/) broke the URL apart so\nthe userinfo pattern no longer matched and a database password survived.\nLong values and the patterns now run first, exactly as the default does;\nthe strict pass then redacts short values and short Bearer tokens in one\nalternation over the text between existing markers.\n\nRefs #3410\n\n* fix(cli): mask credential spans as one union before literal values split them\n\nItem 4 of the #3410 patch train, review findings G1/G2. redactSecrets\nreplaced literal secret-named env values first, so a value that was a\nBearer-token prefix (SMRT_TOKEN=abcdefgh vs Bearer abcdefghXYZ123) left\nthe token tail visible, and a value equal to a URL scheme and host\n(BASE_URL=postgres://smrt) stopped the userinfo pattern from matching and\nlet the password through - in the default and the strict mode.\n\nEvery structural span (URL userinfo, query credential, Bearer token) and\nevery literal value occurrence is now located on the raw text and the\nunion is masked at once; a final structural pass over the result only\nadds masks, so nothing the previous order masked is exposed (checked\nagainst the previous algorithm in the tests).\n\nRefs #3410\n\n* fix(cli): keep redaction markers opaque and the start tail bounded\n\nItem 4 of the #3410 patch train, review finding H1. The envelope''s second\nstrict pass rescanned existing [redacted] markers: with a one-character\nsecret (SMRT_SECRET_KEY=e) every marker''s own e characters matched again,\ncorrupting the markers and growing an 8 KiB tail to about 22 KiB.\n\nredactSecrets now treats existing markers as opaque - a literal match\ninside one is skipped and markers join the masked union, so a touching\nspan merges into them - which makes a second pass a no-op on already\nredacted text. The capture cut and the envelope both go through a shared\nboundedTail, so the reported output stays within START_OUTPUT_TAIL_BYTES\nafter every pass.\n\nRefs #3410\n\n* feat(core): generated SvelteKit routes resolve collections through the app runtime\n\nGenerated /api routes (CRUD, custom actions, _changes, _events, sync/apply,\n_dev) no longer import a hand-written getCollection/getSmrtConfig from\n$lib/server/smrt. Each opens with a prelude that imports the generated\nsmrt-register module and resolves its accessors through the new\ncreateGeneratedCollectionAccess() over the app''s config module: the exported\napp-runtime `runtime` (runtime.getCollection()/classOptions(), evaluated per\ncall so an RLS request gets its transaction-bound database), or, deprecated\nfor one release with a warning, a legacy getCollection/getSmrtConfig export.\n\nsmrtPlugin() now prepends the generated registration import to the\nconfigured config module, so apps drop the guarded smrt-register import. A\nmissing config module is generated runtime-shaped when the app installs\n@happyvertical/smrt-app-runtime.\n\nRefs #3416\n\n* feat(app-runtime): runtime.getCollection() and a default local writer lease\n\ncreateSmrtSvelteKitRuntime() gains getCollection(className), which builds\nthe registered collection from classOptions() on every call (the request\nRLS transaction inside a database-rls request, the base config outside it,\nclass db overrides kept). Generated routes resolve collections through it.\n\nIn the local profile the runtime now takes the state-root writer lease\nshared with smrt app operations by default (defaultWriterLease(): the same\nacquireWriterLease(prepareApplicationStateRoot(context)) call apps wrote,\npresenting SMRT_OPERATION_INSTANCE). An explicit acquireWriterLease factory\nstill replaces it; acquireWriterLease: false opts out. Deployed profiles\nnever take it.\n\nRefs #3416\n\n* docs(agents): shorten the scoped-name rule to keep the chat chain under the cap\n\nLane #3408''s root AGENTS.md line and lane #3414''s chat AGENTS.md each fit\nalone; combined they put the chat chain 14 bytes over 32 KB.\n\nRefs #3408\n\n* refactor(template-sveltekit): reduce smrt.ts to the runtime and its options\n\nThe template''s src/lib/server/smrt.ts drops the guarded smrt-register\nimport and its isMissingRegisterModule predicate, the local manifest\nhydration, the objects index import, the hand-wired writer lease, and the\ngetCollection/getSmrtConfig exports: the smrt() plugin now registers the\ngenerated objects, generated routes resolve collections through\nruntime.getCollection(), and the runtime holds the local writer lease by\ndefault. The home page uses runtime.getCollection()/classOptions().\n\nRefs #3416\n\n* fix(core): refuse a SvelteKit config module named like the generated registration\n\nA svelteKit.configFileName resolving to smrt-register (any script extension\nor case, or a path ending in it) made generation overwrite the authored\nconfig with the generated registration module, and the generated route\nprelude then read that module as the application config: builds stayed green\nand every request failed for lack of a runtime. Generation now fails with a\nclear error before any file is written or modified.\n\nRefs #3416\n\n* docs(core,app-runtime,template-sveltekit): describe the embedded route access prelude\n\nReconcile the contract with what ships: generated routes embed a prelude\nthat imports the generated smrt-register module and the app''s config module\n($lib/server/smrt by default) and resolve collections through its exported\nruntime; a legacy getCollection/getSmrtConfig export takes precedence for\none release with a deprecation warning. There is no generated route-access\nmodule.\n\nRefs #3416\n\n* feat(app-runtime): owner-minted local MCP tokens and hosted principal resolver\n\nAdd a local-profile token store for MCP clients: owner-bound, scoped,\nexpiring and revocable bearer tokens whose plaintext is returned once and\nwhose domain-separated HMAC is the only stored value (runtime-owned\n`_smrt_local_mcp_tokens` system table). Issue refuses scopes the owner does\nnot hold; verify fails closed and caps scopes to live permissions.\n\n`openLocalMcpTokenStore()` serves operator commands on an uncached\nconnection without the writer lease. The SvelteKit runtime gains\n`verifyLocalMcpToken()` and a default membership-backed\n`resolveMcpPrincipal()` for hosted profiles.\n\nRefs #3413\n\n* feat(smrt-app-mcp): accept local owner tokens and runtime principal bindings\n\n`createHostedMcpResourceAuth({ runtime })` now takes the application\nruntime''s credential bindings. In the local profile a runtime\n`verifyLocalMcpToken` yields the new `createLocalMcpTokenAuth` adapter, a\n`sessionFallback` adapter: requests without `Authorization` keep the\nsession principal, while a presented bearer must verify (401, never cookie\nfallback) and dispatches through `bindPrincipal`. The origin check still\nruns first and the metadata route stays 404 locally. Hosted profiles default\nto the runtime''s membership-backed `resolveMcpPrincipal`; an explicit\n`resolvePrincipal` still overrides it.\n\nRefs #3413\n\n* feat(app-cli): configurable MCP endpoint path for the stdio bridge\n\nAdd `--mcp-path` / `SMRT_MCP_PATH` to `smrt-mcp-bridge`, `--mcp-path` /\n`SMRT_APP_MCP_PATH` to `smrt-app`, `CreateAppCliOptions.mcpPath` and\n`startMcpBridge({ mcpPath })`. The default stays `/api/mcp`; the path is\nvalidated as same-server absolute before the bridge listens.\n\nRefs #3413\n\n* feat(cli): smrt app token for local MCP client credentials\n\n`smrt app token --scopes <s> [--expires 30d] [--label …]` issues an\nowner-bound bearer token for a local MCP client and prints it once;\n`token list` and `token revoke <id>` never print token values. Local\nprofile only; arguments are validated before any state is touched, the\nstore opens without the writer lease (the app may keep running), and\nwrites serialize under the operation lock.\n\nRefs #3413\n\n* feat(template-sveltekit): overlay uses runtime MCP credential bindings\n\nThe MCP Apps overlay passes the runtime to `createHostedMcpResourceAuth`,\nso the local profile accepts owner-minted tokens and hosted profiles use\nthe default membership-backed principal mapping; the placeholder\n`mcp-hosted-principal.ts` binding is removed. A new end-to-end test mints\nwith `smrt app token`, drives the real `smrt-mcp-bridge` binary over stdio\n(`--mcp-path=/mcp`) against `mountMcpAppRoute` on the real runtime, and\nproves read-only tools, owner-tenant data, revocation, expiry, wrong-tenant\nand live-permission denial. Adds `@happyvertical/smrt-app-cli` and\n`@modelcontextprotocol/client` as test devDependencies.\n\nRefs #3413\n\n* docs(app-cli,smrt-app-mcp): use s-m-r-t prose in the new MCP credential sections\n\nRefs #3413\n\n* fix(app-runtime): bind bearer principals only through a direct membership\n\nLocal MCP token verification and `runAsPrincipal` resolved permissions with\n`PermissionResolver`''s inheritance fallback, so deleting the owner''s direct\nmembership in the token''s tenant left an inheriting ancestor membership''s\npermissions in force. Both now require an active direct membership of the\nprincipal''s user in exactly its tenant and pin that row into permission\nresolution (`direct-membership.ts`), so inherited authority can never\nsubstitute for it. Tests cover deletion with an inheriting ancestor\n(runtime and the stdio route), suspension, and the active case.\n\nRefs #3413\n\n* fix(app-cli): reject malformed or repeated smrt-mcp-bridge options\n\nThe bridge binary took the first matching argument and treated an empty or\nmissing `--mcp-path` value as absent, silently targeting `/api/mcp`.\n`parseMcpBridgeArgs` now requires a non-empty value for every value option,\nrejects repeats, and validates any explicitly supplied path, including an\nempty `SMRT_MCP_PATH`, through `resolveMcpPath`; usage errors print to\nstderr and exit 2 before the bridge listens.\n\nRefs #3413\n\n* fix(app-runtime,smrt-app-mcp): explicit tenant binding mode for bearer principals\n\nThe F1 fix made `runAsPrincipal` direct-only for every bearer, which denied\nhosted application mappings to tenants held legitimately through an active\ninheritable ancestor membership. The binding mode is now carried from the\nauthentication adapter as `principal.tenantBinding`: the local owner-token\nadapter always stamps `direct`; the JWT adapter stamps the mapping''s value\nor `direct-or-inherited`; the runtime''s default hosted resolver maps\n`direct`. `runAsPrincipal` applies `direct` (active direct membership in\nexactly the tenant) or `direct-or-inherited` (the default, the session\nstep''s `isSessionTenantAuthorized` rule), always pinning an existing direct\nrow so inheritance never substitutes for it. Unknown modes are rejected.\n\nRefs #3413\n\n* fix(app-runtime): local token principals always bind direct-only\n\n`verifyLocalMcpToken()` / `mcpTokens.verify()` returned a principal without\na binding mode, so passing it straight to `runAsPrincipal()` defaulted to\n`direct-or-inherited` and an inheriting ancestor could replace a deleted\ndirect membership. Verified principals are now frozen, carry a readonly\n`tenantBinding: ''direct''` and an enumerable `LOCAL_MCP_TOKEN_PRINCIPAL`\nbrand that survives spreading; `runAsPrincipal` binds any branded principal\ndirect-only and rejects (does not ignore) a copy that sets another binding.\n\nRefs #3413\n\n* fix(app-runtime,smrt-app-mcp): freeze verified token scopes; binders copy scopes\n\nA verified local-token principal was frozen but its `scopes` array was not,\nso `verified.scopes.push(...)` before `runAsPrincipal()` widened the bound\nscopes beyond the minted token. `LocalMcpTokenPrincipal.scopes` is now\n`readonly string[]` and every verifier result freezes a copied array;\n`runAsPrincipal` snapshots the requested scopes before any await, and the\nlocal-token adapter copies them. The MCP runtime binding type accepts a\nreadonly scopes array (`McpLocalTokenPrincipal`).\n\nRefs #3413\n\n* fix(app-runtime): bind one immutable snapshot of the principal\n\n`runAsPrincipal()` snapshotted `scopes` before awaiting but built the\ncallback principal from `{ ...principal }` afterwards, so a caller mutating\n`id` or `tenantId` during membership resolution could hand `fn` an identity\nor tenant different from the bound permission/RLS context. It now takes one\ncomplete, validated snapshot (id, tenantId, kind, tenantBinding, scopes)\nbefore the first await, authorizes from it, never reads the caller''s object\nagain, and passes `fn` a frozen copy of the snapshot with the effective\nbinding and frozen effective scopes.\n\nRefs #3413\n\n* fix(app-runtime,smrt-app-mcp): deep-freeze the bound principal snapshot\n\nThe principal snapshot was a shallow copy, so `roles` (and any other array\nor object field) stayed shared with the caller and unfrozen: appending a\nprivileged role while membership resolution awaited reached `fn`.\n`runAsPrincipal` now takes a validated, deep-frozen copy of the whole\nprincipal before the first await: known fields are type-checked (strings;\n`scopes`/`roles` string arrays; `allowCrossTenant` boolean), unknown own\nenumerable fields are kept as deep-frozen copies of plain data, and\nfunctions, class instances or over-deep values are rejected. The callback\ntype is now `SmrtRuntimeBoundPrincipalSnapshot<P>` (deeply readonly), and\n`McpPrincipalBinder`''s `run` accepts the readonly `McpBoundPrincipal`.\n\nRefs #3413\n\n* fix(app-runtime,smrt-app-mcp): own-data-only principal snapshots; reject prototype poison\n\n`deepFrozenCopy` assigned keys into `{}`, so a JSON-parsed principal with\nan own `__proto__` key swapped the copy''s prototype and the identity checks\nread inherited values: a principal could bind as another user. Copies are\nnow built by `deepFrozenPlainCopy` (`plain-data.ts`) from own data\nproperties into null-prototype objects and fresh dense arrays, deep-frozen,\nrejecting `__proto__`/`constructor`/`prototype` keys at every depth,\naccessors (never invoked), non-plain or inheriting objects, sparse or\nextended arrays, functions and deep nesting. Authority fields are read with\nown-property access; the principal handed to `fn` is null-prototype too.\nToken `issue()` input, `resolveMcpPrincipal`''s identity, and both MCP\nadapters'' principal mappings (`own-data.ts`) get the same own-data reads.\n\nRefs #3413\n\n* test(vitest): scope the issue-2750 registry fixture package name\n\n#3408 fails generation early for unscoped app names that declare classes;\nthis fixture declared classes under an unscoped name and the root test\nrun caught it after the lanes were combined.\n\nRefs #3408\n\n* fix(cli): drop a failed start''s oversized leading record before redaction\n\n`smrt app start` reads the last 64 KiB of a failed child''s output and drops\nthe window''s leading partial line before redacting. When that window held\nno newline, `slice(indexOf(''\\n'') + 1)` kept the whole window: a single\nrecord longer than the window whose credential prefix (`Bearer `, URL\nuserinfo, `?token=`) fell before it was reported unredacted while the\nenvelope said `secretValuesIncluded: false`. A truncated window with no\nnewline is now one record''s suffix and is dropped entirely.\n\nRefs #3410\n\n* fix(chat): never keep the request''s RLS transaction past a streamed turn\n\nUnder PostgreSQL `database-rls` with the documented\n`db: () => runtime.databaseConfig()`, `mountAssistantRoutes` handed the\nrequest''s transaction to ChatService, the tools and the outcome callbacks,\nbut the detached turn kept running after the streaming Response returned,\nand the runtime''s session step commits that transaction when `resolve`\nreturns. Tool calls, the reply and the outcome then ran against a completed\ntransaction: a stored user message with no settled turn.\n\n- New `runtime` option (structural `AssistantRouteRuntime`:\n  `databaseConfig()` + `runAsPrincipal()`, satisfied by the app runtime).\n  `db` defaults to `() => runtime.databaseConfig()`.\n- Inside an RLS request transaction, with `runtime`, the turn waits for\n  that transaction to end, then runs in its own principal-bound transaction\n  (`runtime.runAsPrincipal`, scopes capped to a permission snapshot): chat,\n  tools and continuations are rebound there, the stored send is checked\n  first (a rolled-back request runs no turn), and `client_tool_calls`,\n  `done` and `error` are held until that transaction commits. If it fails,\n  the send is settled `failed` in a fresh lifetime.\n- Without `runtime`, such a turn runs to completion inside the request\n  before the response returns, so the existing wiring stays correct.\n- Outside an RLS transaction (SQLite, the local profile) nothing changes.\n\nPostgreSQL integration cases (NOSUPERUSER NOBYPASSRLS role, FORCEd tenant\npolicy on chat_messages) cover a reply delayed past the handler, client\ncancellation, a request rollback, a turn-transaction rollback and the\nin-request fallback; `test:postgres` runs them.\n\nRefs #3414\n\n* fix(chat): run a bound turn with the runtime''s effective scopes\n\n`runtime.runAsPrincipal` caps live permissions to the supplied scopes and\nhands its callback the bound principal, but the turn ignored it and was\nrebuilt from the request''s `principal.permissions`; `executeAsPrincipal`\nthen published that pre-bind set explicitly, bypassing live resolution, so\na permission revoked between the send and the bind was regained by tools.\n\nThe callback now receives the bound principal (`AssistantRouteBoundPrincipal`)\nand the rebuilt turn, and its tool permission context, use its effective\n`scopes`, kept within the cap the route supplied. Malformed scopes refuse\nthe turn.\n\nThe PostgreSQL fixture now resolves live permissions from real membership\nrows for the request and the bind, and its `runAsPrincipal` follows the\nruntime (cap only when scopes are given; the callback gets the effective\nset). New case: a snapshotted permission revoked before the turn binds is\nabsent from the tool''s run and its database session.\n\nRefs #3414\n\n* fix(chat): cap a bound turn to the request''s frozen permission set\n\n`resolveAssistantPrincipalFromLocals()` carries no permission snapshot, so\n`respondWithTurn()` omitted `scopes` and the runtime applied no cap: a turn\nbinding after the request committed got every permission live at bind time,\nincluding grants made after the send was accepted.\n\nThe route now freezes the request''s authority before the response returns\n(the principal''s snapshot, else the permissions the request''s RLS context\npublished; an empty set stays empty) and always passes it as `scopes`, so\nthe turn runs with (request snapshot ∩ live at bind).\n\nCases: a permission granted between the send and the bind is absent from\nthe tool''s run and database session, and an empty request set stays empty\nwhen a permission is granted during the handoff.\n\nRefs #3414\n\n* fix(chat): settle a send whose request commits after the turn start timed out\n\nWhen a streamed turn''s request transaction was still open after the 60 s\nstart wait, the turn reported an error and settled the send only if it had\nalready confirmed it, which happens after the wait. A request that committed\nlater left its user message unsettled while the client had an error.\n\nAfter reporting the timeout the route keeps watching the request''s\ntransaction (up to `abandonedTurnMs`): once it ends, a fresh principal\nlifetime records the send `failed` if it committed, and does nothing if it\nrolled back. The wait is configurable as `turnStartTimeoutMs`\n(`DEFAULT_ASSISTANT_TURN_START_TIMEOUT_MS`, 60 s).\n\nCases with a 50 ms start timeout: a request committing after it settles\n`failed` without calling the model; one rolling back after it stores and\nsettles nothing.\n\nRefs #3414\n\n* fix(cli): print smrt app token usage for --help before the implicit create\n\n--help was classified as an implicit create option and rejected as an\nunknown token option. Handle help, --help and -h first.\n\nRefs #3413","tree":{"sha":"8acc8b458e1bcca0bc89ec63e066ca57e9a77aa4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/git/trees/8acc8b458e1bcca0bc89ec63e066ca57e9a77aa4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/git/commits/5db5509e0c36a99f1c432f05ec48f1bf7a509cd0","verification":{"payload":"tree 8acc8b458e1bcca0bc89ec63e066ca57e9a77aa4\nparent c5cff827ded039ff35667f1971b9b63692f21e33\nauthor Will Griffin <willgriffin@gmail.com> 1791085189 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791085189 +0000\n\nfeat: starter gaps — local MCP tokens, runtime collections, assistant defaults (#3367) (#3472)\n\n* fix(web): accept the generated { items } list envelope in unwrapListResult\n\nRefs #3412\n\n* feat(svelte): AppShell passes the Provider''s DataSurfaceRegistry to the dock snippet\n\nFix the ShellDockTool icon docs example (icon takes a component).\n\nRefs #3415\n\n* feat(chat): default mountAssistantRoutes tools, db and ai\n\nmountAssistantRoutes now needs no glue for the common case:\n\n- Without `tools`, the route offers the manifest operations `allowedTools`\n  names (buildManifestToolCatalog), minus names an `extraTools` entry\n  serves. Fail-closed is unchanged: absent or empty offers nothing. A name\n  nothing provides is an error: at mount when its collection is already\n  registered, otherwise the turn answers 503 before anything is stored\n  (skipped when `actions` is set, since action tools are allow-listed too).\n  An explicit `tools` value (even []) keeps the old behaviour.\n- `db` also accepts a per-request resolver, called once per request, so a\n  `database-rls` app passes `() => runtime.databaseConfig()`. The fixed\n  form still works.\n- `ai` is optional: omitted, each turn builds the client from the\n  smrt.config `ai` block through resolveConfiguredAIProvider and\n  toAIClientOptions (loading the config file if no one has). Nothing\n  configured answers 503 and sends AIProviderNotConfiguredError, which names\n  variables and never values, to onError only. An explicitly empty `ai` is\n  still a mount error.\n\nRefs #3414\n\n* fix(chat): honour PLAYWRIGHT_CHROMIUM_EXECUTABLE_PATH in e2e config\n\nThe chat e2e config ignored the override the sibling package configs\nhonour, so test:e2e could not run where the downloaded Chromium cannot\nload (missing libgbm).\n\nRefs #3414\n\n* fix(core): fail at scan time when an app package name is unscoped\n\nAn unscoped package.json name made generation emit pkg:Class keys that\nisQualifiedName (and the isolated-manifest validator) reject, surfacing\nas CONFIG_INVALID_ISOLATED_MANIFEST at build. The @scope/ requirement is\na deliberate contract (#713), so manifest generation now throws\nCONFIG_UNSCOPED_PACKAGE_NAME with a rename hint when a package declares\nclasses. Test fixtures now use scoped names.\n\nRefs #3408\n\n* fix(app-runtime): remove onboarding hand-off files after a committed owner claim\n\ncreateOwnerSetupPage now deletes onboarding.json and onboarding-launch.html\nfrom the private state root once claimOwner resolves, so pnpm app:open stops\noffering the spent invitation. Failed claims leave them untouched;\nonOwnerClaimed still runs for extra cleanup and removeOnboardingHandoff:false\nopts out. Adds runtime.applicationStateRoot() and ONBOARDING_HANDOFF_FILES.\nThe template drops its copied onOwnerClaimed glue.\n\nRefs #3411\n\n* feat(cli): print the one-time setup URL to the operator terminal\n\nsmrt app setup and recover print the loopback /setup?token= URL through an\noptional io.operatorTerminal sink that exists only when stdout and stderr are\nTTYs; the URL never reaches stdout/stderr logs or pipes.\n\nRefs #3411\n\n* fix(app-runtime): clean up onboarding hand-off before setting the session cookie\n\nA throwing cookies.set() after the claim committed skipped the removal and left\nthe spent invitation. Removal now runs right after claimOwner resolves. Updates\nthe AGENTS.md note that still called cleanup an injected hook.\n\nRefs #3411\n\n* fix(cli): default smrt app to the local profile without a runtime block\n\nItem 1 of the #3410 patch train. smrt app setup failed \"profile must be\nlocal, self-hosted, or cloud\" for a smrt.config with no runtime block,\nwhile app-runtime''s SvelteKit entry resolves that config as local. The\nCLI resolver now applies the same rule; a present but invalid block still\nfails closed.\n\nRefs #3410\n\n* fix(cli): honour DATABASE_URL/DATABASE_TYPE as the db command fallback\n\nItem 2 of the #3410 patch train. smrt app setup and smrt app migrate\nexport DATABASE_URL/DATABASE_TYPE for the child smrt db:migrate, but every\ndb command read only packages.cli.database and failed \"Database\nconfiguration required\", so an application had to forward the variables\nin its own config.\n\nmain() now applies the environment once, after loadConfig, with an\nexplicit precedence: a config-declared packages.cli.database.url wins (a\nstray shell URL never retargets a configured project), then DATABASE_URL\nwith the engine from config type, DATABASE_TYPE, or the URL scheme, then\nthe :memory: default the schema commands refuse. URL and engine travel as\na pair; an unsupported DATABASE_TYPE disables the fallback with a warning\nthat never echoes the URL.\n\nThe template''s smrt.config.ts drops its packages.cli.database forwarding.\n\nRefs #3410\n\n* fix(cli): load .env beside a TypeScript smrt.config\n\nDrive-by on the #3410 patch train (item 2''s path). main() looks for .env\nnext to smrt.config.{js,mjs,cjs,json} only, while the config loader also\nfinds smrt.config.{ts,mts,cts} (the template default), so a direct smrt\ndb:migrate in such an app never saw DATABASE_URL from .env. The shell\nstill wins over the file.\n\nRefs #3410\n\n* fix(cli): bind smrt app dev to the loopback host the URLs name\n\nItem 3 of the #3410 patch train. smrt app dev ran vite dev with the\ncaller''s arguments only, so Vite bound its default host localhost, which\nNode resolves to [::1] first, while onboarding and app:open hand out\nhttp://127.0.0.1:<PORT>/ - connection refused until the user edited the\nURL. smrt app dev now adds --host 127.0.0.1 unless --host is given, and\n--port $PORT when PORT is set and --port is not (devServerArguments,\nexported from ./app). smrt app vite stays verbatim.\n\nThe template''s browser fixture drops its --host/--port workaround.\n\nRefs #3410\n\n* fix(cli): keep a redacted tail of a failed smrt app start''s output\n\nItem 4 of the #3410 patch train. smrt app start spawned the detached web\nprocess with stdio ''ignore'', so \"exited before becoming ready\" left no\ntrace of why. The process now writes stdout/stderr to a fresh 0600\n<state>/app.log per start (removed, then created exclusively, so a planted\nlink is never written through; a pipe would EPIPE once the CLI exits).\nA start that never proves readiness throws ApplicationStartError, and the\nenvelope gains output (the last <= 8 KiB, redacted with redactSecrets\nagainst the child environment before the cut) and logFile. Message and\nexit code are unchanged.\n\nRefs #3410\n\n* docs(cli): keep the db precedence note inside the AGENTS chain cap\n\nItem 2 of the #3410 patch train: the precedence paragraph pushed the\npackages/cli AGENTS chain 166 bytes over the 32 KB cap; the README keeps\nthe full rule.\n\nRefs #3410\n\n* fix(cli): fail closed on a present falsy runtime block\n\nItem 1 of the #3410 patch train, review finding F2. resolveConfiguredRuntime\nsent runtime: null / false / 0 / '''' down the local default branch. Only an\nabsent property (or an explicit undefined) now means \"no runtime block\";\nany other present value goes to the existing validator, which rejects it.\n\nRefs #3410\n\n* fix(cli): redact short secrets from a failed start''s captured output\n\nItem 4 of the #3410 patch train, review finding F1. The start output tail\nwent through redactSecrets, which skips secret-named environment values\nshorter than eight characters and Bearer tokens shorter than eight, so a\nchild printing a six-character key leaked it under\nsecretValuesIncluded: false.\n\nredactSecrets gains an opt-in { strict: true } that redacts every\nnon-empty secret-named value and every Bearer token whatever its length;\nthe capture path (and the envelope''s second pass over it) uses it. The\ndefault is unchanged: its floor keeps short flag values from erasing\nordinary characters in operator messages, and strict never redacts less.\n\nRefs #3410\n\n* fix(cli): run strict redaction after the credential patterns\n\nItem 4 of the #3410 patch train, review finding F1 (follow-up). The strict\npass replaced short secret-named values before the URL-userinfo pattern\nran; a value that is URL syntax (Vite''s BASE_URL=/) broke the URL apart so\nthe userinfo pattern no longer matched and a database password survived.\nLong values and the patterns now run first, exactly as the default does;\nthe strict pass then redacts short values and short Bearer tokens in one\nalternation over the text between existing markers.\n\nRefs #3410\n\n* fix(cli): mask credential spans as one union before literal values split them\n\nItem 4 of the #3410 patch train, review findings G1/G2. redactSecrets\nreplaced literal secret-named env values first, so a value that was a\nBearer-token prefix (SMRT_TOKEN=abcdefgh vs Bearer abcdefghXYZ123) left\nthe token tail visible, and a value equal to a URL scheme and host\n(BASE_URL=postgres://smrt) stopped the userinfo pattern from matching and\nlet the password through - in the default and the strict mode.\n\nEvery structural span (URL userinfo, query credential, Bearer token) and\nevery literal value occurrence is now located on the raw text and the\nunion is masked at once; a final structural pass over the result only\nadds masks, so nothing the previous order masked is exposed (checked\nagainst the previous algorithm in the tests).\n\nRefs #3410\n\n* fix(cli): keep redaction markers opaque and the start tail bounded\n\nItem 4 of the #3410 patch train, review finding H1. The envelope''s second\nstrict pass rescanned existing [redacted] markers: with a one-character\nsecret (SMRT_SECRET_KEY=e) every marker''s own e characters matched again,\ncorrupting the markers and growing an 8 KiB tail to about 22 KiB.\n\nredactSecrets now treats existing markers as opaque - a literal match\ninside one is skipped and markers join the masked union, so a touching\nspan merges into them - which makes a second pass a no-op on already\nredacted text. The capture cut and the envelope both go through a shared\nboundedTail, so the reported output stays within START_OUTPUT_TAIL_BYTES\nafter every pass.\n\nRefs #3410\n\n* feat(core): generated SvelteKit routes resolve collections through the app runtime\n\nGenerated /api routes (CRUD, custom actions, _changes, _events, sync/apply,\n_dev) no longer import a hand-written getCollection/getSmrtConfig from\n$lib/server/smrt. Each opens with a prelude that imports the generated\nsmrt-register module and resolves its accessors through the new\ncreateGeneratedCollectionAccess() over the app''s config module: the exported\napp-runtime `runtime` (runtime.getCollection()/classOptions(), evaluated per\ncall so an RLS request gets its transaction-bound database), or, deprecated\nfor one release with a warning, a legacy getCollection/getSmrtConfig export.\n\nsmrtPlugin() now prepends the generated registration import to the\nconfigured config module, so apps drop the guarded smrt-register import. A\nmissing config module is generated runtime-shaped when the app installs\n@happyvertical/smrt-app-runtime.\n\nRefs #3416\n\n* feat(app-runtime): runtime.getCollection() and a default local writer lease\n\ncreateSmrtSvelteKitRuntime() gains getCollection(className), which builds\nthe registered collection from classOptions() on every call (the request\nRLS transaction inside a database-rls request, the base config outside it,\nclass db overrides kept). Generated routes resolve collections through it.\n\nIn the local profile the runtime now takes the state-root writer lease\nshared with smrt app operations by default (defaultWriterLease(): the same\nacquireWriterLease(prepareApplicationStateRoot(context)) call apps wrote,\npresenting SMRT_OPERATION_INSTANCE). An explicit acquireWriterLease factory\nstill replaces it; acquireWriterLease: false opts out. Deployed profiles\nnever take it.\n\nRefs #3416\n\n* docs(agents): shorten the scoped-name rule to keep the chat chain under the cap\n\nLane #3408''s root AGENTS.md line and lane #3414''s chat AGENTS.md each fit\nalone; combined they put the chat chain 14 bytes over 32 KB.\n\nRefs #3408\n\n* refactor(template-sveltekit): reduce smrt.ts to the runtime and its options\n\nThe template''s src/lib/server/smrt.ts drops the guarded smrt-register\nimport and its isMissingRegisterModule predicate, the local manifest\nhydration, the objects index import, the hand-wired writer lease, and the\ngetCollection/getSmrtConfig exports: the smrt() plugin now registers the\ngenerated objects, generated routes resolve collections through\nruntime.getCollection(), and the runtime holds the local writer lease by\ndefault. The home page uses runtime.getCollection()/classOptions().\n\nRefs #3416\n\n* fix(core): refuse a SvelteKit config module named like the generated registration\n\nA svelteKit.configFileName resolving to smrt-register (any script extension\nor case, or a path ending in it) made generation overwrite the authored\nconfig with the generated registration module, and the generated route\nprelude then read that module as the application config: builds stayed green\nand every request failed for lack of a runtime. Generation now fails with a\nclear error before any file is written or modified.\n\nRefs #3416\n\n* docs(core,app-runtime,template-sveltekit): describe the embedded route access prelude\n\nReconcile the contract with what ships: generated routes embed a prelude\nthat imports the generated smrt-register module and the app''s config module\n($lib/server/smrt by default) and resolve collections through its exported\nruntime; a legacy getCollection/getSmrtConfig export takes precedence for\none release with a deprecation warning. There is no generated route-access\nmodule.\n\nRefs #3416\n\n* feat(app-runtime): owner-minted local MCP tokens and hosted principal resolver\n\nAdd a local-profile token store for MCP clients: owner-bound, scoped,\nexpiring and revocable bearer tokens whose plaintext is returned once and\nwhose domain-separated HMAC is the only stored value (runtime-owned\n`_smrt_local_mcp_tokens` system table). Issue refuses scopes the owner does\nnot hold; verify fails closed and caps scopes to live permissions.\n\n`openLocalMcpTokenStore()` serves operator commands on an uncached\nconnection without the writer lease. The SvelteKit runtime gains\n`verifyLocalMcpToken()` and a default membership-backed\n`resolveMcpPrincipal()` for hosted profiles.\n\nRefs #3413\n\n* feat(smrt-app-mcp): accept local owner tokens and runtime principal bindings\n\n`createHostedMcpResourceAuth({ runtime })` now takes the application\nruntime''s credential bindings. In the local profile a runtime\n`verifyLocalMcpToken` yields the new `createLocalMcpTokenAuth` adapter, a\n`sessionFallback` adapter: requests without `Authorization` keep the\nsession principal, while a presented bearer must verify (401, never cookie\nfallback) and dispatches through `bindPrincipal`. The origin check still\nruns first and the metadata route stays 404 locally. Hosted profiles default\nto the runtime''s membership-backed `resolveMcpPrincipal`; an explicit\n`resolvePrincipal` still overrides it.\n\nRefs #3413\n\n* feat(app-cli): configurable MCP endpoint path for the stdio bridge\n\nAdd `--mcp-path` / `SMRT_MCP_PATH` to `smrt-mcp-bridge`, `--mcp-path` /\n`SMRT_APP_MCP_PATH` to `smrt-app`, `CreateAppCliOptions.mcpPath` and\n`startMcpBridge({ mcpPath })`. The default stays `/api/mcp`; the path is\nvalidated as same-server absolute before the bridge listens.\n\nRefs #3413\n\n* feat(cli): smrt app token for local MCP client credentials\n\n`smrt app token --scopes <s> [--expires 30d] [--label …]` issues an\nowner-bound bearer token for a local MCP client and prints it once;\n`token list` and `token revoke <id>` never print token values. Local\nprofile only; arguments are validated before any state is touched, the\nstore opens without the writer lease (the app may keep running), and\nwrites serialize under the operation lock.\n\nRefs #3413\n\n* feat(template-sveltekit): overlay uses runtime MCP credential bindings\n\nThe MCP Apps overlay passes the runtime to `createHostedMcpResourceAuth`,\nso the local profile accepts owner-minted tokens and hosted profiles use\nthe default membership-backed principal mapping; the placeholder\n`mcp-hosted-principal.ts` binding is removed. A new end-to-end test mints\nwith `smrt app token`, drives the real `smrt-mcp-bridge` binary over stdio\n(`--mcp-path=/mcp`) against `mountMcpAppRoute` on the real runtime, and\nproves read-only tools, owner-tenant data, revocation, expiry, wrong-tenant\nand live-permission denial. Adds `@happyvertical/smrt-app-cli` and\n`@modelcontextprotocol/client` as test devDependencies.\n\nRefs #3413\n\n* docs(app-cli,smrt-app-mcp): use s-m-r-t prose in the new MCP credential sections\n\nRefs #3413\n\n* fix(app-runtime): bind bearer principals only through a direct membership\n\nLocal MCP token verification and `runAsPrincipal` resolved permissions with\n`PermissionResolver`''s inheritance fallback, so deleting the owner''s direct\nmembership in the token''s tenant left an inheriting ancestor membership''s\npermissions in force. Both now require an active direct membership of the\nprincipal''s user in exactly its tenant and pin that row into permission\nresolution (`direct-membership.ts`), so inherited authority can never\nsubstitute for it. Tests cover deletion with an inheriting ancestor\n(runtime and the stdio route), suspension, and the active case.\n\nRefs #3413\n\n* fix(app-cli): reject malformed or repeated smrt-mcp-bridge options\n\nThe bridge binary took the first matching argument and treated an empty or\nmissing `--mcp-path` value as absent, silently targeting `/api/mcp`.\n`parseMcpBridgeArgs` now requires a non-empty value for every value option,\nrejects repeats, and validates any explicitly supplied path, including an\nempty `SMRT_MCP_PATH`, through `resolveMcpPath`; usage errors print to\nstderr and exit 2 before the bridge listens.\n\nRefs #3413\n\n* fix(app-runtime,smrt-app-mcp): explicit tenant binding mode for bearer principals\n\nThe F1 fix made `runAsPrincipal` direct-only for every bearer, which denied\nhosted application mappings to tenants held legitimately through an active\ninheritable ancestor membership. The binding mode is now carried from the\nauthentication adapter as `principal.tenantBinding`: the local owner-token\nadapter always stamps `direct`; the JWT adapter stamps the mapping''s value\nor `direct-or-inherited`; the runtime''s default hosted resolver maps\n`direct`. `runAsPrincipal` applies `direct` (active direct membership in\nexactly the tenant) or `direct-or-inherited` (the default, the session\nstep''s `isSessionTenantAuthorized` rule), always pinning an existing direct\nrow so inheritance never substitutes for it. Unknown modes are rejected.\n\nRefs #3413\n\n* fix(app-runtime): local token principals always bind direct-only\n\n`verifyLocalMcpToken()` / `mcpTokens.verify()` returned a principal without\na binding mode, so passing it straight to `runAsPrincipal()` defaulted to\n`direct-or-inherited` and an inheriting ancestor could replace a deleted\ndirect membership. Verified principals are now frozen, carry a readonly\n`tenantBinding: ''direct''` and an enumerable `LOCAL_MCP_TOKEN_PRINCIPAL`\nbrand that survives spreading; `runAsPrincipal` binds any branded principal\ndirect-only and rejects (does not ignore) a copy that sets another binding.\n\nRefs #3413\n\n* fix(app-runtime,smrt-app-mcp): freeze verified token scopes; binders copy scopes\n\nA verified local-token principal was frozen but its `scopes` array was not,\nso `verified.scopes.push(...)` before `runAsPrincipal()` widened the bound\nscopes beyond the minted token. `LocalMcpTokenPrincipal.scopes` is now\n`readonly string[]` and every verifier result freezes a copied array;\n`runAsPrincipal` snapshots the requested scopes before any await, and the\nlocal-token adapter copies them. The MCP runtime binding type accepts a\nreadonly scopes array (`McpLocalTokenPrincipal`).\n\nRefs #3413\n\n* fix(app-runtime): bind one immutable snapshot of the principal\n\n`runAsPrincipal()` snapshotted `scopes` before awaiting but built the\ncallback principal from `{ ...principal }` afterwards, so a caller mutating\n`id` or `tenantId` during membership resolution could hand `fn` an identity\nor tenant different from the bound permission/RLS context. It now takes one\ncomplete, validated snapshot (id, tenantId, kind, tenantBinding, scopes)\nbefore the first await, authorizes from it, never reads the caller''s object\nagain, and passes `fn` a frozen copy of the snapshot with the effective\nbinding and frozen effective scopes.\n\nRefs #3413\n\n* fix(app-runtime,smrt-app-mcp): deep-freeze the bound principal snapshot\n\nThe principal snapshot was a shallow copy, so `roles` (and any other array\nor object field) stayed shared with the caller and unfrozen: appending a\nprivileged role while membership resolution awaited reached `fn`.\n`runAsPrincipal` now takes a validated, deep-frozen copy of the whole\nprincipal before the first await: known fields are type-checked (strings;\n`scopes`/`roles` string arrays; `allowCrossTenant` boolean), unknown own\nenumerable fields are kept as deep-frozen copies of plain data, and\nfunctions, class instances or over-deep values are rejected. The callback\ntype is now `SmrtRuntimeBoundPrincipalSnapshot<P>` (deeply readonly), and\n`McpPrincipalBinder`''s `run` accepts the readonly `McpBoundPrincipal`.\n\nRefs #3413\n\n* fix(app-runtime,smrt-app-mcp): own-data-only principal snapshots; reject prototype poison\n\n`deepFrozenCopy` assigned keys into `{}`, so a JSON-parsed principal with\nan own `__proto__` key swapped the copy''s prototype and the identity checks\nread inherited values: a principal could bind as another user. Copies are\nnow built by `deepFrozenPlainCopy` (`plain-data.ts`) from own data\nproperties into null-prototype objects and fresh dense arrays, deep-frozen,\nrejecting `__proto__`/`constructor`/`prototype` keys at every depth,\naccessors (never invoked), non-plain or inheriting objects, sparse or\nextended arrays, functions and deep nesting. Authority fields are read with\nown-property access; the principal handed to `fn` is null-prototype too.\nToken `issue()` input, `resolveMcpPrincipal`''s identity, and both MCP\nadapters'' principal mappings (`own-data.ts`) get the same own-data reads.\n\nRefs #3413\n\n* test(vitest): scope the issue-2750 registry fixture package name\n\n#3408 fails generation early for unscoped app names that declare classes;\nthis fixture declared classes under an unscoped name and the root test\nrun caught it after the lanes were combined.\n\nRefs #3408\n\n* fix(cli): drop a failed start''s oversized leading record before redaction\n\n`smrt app start` reads the last 64 KiB of a failed child''s output and drops\nthe window''s leading partial line before redacting. When that window held\nno newline, `slice(indexOf(''\\n'') + 1)` kept the whole window: a single\nrecord longer than the window whose credential prefix (`Bearer `, URL\nuserinfo, `?token=`) fell before it was reported unredacted while the\nenvelope said `secretValuesIncluded: false`. A truncated window with no\nnewline is now one record''s suffix and is dropped entirely.\n\nRefs #3410\n\n* fix(chat): never keep the request''s RLS transaction past a streamed turn\n\nUnder PostgreSQL `database-rls` with the documented\n`db: () => runtime.databaseConfig()`, `mountAssistantRoutes` handed the\nrequest''s transaction to ChatService, the tools and the outcome callbacks,\nbut the detached turn kept running after the streaming Response returned,\nand the runtime''s session step commits that transaction when `resolve`\nreturns. Tool calls, the reply and the outcome then ran against a completed\ntransaction: a stored user message with no settled turn.\n\n- New `runtime` option (structural `AssistantRouteRuntime`:\n  `databaseConfig()` + `runAsPrincipal()`, satisfied by the app runtime).\n  `db` defaults to `() => runtime.databaseConfig()`.\n- Inside an RLS request transaction, with `runtime`, the turn waits for\n  that transaction to end, then runs in its own principal-bound transaction\n  (`runtime.runAsPrincipal`, scopes capped to a permission snapshot): chat,\n  tools and continuations are rebound there, the stored send is checked\n  first (a rolled-back request runs no turn), and `client_tool_calls`,\n  `done` and `error` are held until that transaction commits. If it fails,\n  the send is settled `failed` in a fresh lifetime.\n- Without `runtime`, such a turn runs to completion inside the request\n  before the response returns, so the existing wiring stays correct.\n- Outside an RLS transaction (SQLite, the local profile) nothing changes.\n\nPostgreSQL integration cases (NOSUPERUSER NOBYPASSRLS role, FORCEd tenant\npolicy on chat_messages) cover a reply delayed past the handler, client\ncancellation, a request rollback, a turn-transaction rollback and the\nin-request fallback; `test:postgres` runs them.\n\nRefs #3414\n\n* fix(chat): run a bound turn with the runtime''s effective scopes\n\n`runtime.runAsPrincipal` caps live permissions to the supplied scopes and\nhands its callback the bound principal, but the turn ignored it and was\nrebuilt from the request''s `principal.permissions`; `executeAsPrincipal`\nthen published that pre-bind set explicitly, bypassing live resolution, so\na permission revoked between the send and the bind was regained by tools.\n\nThe callback now receives the bound principal (`AssistantRouteBoundPrincipal`)\nand the rebuilt turn, and its tool permission context, use its effective\n`scopes`, kept within the cap the route supplied. Malformed scopes refuse\nthe turn.\n\nThe PostgreSQL fixture now resolves live permissions from real membership\nrows for the request and the bind, and its `runAsPrincipal` follows the\nruntime (cap only when scopes are given; the callback gets the effective\nset). New case: a snapshotted permission revoked before the turn binds is\nabsent from the tool''s run and its database session.\n\nRefs #3414\n\n* fix(chat): cap a bound turn to the request''s frozen permission set\n\n`resolveAssistantPrincipalFromLocals()` carries no permission snapshot, so\n`respondWithTurn()` omitted `scopes` and the runtime applied no cap: a turn\nbinding after the request committed got every permission live at bind time,\nincluding grants made after the send was accepted.\n\nThe route now freezes the request''s authority before the response returns\n(the principal''s snapshot, else the permissions the request''s RLS context\npublished; an empty set stays empty) and always passes it as `scopes`, so\nthe turn runs with (request snapshot ∩ live at bind).\n\nCases: a permission granted between the send and the bind is absent from\nthe tool''s run and database session, and an empty request set stays empty\nwhen a permission is granted during the handoff.\n\nRefs #3414\n\n* fix(chat): settle a send whose request commits after the turn start timed out\n\nWhen a streamed turn''s request transaction was still open after the 60 s\nstart wait, the turn reported an error and settled the send only if it had\nalready confirmed it, which happens after the wait. A request that committed\nlater left its user message unsettled while the client had an error.\n\nAfter reporting the timeout the route keeps watching the request''s\ntransaction (up to `abandonedTurnMs`): once it ends, a fresh principal\nlifetime records the send `failed` if it committed, and does nothing if it\nrolled back. The wait is configurable as `turnStartTimeoutMs`\n(`DEFAULT_ASSISTANT_TURN_START_TIMEOUT_MS`, 60 s).\n\nCases with a 50 ms start timeout: a request committing after it settles\n`failed` without calling the model; one rolling back after it stores and\nsettles nothing.\n\nRefs #3414\n\n* fix(cli): print smrt app token usage for --help before the implicit create\n\n--help was classified as an implicit create option and rejected as an\nunknown token option. Handle help, --help and -h first.\n\nRefs #3413","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwc2DCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAar8QADI4lQr3JXrVsj76DftAyxcU\nfu0jmQp116mSF2KgwokjIulW+W/W6g1uE/t9+gxtVBNoLpXXJCAMdnYJUY/30sP0\nRK32ZHpiZwWKpTJh3O/fauhtGyrVSXDj4iUNAkt99BmjL0P2CBbBiNiOyG7mnFMM\nz2bqzPn67Pq40TtEzA25L9Ze6NaSTskv63oryDNxQrBmYgqA1naU+TIyRxFnMokF\nETIIylP6JNV8bfvILA44hiVsfOUa+zcSzPp0LkvKmnhqVE8Fnpj6mGQAUp8xDIlD\nLpWcRfA7qDDioWlsjYyJ0SDvD8nPVwFBFcF5D6eTTqdWCcb90e2tOZ/QUnXxt+BC\nMiUV4R3UfIer/jaXzhSUWsUy3vcNJWhkR+lZBk7/hoqU7uDP1tMYKOeeJGoFWprC\n12BBoM9csbrXjzAnGMeG8SjGq81iczV/EJ5DxReh+MO1zBhclZvpyLJqMqnudFFl\nFNr24B/1UZU6wi7wDQcBwSEmzsi45GmLw7LLFr/b3klqn5ZVXXA0JUGbE5+kBvRh\nTXGwehZGwGFmVg6SmjPzqAIald76i1UTwLaTlopIxLr7VmsweDY+mWS9BDzunk/Z\nddByeHqoGqLjoiZYRPOBxdPW/FXOiMUn+b4TNQGUwh4FBQjy2+SutpCz+ILtpS2o\nqTTWh2/vlzY24H0DLQwT\n=1uXh\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-04T03:52:35Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"h