{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","id":41898282,"login":"github-actions[bot]","node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/happyvertical/smrt/commit/64b6065c10087664edc9fcbbe9ad5c91c1f4dae8","node_id":"C_kwDOQDruXtoAKDY0YjYwNjVjMTAwODc2NjRlZGM5ZmNiYmU5YWQ1YzkxYzFmNGRhZTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/happyvertical/smrt/commit/d25a8d4919513acbd4377cad82856d1b004a2a3e","sha":"d25a8d4919513acbd4377cad82856d1b004a2a3e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/commits/d25a8d4919513acbd4377cad82856d1b004a2a3e"}],"sha":"64b6065c10087664edc9fcbbe9ad5c91c1f4dae8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/commits/64b6065c10087664edc9fcbbe9ad5c91c1f4dae8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/590602?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/willgriffin","id":590602,"login":"willgriffin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU5MDYwMg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/commits/d25a8d4919513acbd4377cad82856d1b004a2a3e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T06:55:34Z","email":"willgriffin@gmail.com","name":"Will Griffin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T06:55:34Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(deps): clear the three high audit advisories blocking Required CI (#3417)\n\n* fix(deps): pin figlet to the patched 1.11.x line\n\nfiglet 1.11.0 (via crawlee''s @crawlee/cli/@crawlee/templates -> yargonaut)\nloops forever in textSync() with whitespaceBreak and a narrow width\n(GHSA-62ch-8vmq-8xm7, high). Add an advisory-range override to 1.11.4,\nwhich yargonaut''s `figlet: ^1.1.1` already admits, and regenerate the\nlockfile (only figlet moves).\n\nRefs #3396\n\n* chore(audit): baseline unpatched braces and http-cache-semantics advisories\n\nNeither advisory has a patched release to override to: braces 3.0.3 and\nhttp-cache-semantics 4.2.0 are both the npm latest and the top of their\naffected ranges, and their parents (micromatch/fast-glob, cacheable-request)\nare already at latest.\n\nEach GHSA gets a suppressed audit-policy.json record with the reachability\nevidence and a 30-day recheck:\n\n- GHSA-vfj7-8cjw-p6xm (braces): braces only parses glob patterns, and every\n  runtime fast-glob call in packages/*/src takes constants or local\n  build/CLI config; no network input reaches a pattern. Waits on\n  micromatch/braces#72.\n- GHSA-ch52-4w7c-c8xp (http-cache-semantics): the shared-cache flaw needs\n  got''s `cache` option, which neither crawlee nor got-scraping sets, and\n  content''s fetchDocument path uses spider''s undici DomAdapter, never\n  loading crawlee. Waits on kornelski/http-cache-semantics#58.\n\nRefs #3396\n\n* docs(standards): document audit-policy records for unpatched advisories\n\nThe S8 dependency-audit standard still described suppression as a PR-only\njustification with a protobufjs example that no longer applies. Point it at\nthe audit-policy.json record that `pnpm audit:policy` enforces, cover the\nno-patched-release case, and name the `audit:policy:drift` live check.\n\nRefs #3396\n\n* docs(standards): state what audit drift mode does and does not compare\n\nDrift compares live advisories with unsuppressed records only; suppressed\nGHSAs are removed from pnpm''s audit payload and are revisited through\ntheir recheckBy date. Addresses the Copilot review thread on PR #3417.\n\nRefs #3396","tree":{"sha":"e1e9b01a55f6b7a6ab3644611dac13619b17a958","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/git/trees/e1e9b01a55f6b7a6ab3644611dac13619b17a958"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/git/commits/d25a8d4919513acbd4377cad82856d1b004a2a3e","verification":{"payload":"tree e1e9b01a55f6b7a6ab3644611dac13619b17a958\nparent 1570fb020be850417ebcebad6f2f81f19406083b\nauthor Will Griffin <willgriffin@gmail.com> 1791010534 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791010534 +0000\n\nfix(deps): clear the three high audit advisories blocking Required CI (#3417)\n\n* fix(deps): pin figlet to the patched 1.11.x line\n\nfiglet 1.11.0 (via crawlee''s @crawlee/cli/@crawlee/templates -> yargonaut)\nloops forever in textSync() with whitespaceBreak and a narrow width\n(GHSA-62ch-8vmq-8xm7, high). Add an advisory-range override to 1.11.4,\nwhich yargonaut''s `figlet: ^1.1.1` already admits, and regenerate the\nlockfile (only figlet moves).\n\nRefs #3396\n\n* chore(audit): baseline unpatched braces and http-cache-semantics advisories\n\nNeither advisory has a patched release to override to: braces 3.0.3 and\nhttp-cache-semantics 4.2.0 are both the npm latest and the top of their\naffected ranges, and their parents (micromatch/fast-glob, cacheable-request)\nare already at latest.\n\nEach GHSA gets a suppressed audit-policy.json record with the reachability\nevidence and a 30-day recheck:\n\n- GHSA-vfj7-8cjw-p6xm (braces): braces only parses glob patterns, and every\n  runtime fast-glob call in packages/*/src takes constants or local\n  build/CLI config; no network input reaches a pattern. Waits on\n  micromatch/braces#72.\n- GHSA-ch52-4w7c-c8xp (http-cache-semantics): the shared-cache flaw needs\n  got''s `cache` option, which neither crawlee nor got-scraping sets, and\n  content''s fetchDocument path uses spider''s undici DomAdapter, never\n  loading crawlee. Waits on kornelski/http-cache-semantics#58.\n\nRefs #3396\n\n* docs(standards): document audit-policy records for unpatched advisories\n\nThe S8 dependency-audit standard still described suppression as a PR-only\njustification with a protobufjs example that no longer applies. Point it at\nthe audit-policy.json record that `pnpm audit:policy` enforces, cover the\nno-patched-release case, and name the `audit:policy:drift` live check.\n\nRefs #3396\n\n* docs(standards): state what audit drift mode does and does not compare\n\nDrift compares live advisories with unsuppressed records only; suppressed\nGHSAs are removed from pnpm''s audit payload and are revisited through\ntheir recheckBy date. Addresses the Copilot review thread on PR #3417.\n\nRefs #3396","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwKb1CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA/EIQAEEvWkWsxxmEM/9V24FGY/1u\nOjhgGwJvZc34cEGAvP