":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","id":41898282,"login":"github-actions[bot]","node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/happyvertical/smrt/commit/85801a661289ccf7e72ccceecebd52434ad08838","node_id":"C_kwDOQDruXtoAKDg1ODAxYTY2MTI4OWNjZjdlNzJjY2NlZWNlYmQ1MjQzNGFkMDg4Mzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/happyvertical/smrt/commit/34abb12b4805306a00e3b00727798dc1b62a0a6b","sha":"34abb12b4805306a00e3b00727798dc1b62a0a6b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/commits/34abb12b4805306a00e3b00727798dc1b62a0a6b"}],"sha":"85801a661289ccf7e72ccceecebd52434ad08838","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/commits/85801a661289ccf7e72ccceecebd52434ad08838"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/590602?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/willgriffin","id":590602,"login":"willgriffin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU5MDYwMg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/commits/34abb12b4805306a00e3b00727798dc1b62a0a6b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T09:57:11Z","email":"willgriffin@gmail.com","name":"Will Griffin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T09:57:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(timesheets): move the shared time entry into smrt-timesheets (#3348)\n\n* feat(timesheets): move shared time entries into smrt-timesheets\n\nAdd @happyvertical/smrt-timesheets (packages/timesheets) and move\nServiceTimeEntry, ServiceChargeSnapshot, ServiceCompensationSnapshot, their\ncollections, and ServiceEvidenceService out of smrt-projects. The base entry\nkeeps a generic work reference (workRefType/workRefId), a smrt-profiles\nparticipant, participantKind, source, period/duration, the status machine and\ncorrection chain, and no domain foreign key; caseId/specialistId live only on\nsmrt-support''s subtype, which now extends the timesheets entry directly and\nfreezes them on approval through the new frozenFieldNames() hook.\n\nTables, columns, indexes, and conflict keys are unchanged and carry no\ndiscriminator, so rows written before the move load through every package with\nno schema change. smrt-projects re-exports the moved classes (a projects\nsubclass would make a third same-named level on the table, which the\nmanifest-path single-family resolution cannot carry). The time-entry Svelte\ncomponents (TimeEntryList, TimeEntryCard, TimeSummary, DurationDisplay,\nTimeEntryApprovalQueue) move with their tests and stay re-exported from the\nprojects and support svelte subpaths; the approval queue''s strings now go\nthrough i18n and timesheets joins the strict hardcoded-string gate.\n\nCompatibility is proven against the pre-move schemas (fixtures extracted from\nthe 02590837 built manifests): rows load through each package, unmodelled\ncase columns survive saves, approved evidence stays frozen, and the CLI''s\nmanifest-path migration plan emits no DDL. A manifest-path test shows a\nconsumer subtype can require tenancy and close every generated surface.\n\nRefs #3288\n\n* docs(timesheets): point projects and support docs at smrt-timesheets\n\nRecord the #3288 ownership move in the projects and support guidance: the\nmoved classes are re-exports in projects, support subclasses the timesheets\nentry directly, the money PostgreSQL lane moved with the snapshots, and the\nService Time Entry migration note maps the old imports to the new package and\nstates that existing service_time_entries rows need no schema change.\n\nRefs #3288\n\n* chore(projects): regenerate the legacy source manifest\n\nsrc/manifest/manifest.json is the fallback manifest read when no build or\ndev artifact exists. Regenerate it from the current build (repo-relative\nfilePath, as in #2839) so it no longer declares the time-entry models that\nmoved to smrt-timesheets; a stale entry would register a second unrelated\nServiceTimeEntry on service_time_entries in an unbuilt workspace.\n\nRefs #3288\n\n* test(timesheets): pin the projects and support svelte re-exports\n\nAssert that the time-entry components and helpers moved in #3288 are the\nsame bindings when imported from @happyvertical/smrt-projects/svelte and\n@happyvertical/smrt-support/svelte.\n\nRefs #3288\n\n* chore(timesheets): align smrt-timesheets with the 0.52.0 release group\n\nRefs #3288\n\n* chore(timesheets): refresh the lockfile for the sdk 0.98.0 catalog\n\nRefs #3288\n\n* docs(timesheets): require a direct smrt-timesheets dependency under pnpm\n\nThe CLI manifest discovery reads only top-level node_modules packages, so a\npnpm consumer of smrt-projects or smrt-support without a direct\n@happyvertical/smrt-timesheets dependency stops planning\nservice_time_entries, service_charge_snapshots, and\nservice_compensation_snapshots (verified with smrt db:status against a\npnpm-style layout). State the requirement in the timesheets migration table,\nthe projects and support installation sections, and\nSERVICE_TIME_MIGRATION.md, which ships in the smrt-projects tarball.\n\nRefs #3288\n\n* test(timesheets): close the snapshot surfaces in the consumer contract\n\nExtend the consumer-closed surface contract from ServiceTimeEntry to\nServiceChargeSnapshot and ServiceCompensationSnapshot: the README shows the\nsame-named closed subclasses for all three tables, and the test asserts REST\nis disabled, no servicechargesnapshot_* / servicecompensationsnapshot_* MCP\ntools are generated, and tenancy is required for each. Document that the\nsnapshots keep their explicit time_entry_id conflict key when a consumer\nrequires tenancy; widening it is the consumer schema change, not a default.\n\nRefs #3288\n\n* feat(timesheets): keep the moved classes'' smrt-projects names resolving\n\nDeclare previousQualifiedNames (#3338) on ServiceTimeEntry,\nServiceChargeSnapshot, and ServiceCompensationSnapshot so references stored\nor declared under their pre-#3288 @happyvertical/smrt-projects:* names keep\nresolving to the smrt-timesheets classes: polymorphic associations hydrate,\n@crossPackageRef targets load, and new association writes store the current\nname. smrt-projects'' manifest (built and legacy source) does not list the\nclasses, so the aliases do not collide; its re-exports are constructors, not\ndefinitions.\n\nThe consumer-closed-surface test''s subclass manifest no longer copies the\nbase''s previousQualifiedNames, matching what the scanner emits for a\nsubclass; copying them would be a second claimant of the old names.\n\nThe regression test reproduces the F3 failure (hydrate() returned null for\nan association stored as @happyvertical/smrt-projects:ServiceTimeEntry) and\nfails without the aliases.\n\nRefs #3288\n\n* docs(timesheets): document the smrt-projects name aliases and their gap\n\nThe moved models'' old @happyvertical/smrt-projects:* names now resolve as\ndeprecated aliases, so the no-data-migration statement holds for stored\nreferences. Document it in the timesheets migration note, the projects and\nsupport READMEs, SERVICE_TIME_MIGRATION.md, and timesheets AGENTS: smrt\ndoctor --db counts remaining stored references, smrt db:migrate-qualified-names\nis the opt-in backfill, and source references should move to the new names\nbefore a later breaking release removes the aliases. Record the known gap:\na same-named subtype that replaces a moved class (smrt-support''s\nServiceTimeEntry, or a consumer''s closing subclass) drops that class''s alias,\nwith an interim workaround, and warn closing subclasses not to redeclare it.\n\nRefs #3288\n\n* fix(timesheets): refuse non-integer snapshot amounts at the model boundary\n\nServiceChargeSnapshot and ServiceCompensationSnapshot promise integer minor\nunits, but nothing enforced it: SQLite stored 19.99 in the INTEGER column and\nonly PostgreSQL rejected it, at the driver (22P02). Both models'' save() now\nthrows VALIDATION_INVALID_VALUE unless amount is a safe integer, so direct\ncollection writes and ServiceEvidenceService approvals behave the same on\nevery engine. Sign is not constrained.\n\nExisting writers already produce integers: SubscriptionServiceCommercialResolver\npasses through ClientCharge.amount, which CommercialUsageService rounds to a\nwhole minor unit; provider compensation comes from the application''s\nProviderCompensationResolver, whose fractional output is now refused instead\nof stored. Tests cover direct writes (19.99, NaN, Infinity, 2^53) and a\nfractional resolver on SQLite, and both snapshots on PostgreSQL.\n\nRefs #3288\n\n* docs(timesheets): describe how projects and support use the package accurately\n\nThe package documentation said smrt-projects and smrt-support both subclass\nthe models. smrt-projects only re-exports them, and smrt-support subclasses\nServiceTimeEntry alone; say so. No other doc made the claim.\n\nRefs #3288\n\n* docs(timesheets): name the replacing class for support apps'' references\n\nWith smrt-support installed, support''s ServiceTimeEntry subtype replaces the\ntimesheets entry in a built application, so\n@happyvertical/smrt-timesheets:ServiceTimeEntry is not registered: it does\nnot resolve, a @crossPackageRef to it fails to load, and an association\nstored under it hydrates to null (probe at e96344df3; support''s vitest\nenvironment keeps both classes and hides this). Tell support apps, and apps\nwith their own closing subclass, to reference the class they register, e.g.\n@happyvertical/smrt-support:ServiceTimeEntry, in the timesheets README and\nmigration table, the projects and support READMEs, SERVICE_TIME_MIGRATION.md,\nand timesheets AGENTS.\n\nRefs #3288","tree":{"sha":"a80b8f25283c4afd4a0d5ca9661fffb274886026","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/git/trees/a80b8f25283c4afd4a0d5ca9661fffb274886026"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/git/commits/34abb12b4805306a00e3b00727798dc1b62a0a6b","verification":{"payload":"tree a80b8f25283c4afd4a0d5ca9661fffb274886026\nparent 6c1d6f76affbdd8fb9055ce829d4c78486fcad29\nauthor Will Griffin <willgriffin@gmail.com> 1790935031 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790935031 +0000\n\nfeat(timesheets): move the shared time entry into smrt-timesheets (#3348)\n\n* feat(timesheets): move shared time entries into smrt-timesheets\n\nAdd @happyvertical/smrt-timesheets (packages/timesheets) and move\nServiceTimeEntry, ServiceChargeSnapshot, ServiceCompensationSnapshot, their\ncollections, and ServiceEvidenceService out of smrt-projects. The base entry\nkeeps a generic work reference (workRefType/workRefId), a smrt-profiles\nparticipant, participantKind, source, period/duration, the status machine and\ncorrection chain, and no domain foreign key; caseId/specialistId live only on\nsmrt-support''s subtype, which now extends the timesheets entry directly and\nfreezes them on approval through the new frozenFieldNames() hook.\n\nTables, columns, indexes, and conflict keys are unchanged and carry no\ndiscriminator, so rows written before the move load through every package with\nno schema change. smrt-projects re-exports the moved classes (a projects\nsubclass would make a third same-named level on the table, which the\nmanifest-path single-family resolution cannot carry). The time-entry Svelte\ncomponents (TimeEntryList, TimeEntryCard, TimeSummary, DurationDisplay,\nTimeEntryApprovalQueue) move with their tests and stay re-exported from the\nprojects and support svelte subpaths; the approval queue''s strings now go\nthrough i18n and timesheets joins the strict hardcoded-string gate.\n\nCompatibility is proven against the pre-move schemas (fixtures extracted from\nthe 02590837 built manifests): rows load through each package, unmodelled\ncase columns survive saves, approved evidence stays frozen, and the CLI''s\nmanifest-path migration plan emits no DDL. A manifest-path test shows a\nconsumer subtype can require tenancy and close every generated surface.\n\nRefs #3288\n\n* docs(timesheets): point projects and support docs at smrt-timesheets\n\nRecord the #3288 ownership move in the projects and support guidance: the\nmoved classes are re-exports in projects, support subclasses the timesheets\nentry directly, the money PostgreSQL lane moved with the snapshots, and the\nService Time Entry migration note maps the old imports to the new package and\nstates that existing service_time_entries rows need no schema change.\n\nRefs #3288\n\n* chore(projects): regenerate the legacy source manifest\n\nsrc/manifest/manifest.json is the fallback manifest read when no build or\ndev artifact exists. Regenerate it from the current build (repo-relative\nfilePath, as in #2839) so it no longer declares the time-entry models that\nmoved to smrt-timesheets; a stale entry would register a second unrelated\nServiceTimeEntry on service_time_entries in an unbuilt workspace.\n\nRefs #3288\n\n* test(timesheets): pin the projects and support svelte re-exports\n\nAssert that the time-entry components and helpers moved in #3288 are the\nsame bindings when imported from @happyvertical/smrt-projects/svelte and\n@happyvertical/smrt-support/svelte.\n\nRefs #3288\n\n* chore(timesheets): align smrt-timesheets with the 0.52.0 release group\n\nRefs #3288\n\n* chore(timesheets): refresh the lockfile for the sdk 0.98.0 catalog\n\nRefs #3288\n\n* docs(timesheets): require a direct smrt-timesheets dependency under pnpm\n\nThe CLI manifest discovery reads only top-level node_modules packages, so a\npnpm consumer of smrt-projects or smrt-support without a direct\n@happyvertical/smrt-timesheets dependency stops planning\nservice_time_entries, service_charge_snapshots, and\nservice_compensation_snapshots (verified with smrt db:status against a\npnpm-style layout). State the requirement in the timesheets migration table,\nthe projects and support installation sections, and\nSERVICE_TIME_MIGRATION.md, which ships in the smrt-projects tarball.\n\nRefs #3288\n\n* test(timesheets): close the snapshot surfaces in the consumer contract\n\nExtend the consumer-closed surface contract from ServiceTimeEntry to\nServiceChargeSnapshot and ServiceCompensationSnapshot: the README shows the\nsame-named closed subclasses for all three tables, and the test asserts REST\nis disabled, no servicechargesnapshot_* / servicecompensationsnapshot_* MCP\ntools are generated, and tenancy is required for each. Document that the\nsnapshots keep their explicit time_entry_id conflict key when a consumer\nrequires tenancy; widening it is the consumer schema change, not a default.\n\nRefs #3288\n\n* feat(timesheets): keep the moved classes'' smrt-projects names resolving\n\nDeclare previousQualifiedNames (#3338) on ServiceTimeEntry,\nServiceChargeSnapshot, and ServiceCompensationSnapshot so references stored\nor declared under their pre-#3288 @happyvertical/smrt-projects:* names keep\nresolving to the smrt-timesheets classes: polymorphic associations hydrate,\n@crossPackageRef targets load, and new association writes store the current\nname. smrt-projects'' manifest (built and legacy source) does not list the\nclasses, so the aliases do not collide; its re-exports are constructors, not\ndefinitions.\n\nThe consumer-closed-surface test''s subclass manifest no longer copies the\nbase''s previousQualifiedNames, matching what the scanner emits for a\nsubclass; copying them would be a second claimant of the old names.\n\nThe regression test reproduces the F3 failure (hydrate() returned null for\nan association stored as @happyvertical/smrt-projects:ServiceTimeEntry) and\nfails without the aliases.\n\nRefs #3288\n\n* docs(timesheets): document the smrt-projects name aliases and their gap\n\nThe moved models'' old @happyvertical/smrt-projects:* names now resolve as\ndeprecated aliases, so the no-data-migration statement holds for stored\nreferences. Document it in the timesheets migration note, the projects and\nsupport READMEs, SERVICE_TIME_MIGRATION.md, and timesheets AGENTS: smrt\ndoctor --db counts remaining stored references, smrt db:migrate-qualified-names\nis the opt-in backfill, and source references should move to the new names\nbefore a later breaking release removes the aliases. Record the known gap:\na same-named subtype that replaces a moved class (smrt-support''s\nServiceTimeEntry, or a consumer''s closing subclass) drops that class''s alias,\nwith an interim workaround, and warn closing subclasses not to redeclare it.\n\nRefs #3288\n\n* fix(timesheets): refuse non-integer snapshot amounts at the model boundary\n\nServiceChargeSnapshot and ServiceCompensationSnapshot promise integer minor\nunits, but nothing enforced it: SQLite stored 19.99 in the INTEGER column and\nonly PostgreSQL rejected it, at the driver (22P02). Both models'' save() now\nthrows VALIDATION_INVALID_VALUE unless amount is a safe integer, so direct\ncollection writes and ServiceEvidenceService approvals behave the same on\nevery engine. Sign is not constrained.\n\nExisting writers already produce integers: SubscriptionServiceCommercialResolver\npasses through ClientCharge.amount, which CommercialUsageService rounds to a\nwhole minor unit; provider compensation comes from the application''s\nProviderCompensationResolver, whose fractional output is now refused instead\nof stored. Tests cover direct writes (19.99, NaN, Infinity, 2^53) and a\nfractional resolver on SQLite, and both snapshots on PostgreSQL.\n\nRefs #3288\n\n* docs(timesheets): describe how projects and support use the package accurately\n\nThe package documentation said smrt-projects and smrt-support both subclass\nthe models. smrt-projects only re-exports them, and smrt-support subclasses\nServiceTimeEntry alone; say so. No other doc made the claim.\n\nRefs #3288\n\n* docs(timesheets): name the replacing class for support apps'' references\n\nWith smrt-support installed, support''s ServiceTimeEntry subtype replaces the\ntimesheets entry in a built application, so\n@happyvertical/smrt-timesheets:ServiceTimeEntry is not registered: it does\nnot resolve, a @crossPackageRef to it fails to load, and an association\nstored under it hydrates to null (probe at e96344df3; support''s vitest\nenvironment keeps both classes and hides this). Tell support apps, and apps\nwith their own closing subclass, to reference the class they register, e.g.\n@happyvertical/smrt-support:ServiceTimeEntry, in the timesheets README and\nmigration table, the projects and support READMEs, SERVICE_TIME_MIGRATION.md,\nand timesheets AGENTS.\n\nRefs #3288","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqv4AHCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA35IQAA/BTxYZ4NrlDZJ3SJ83252s\nIX5O5XJ1raqhYMjkKJRRPXp22UMDc5H4LGe2PhiU2OFqfJ27doGzoLXZyiV7Thub\nqWAvwv9THbR8VftzKwhAQbLA4Ql9LLIp+frVAk4q4gbEJzxgTz09FhiGSaFe+jVy\nU3VwOtbYURyCM+fVsWXPg6nbVLJDUiIwrdBAN/AQt5oAu0g/7eceI+Py72UTTjN1\nRoz+F/oLIH4i6l+YtNJRR545dERq2Ph/4YFFMQ8K3h7IldOgy+LpnvB1GMnhXSIs\nVv6Izo7TNy6sKLguSjB+DaSmPbTwyVwnu4d6r/42UBzXZVcErJs7fD28OuAZkD25\n3YW2Z9zan5FzXKui8+gZFIY/AQ7AgRCHzVGwMiOcwqpRsG0Kx9Fg1Jwok1GMUvNR\nWmfjOe1/If3iJZVTbQLcCk99tloIle8z+0hZ0AE58xVhQWhHYXE0ZxBsSrvtM5gs\nttGXEZE9jrgnjnzZxgPe6551iju5aKPVljCMIfisLUOqZN/ndHp7OKz7M4xB2kI0\neqxYnZFJNmU6BOe4QWDRMt+FpznbvUFt6HktaaZQTwvZ5HvlE7oysapzDEV1CyCl\n8u/2afcj4gU0/FT0ibnPyS3cvkT4T0YE4F1h9LJZUexX5rQNw+fmLtot6wscc0jx\nG9x5EtqUAeUh9mKTVS/a\n=FgHD\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-02T09:57:27Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/happyvertical/smrt/commit/34abb12b4805306a00e3b00727798dc1b62a0a6b","node_id":"C_kwDOQDruXtoAKDM0YWJiMTJiNDgwNTMwNmEwMGUzYjAwNzI3Nzk4ZGMxYjYyYTBhNmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/happyvertical/smrt/commit/6c1d6f76affbdd8fb9055ce829d4c78486fcad29","sha":"6c1d6f76affbdd8fb9055ce829d4c78486fcad29","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/commits/6c1d6f76affbdd8fb9055ce829d4c78486fcad29"}],"sha":"34abb12b4805306a00e3b00727798dc1b62a0a6b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/commits/34abb12b4805306a00e3b00727798dc1b62a0a6b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/590602?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/willgriffin","id":590602,"login":"willgriffin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU5MDYwMg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/commits/6c1d6f76affbdd8fb9055ce829d4c78486fcad29/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T08:45:01Z","email":"willgriffin@gmail.com","name":"Will Griffin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T08:45:01Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(core): deprecated qualified-name aliases so moved models keep resolving (#3341)\n\n* feat(core): resolve deprecated qualified-name aliases for moved models\n\nAdd `@smrt({ previousQualifiedNames })`. A class that moved package keeps\nresolving under its old qualified name through a derived per-generation\nalias index. Qualified lookups, polymorphic hydration, relationship and\n`@crossPackageRef` targets, delete cascades and playbook preflight all\nconsult it. The lazy loader resolves an old package identity through the\nnew owner''s manifest when the old manifest no longer lists the class.\n\nAliases never become registry keys, so tables, tools, routes and\niterations still see one class. Registration and manifest generation\nrefuse an alias that names a live class or is claimed twice. The first\nresolution of each old name logs a deprecation warning, and polymorphic\nsaves store the current name. The knowledge artifact and graph carry the\nnames.\n\nRefs #3338\n\n* feat(core): count and backfill stored deprecated qualified names\n\n`countLegacyQualifiedNameReferences()` reports polymorphic `meta_type` and\nSTI `_meta_type` rows that still store an old qualified name. Doctor\nuses it. `backfillLegacyQualifiedNames()` is the opt-in, idempotent\nrewrite. It runs in one transaction, can be scoped to one tenant, and\nskips rows whose rewrite would duplicate a current-name row. Once nothing\nin scope remains it records a `_smrt_backfills` marker for the alias set.\n\nSQLite and PostgreSQL suites cover hydration under an old metaType,\ncurrent-name writes, cascades, counts and the backfill.\n\nRefs #3338\n\n* feat(assets): match moved owners'' old and current metaType\n\n`byLeft()`, `detach()` and `setLinks()` filter on every equivalent\nqualified name of the owner class. Associations written before and after\na model move therefore both match, while new rows store the current name.\n\nRefs #3338\n\n* feat(cli): report deprecated qualified names and add their backfill\n\n`smrt doctor --db` gains a \"Deprecated Qualified Names\" section. It lists\ndeclared aliases and counts the stored rows that still use them, warning\nwhile any remain. `smrt db:migrate-qualified-names [--dry-run] [--tenant]\n[--force]` runs the opt-in core backfill.\n\nRefs #3338\n\n* docs(core): document moving a model between packages\n\nCover declaring previousQualifiedNames, resolution and its limits, the\ncollision rules, the doctor count, the opt-in backfill, and the alias\nlifecycle that ends in a breaking removal.\n\nRefs #3338\n\n* fix(core): resolve unregistered owners before normalizing or filtering metaType\n\nPolymorphic saves and AssetAssociationCollection owner filters used the\nsync alias lookups, which only see registered classes. With the moved\nclass known only from its installed manifest, a write by the old name\nstored the old name. byLeft/detach/setLinks also missed legacy rows, so\nsetLinks left them behind.\n\nAdd ObjectRegistry.resolveQualifiedNameAsync() and\ngetEquivalentQualifiedNamesAsync(). On a qualified miss they lazily load\nthe class from its manifest first. Use them at both call sites. A\ngenuinely unknown name is still stored as given.\n\nRefs #3338\n\n* fix(core): refuse a lazily resolved alias claimed by two manifests\n\nThe lazy alias search returned the first manifest that declared an old\nname. When two installed or cached owners claimed it and neither was\nregistered, it silently picked one. It now collects every claimant across\nloaded and discoverable manifests, and throws\nCONFIG_QUALIFIED_NAME_ALIAS_COLLISION when more than one distinct owner\nclaims the name, matching the eager registration rule.\n\nRefs #3338\n\n* fix(core): validate alias updates before mutating a live registration\n\nA same-key re-registration of an existing constructor validated aliases\nonly when the key was promoted. It could add a malformed alias, a live\nclass''s name, or another class''s alias unchecked. The manifest merge path\nchecked only after mergeManifestIntoExistingRegistration had already\nrewritten the entry.\n\nBoth paths now validate the proposed entry first, treating the live entry\nit replaces as itself. A refused update leaves the registration\nunchanged.\n\nRefs #3338\n\n* fix(core): refuse unscoped previousQualifiedNames entries\n\nAlias validation accepted an unscoped `package:Class`. Every qualified\nlookup that would resolve it uses the scoped-only isQualifiedName():\nfindClass, findClassStrict, resolveType and the lazy loader. Such an\nalias could never resolve. That predicate is how this repo defines a\nqualified name, so validation now uses it too. Registration and manifest\ngeneration refuse unscoped aliases as CONFIG_QUALIFIED_NAME_ALIAS_INVALID.\n\nRefs #3338\n\n* fix(core): check manifest alias claims before any lazy registration\n\nFix 2 refused competing manifest claims only when the old name was looked\nup first. Loading the current name first, through\nresolveQualifiedNameAsync, ensureManifestLoaded or\ntryLoadFromExternalPackage, registered that owner without consulting\ncompeting manifests. The later old-name lookup then returned it through\nthe sync fast path.\n\nAlias registration now enforces one manifest-claim rule. A class declaring\npreviousQualifiedNames is refused with\nCONFIG_QUALIFIED_NAME_ALIAS_COLLISION when any loaded manifest''s class\nalso claims one of its old names. This covers eager registrations too.\nBefore a lazy load publishes a manifest that declares aliases, it loads\nevery discoverable manifest into the cache, so the rule sees all installed\nclaimants whichever name was requested. The old-name lookup reuses the\nsame inventory. The inventory is cached per registry generation and\nreplaces the previous miss memo, and manifests without aliases skip the\nscan.\n\nRefs #3338\n\n* fix(core): refuse a colon in a previousQualifiedNames package part\n\n`@scope/pkg:legacy:Moved` passed isQualifiedName(), which splits at the\nlast colon, so it passed alias validation as package `@scope/pkg:legacy`,\na package the lazy loader cannot resolve. Alias validation, used at\nregistration and at manifest generation, now requires exactly one colon.\nThe shared isQualifiedName() is unchanged for other callers.\n\nRefs #3338\n\n* fix(scanner): fail the knowledge graph on duplicate alias claimants\n\nWhen two artifacts'' objects claimed the same previousQualifiedNames\nentry, the graph silently mapped it to whichever object sorted first, so\na cross-package edge by the old name could target the wrong moved object.\nAlias ownership is now tracked per old name. Graph generation throws a\nclear error naming every distinct owner. The same object repeated across\nartifacts, such as a package artifact plus a consumer aggregate, still\ncounts as one claim.\n\nRefs #3338\n\n* fix(cli): never call aliases removable from a partial legacy-name count\n\nA tenant-scoped db:migrate-qualified-names count, or one that skipped\nuntenanted tables, reported \"these aliases can be removed\" whenever its\ntotal was zero. A zero now reads as a removal signal only for a global,\ncomplete count. Tenant-scoped output says it is not one and points to an\nunscoped run. Skipped tables are listed. Every report also reminds the\noperator that source still naming an old qualified name\n(@crossPackageRef / relationship targets, playbook step models) must be\nupdated before removal. smrt doctor --db semantics are otherwise\nunchanged.\n\nRefs #3338\n\n* fix(core): refuse an alias that a stale installed manifest still defines\n\nThe manifest inventory indexed only alias claims. Suppose a stale old\npackage manifest still defined OLD as a class and the successor declared\npreviousQualifiedNames: [OLD]. Lazily loading the successor''s current\nname then registered it, and later OLD lookups selected the successor,\nalthough OLD is a live class name.\n\nThe per-generation inventory now also indexes every qualified name a\nloaded or discoverable manifest defines. The one manifest rule,\nassertNoCompetingManifestClaims, refuses a declared old name defined as a\nclass by any manifest, even an unregistered one, with\nCONFIG_QUALIFIED_NAME_ALIAS_COLLISION before publishing. The legitimate\nmove, where the old manifest no longer lists the class, still resolves.\nA re-exported constructor is not a manifest definition.\n\nRefs #3338","tree":{"sha":"561503f373fc0d434b13e74361e3a974969144c5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/git/trees/561503f373fc0d434b13e74361e3a974969144c5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/git/commits/6c1d6f76affbdd8fb9055ce829d4c78486fcad29","verification":{"payload":"tree 561503f373fc0d434b13e74361e3a974969144c5\nparent d54f3970e2ec510f8d3fb9b31d95677a1178995c\nauthor Will Griffin <willgriffin@gmail.com> 1790930701 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790930701 +0000\n\nfeat(core): deprecated qualified-name aliases so moved models keep resolving (#3341)\n\n* feat(core): resolve deprecated qualified-name aliases for moved models\n\nAdd `@smrt({ previousQualifiedNames })`. A class that moved package keeps\nresolving under its old qualified name through a derived per-generation\nalias index. Qualified lookups, polymorphic hydration, relationship and\n`@crossPackageRef` targets, delete cascades and playbook preflight all\nconsult it. The lazy loader resolves an old package identity through the\nnew owner''s manifest when the old manifest no longer lists the class.\n\nAliases never become registry keys, so tables, tools, routes and\niterations still see one class. Registration and manifest generation\nrefuse an alias that names a live class or is claimed twice. The first\nresolution of each old name logs a deprecation warning, and polymorphic\nsaves store the current name. The knowledge artifact and graph carry the\nnames.\n\nRefs #3338\n\n* feat(core): count and backfill stored deprecated qualified names\n\n`countLegacyQualifiedNameReferences()` reports polymorphic `meta_type` and\nSTI `_meta_type` rows that still store an old qualified name. Doctor\nuses it. `backfillLegacyQualifiedNames()` is the opt-in, idempotent\nrewrite. It runs in one transaction, can be scoped to one tenant, and\nskips rows whose rewrite would duplicate a current-name row. Once nothing\nin scope remains it records a `_smrt_backfills` marker for the alias set.\n\nSQLite and PostgreSQL suites cover hydration under an old metaType,\ncurrent-name writes, cascades, counts and the backfill.\n\nRefs #3338\n\n* feat(assets): match moved owners'' old and current metaType\n\n`byLeft()`, `detach()` and `setLinks()` filter on every equivalent\nqualified name of the owner class. Associations written before and after\na model move therefore both match, while new rows store the current name.\n\nRefs #3338\n\n* feat(cli): report deprecated qualified names and add their backfill\n\n`smrt doctor --db` gains a \"Deprecated Qualified Names\" section. It lists\ndeclared aliases and counts the stored rows that still use them, warning\nwhile any remain. `smrt db:migrate-qualified-names [--dry-run] [--tenant]\n[--force]` runs the opt-in core backfill.\n\nRefs #3338\n\n* docs(core): document moving a model between packages\n\nCover declaring previousQualifiedNames, resolution and its limits, the\ncollision rules, the doctor count, the opt-in backfill, and the alias\nlifecycle that ends in a breaking removal.\n\nRefs #3338\n\n* fix(core): resolve unregistered owners before normalizing or filtering metaType\n\nPolymorphic saves and AssetAssociationCollection owner filters used the\nsync alias lookups, which only see registered classes. With the moved\nclass known only from its installed manifest, a write by the old name\nstored the old name. byLeft/detach/setLinks also missed legacy rows, so\nsetLinks left them behind.\n\nAdd ObjectRegistry.resolveQualifiedNameAsync() and\ngetEquivalentQualifiedNamesAsync(). On a qualified miss they lazily load\nthe class from its manifest first. Use them at both call sites. A\ngenuinely unknown name is still stored as given.\n\nRefs #3338\n\n* fix(core): refuse a lazily resolved alias claimed by two manifests\n\nThe lazy alias search returned the first manifest that declared an old\nname. When two installed or cached owners claimed it and neither was\nregistered, it silently picked one. It now collects every claimant across\nloaded and discoverable manifests, and throws\nCONFIG_QUALIFIED_NAME_ALIAS_COLLISION when more than one distinct owner\nclaims the name, matching the eager registration rule.\n\nRefs #3338\n\n* fix(core): validate alias updates before mutating a live registration\n\nA same-key re-registration of an existing constructor validated aliases\nonly when the key was promoted. It could add a malformed alias, a live\nclass''s name, or another class''s alias unchecked. The manifest merge path\nchecked only after mergeManifestIntoExistingRegistration had already\nrewritten the entry.\n\nBoth paths now validate the proposed entry first, treating the live entry\nit replaces as itself. A refused update leaves the registration\nunchanged.\n\nRefs #3338\n\n* fix(core): refuse unscoped previousQualifiedNames entries\n\nAlias validation accepted an unscoped `package:Class`. Every qualified\nlookup that would resolve it uses the scoped-only isQualifiedName():\nfindClass, findClassStrict, resolveType and the lazy loader. Such an\nalias could never resolve. That predicate is how this repo defines a\nqualified name, so validation now uses it too. Registration and manifest\ngeneration refuse unscoped aliases as CONFIG_QUALIFIED_NAME_ALIAS_INVALID.\n\nRefs #3338\n\n* fix(core): check manifest alias claims before any lazy registration\n\nFix 2 refused competing manifest claims only when the old name was looked\nup first. Loading the current name first, through\nresolveQualifiedNameAsync, ensureManifestLoaded or\ntryLoadFromExternalPackage, registered that owner without consulting\ncompeting manifests. The later old-name lookup then returned it through\nthe sync fast path.\n\nAlias registration now enforces one manifest-claim rule. A class declaring\npreviousQualifiedNames is refused with\nCONFIG_QUALIFIED_NAME_ALIAS_COLLISION when any loaded manifest''s class\nalso claims one of its old names. This covers eager registrations too.\nBefore a lazy load publishes a manifest that declares aliases, it loads\nevery discoverable manifest into the cache, so the rule sees all installed\nclaimants whichever name was requested. The old-name lookup reuses the\nsame inventory. The inventory is cached per registry generation and\nreplaces the previous miss memo, and manifests without aliases skip the\nscan.\n\nRefs #3338\n\n* fix(core): refuse a colon in a previousQualifiedNames package part\n\n`@scope/pkg:legacy:Moved` passed isQualifiedName(), which splits at the\nlast colon, so it passed alias validation as package `@scope/pkg:legacy`,\na package the lazy loader cannot resolve. Alias validation, used at\nregistration and at manifest generation, now requires exactly one colon.\nThe shared isQualifiedName() is unchanged for other callers.\n\nRefs #3338\n\n* fix(scanner): fail the knowledge graph on duplicate alias claimants\n\nWhen two artifacts'' objects claimed the same previousQualifiedNames\nentry, the graph silently mapped it to whichever object sorted first, so\na cross-package edge by the old name could target the wrong moved object.\nAlias ownership is now tracked per old name. Graph generation throws a\nclear error naming every distinct owner. The same object repeated across\nartifacts, such as a package artifact plus a consumer aggregate, still\ncounts as one claim.\n\nRefs #3338\n\n* fix(cli): never call aliases removable from a partial legacy-name count\n\nA tenant-scoped db:migrate-qualified-names count, or one that skipped\nuntenanted tables, reported \"these aliases can be removed\" whenever its\ntotal was zero. A zero now reads as a removal signal only for a global,\ncomplete count. Tenant-scoped output says it is not one and points to an\nunscoped run. Skipped tables are listed. Every report also reminds the\noperator that source still naming an old qualified name\n(@crossPackageRef / relationship targets, playbook step models) must be\nupdated before removal. smrt doctor --db semantics are otherwise\nunchanged.\n\nRefs #3338\n\n* fix(core): refuse an alias that a stale installed manifest still defines\n\nThe manifest inventory indexed only alias claims. Suppose a stale old\npackage manifest still defined OLD as a class and the successor declared\npreviousQualifiedNames: [OLD]. Lazily loading the successor''s current\nname then registered it, and later OLD lookups selected the successor,\nalthough OLD is a live class name.\n\nThe per-generation inventory now also indexes every qualified name a\nloaded or discoverable manifest defines. The one manifest rule,\nassertNoCompetingManifestClaims, refuses a declared old name defined as a\nclass by any manifest, even an unregistered one, with\nCONFIG_QUALIFIED_NAME_ALIAS_COLLISION before publishing. The legitimate\nmove, where the old manifest no longer lists the class, still resolves.\nA re-exported constructor is not a manifest definition.\n\nRefs #3338","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqv28dCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAwzMQAHN1ZpU0lV1I1//WojWMzfRa\nl8LO4GB+C/ZfB/K39gjhUZ6yiU/6trts3Xx3uG+TKb4TtddnUag5d8DXvphAaQx5\nZwe3AH0IlSoIvFcqx5hx95BjV+plrg9Ehw5ihNWN+wOWvFEwf5gOoavY8xXvmebZ\n0a/pSDkNkQbCoJRkiot73gq73nTMJI6b0voOikm+AA74Ol6JvOB5YlMAU+2SaVre\nOV4qYM7b9DG5KV7X2dVnrUBMcD+rXjowZhe4OekJz7y9St9o4WCP9vrB1KRAX8hM\nSrFmok2tIUXc7W5UhbGJZmN5TSeZDJTKxv3YoYxyzsNJL1MKEKjKbm1HpjPz049V\nCSkUUV44a4mxkAp+CAyEV6sSlEyDdPQT+xm+OqM3t4X8EWRd06GXayxb4id2ETt3\nedh2C7EwwK1lBPIuLIthEdIJhjoL0s8lraDIr/L7xhK63DYhjkyJKQRDLLkjaHS4\n0L0n4biFZCm2QTfHd4feO1LrvH5KRxXks7rD45oftqa3UP7C1IYiCLP2fhFt5iSg\nODBFMgDio6YAFl1T617YJDPfFKXLhD7v2fpPTpTW1kISMy+T3Qh6V6QBNu+5qWxo\n9ksG9+D7Oj8zhi1heN/NuU+DsLBr7UKTTURBFUlBaiZO5z2DbwqkbyesM4NSV4pD\ni27UHCdjDMjxQj20ww/I\n=V1JM\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-02T08:45:17Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/happyvertical/smrt/commit/6c1d6f76affbdd8fb9055ce829d4c78486fcad29","node_id":"C_kwDOQDruXtoAKDZjMWQ2Zjc2YWZmYmRkOGZiOTA1NWNlODI5ZDRjNzg0ODZmY2FkMjk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/happyvertical/smrt/commit/d54f3970e2ec510f8d3fb9b31d95677a1178995c","sha":"d54f3970e2ec510f8d3fb9b31d95677a1178995c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/commits/d54f3970e2ec510f8d3fb9b31d95677a1178995c"}],"sha":"6c1d6f76affbdd8fb9055ce829d4c78486fcad29","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/commits/6c1d6f76affbdd8fb9055ce829d4c78486fcad29"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/590602?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/willgriffin","id":590602,"login":"willgriffin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU5MDYwMg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/willgriffin","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/commits/d54f3970e2ec510f8d3fb9b31d95677a1178995c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T07:30:44Z","email":"willgriffin@gmail.com","name":"Will Griffin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T07:30:44Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(expenses): reviewed expense and deduplicated receipt models in smrt-expenses (#3339)\n\n* feat(expenses): add expense and receipt models in smrt-expenses\n\nNew workspace package @happyvertical/smrt-expenses for a cost someone\nincurred and the paper that proves it.\n\n- Expense: polymorphic cost object (qualified type + id, one per\n  expense), category, integer minor-unit amount with ISO currency,\n  incurredOn date apart from recordedAt, recorded-by and paid-by\n  profiles (company or a named person out of pocket), optional commerce\n  vendor and commitment (PurchaseOrder contract or one of its lines),\n  reimbursement recording, and a review state changed only by\n  review()/reject()/markDuplicate()/reopen(). A plain write to review\n  fields is refused on save; a reviewed expense''s money is frozen until\n  reopen().\n- ExpenseReceipt: expense-owned join to a smrt-assets Asset with\n  uploader, filename, MIME type, byte count and contentSha256. The same\n  file twice on one expense is refused (pre-insert check plus a unique\n  index on tenant, expense and hash, surfaced as DuplicateReceiptError);\n  the same file on two expenses is reported by findDuplicateReceipts().\n- ExpenseCollection.commitmentPosition(): reviewed, non-duplicate\n  actuals in the commitment''s currency reduce what remains open, each\n  once. totalsByCurrency() never sums across currencies; a commitment\n  match in another currency is refused.\n- Models and collections close their generated API, MCP and CLI\n  surface; consumers can require tenancy with a qualified\n  registerTenantScopedClass().\n\nThe behaviour suite runs on SQLite and, through test:postgres, against\na PostgreSQL schema created by migrateSmrtSchemas with live parity.\n\nRefs #3289\n\n* chore(expenses): register smrt-expenses in the release group and catalogs\n\nAdd the package to the changesets fixed group, the root README package\ncatalog, the CONTEXT-MAP business row, and the Biome noExplicitAny\nstrict list.\n\nRefs #3289\n\n* fix(expenses): check a commitment match only when it is made or changed\n\nValidating the commitment on every save meant a later edit to the\npurchase order (a currency change, a deletion) blocked unrelated saves\nof an already-matched expense, including recording its reimbursement.\nThe match, line and currency are now checked when set or changed; rows a\nlater commitment change leaves in another currency are reported in\notherCurrencies and never drawn.\n\nRefs #3289\n\n* chore(expenses): align smrt-expenses with the 0.52.0 release group\n\nEvery publishable smrt package carries the fixed group''s version; main\nreleased 0.52.0 while this branch was open.\n\nRefs #3289\n\n* fix(expenses): pin expense and receipt saves to the row their guards checked\n\nThe review lock and receipt immutability read the row stored under the\nobject''s id, but core''s natural-key save adopts any same-owner row on\n(tenant_id, slug, context). Both models derive their slug from the id,\nso create({ slug: <reviewed expense id>, amount }) found nothing by id,\npassed every guard, then upserted onto the reviewed expense: back to\nunreviewed with new money. The same overwrote a receipt''s hash.\n\nA new row''s first save is now a plain INSERT (requireInsertOnSave), so\na natural-key collision raises EXPENSE_IDENTITY_CONFLICT instead of\nadopting, and an existing row refuses a changed slug or context. A\nrefused receipt INSERT is re-read to report a racing duplicate file as\nDuplicateReceiptError and anything else as an identity conflict.\n\nRefs #3289\n\n* fix(expenses): refuse a vendor from another tenant\n\nvendorId is a crossPackageRef, which neither validates its target nor\ncreates a foreign key, so an expense in tenant A could name tenant B''s\nvendor. The vendor is now resolved through the commerce collection (so\ntenant interceptors apply) and must belong to the expense''s tenant\nwhenever it is set or changed, like the commitment check; otherwise\nEXPENSE_VENDOR_MISMATCH.\n\nRefs #3289\n\n* fix(expenses): enforce one copy of a receipt file per expense for every tenant\n\nThe unique index led with the nullable tenant_id, and NULLs are distinct\nin a unique index on PostgreSQL and SQLite, so two concurrent attaches of\nthe same file to a global (NULL-tenant) expense both committed. The key\nis now (expense_id, content_sha256): an expense belongs to exactly one\ntenant, so it is already tenant-scoped, and it holds for NULL tenants.\nCreated by smrt db:migrate; live parity stays clean.\n\nRefs #3289\n\n* fix(expenses): refuse inherited junction writers that would lose receipt evidence\n\nExpenseReceiptCollection inherited SmrtJunction.setLinks(), which deletes\nevery receipt of the expense and then re-attaches through attach() with\nno content hash; each attach failed EXPENSE_RECEIPT_INVALID after the\nevidence was already gone. attach() and setLinks() now throw before\ntouching anything and point to attachReceipt(). detach() stays: removing\na link is an explicit act and keeps the asset. The batch junction path\ncannot bypass save(): ExpenseReceipt overrides it, so\nhasBaseJunctionLifecycle() is false, which the test asserts.\n\nRefs #3289\n\n* fix(expenses): bind review transitions to their complete resulting state\n\nThe transition token authorized every review-field change once the\nstatus endpoints matched, so a caller could set duplicateOfId directly\nand then call review() or reject(): the marker was persisted without\nmarkDuplicate()''s same-tenant check, and review() could even store a\nreviewed duplicate. review() and reject() now clear duplicateOfId, every\ntransition assigns every review field, and the token carries that whole\nstate; save() refuses any review field that differs from it. A reviewed\nexpense with a duplicate marker is refused outright.\n\nRefs #3289\n\n* fix(expenses): keep a receipt''s tenant immutable after insert\n\nExisting receipts skip the link-target checks, so a save without tenant\ncontext (optional tenancy lets it through) could change a receipt''s\ntenantId while expenseId still pointed at the original tenant''s expense,\nbreaking receipt isolation. The tenant, derived from the expense on\ninsert, is now one of the receipt''s immutable columns.\n\nRefs #3289\n\n* fix(expenses): limit duplicate receipt groups after filtering, not before\n\nWith expenseId, findDuplicateReceipts() sliced the expense''s own hashes\nto the limit before grouping, and those include its unique receipts, so\nan expense with many older unique receipts hid a later shared one (100\nunique plus one shared returned nothing at the default limit). The\ntargeted path now groups every hash and limits the groups; only the\nfacet path, whose hashes are already shared, is limited up front.\n\nRefs #3289\n\n* fix(expenses): freeze recordedAt on a reviewed expense\n\nThe README promises a reviewed expense''s dates stay frozen until\nreopen(), but recordedAt was not in the reviewed-field lock, so it could\nbe rewritten on a reviewed expense. It is now locked and compared as an\ninstant, because drivers return the stored value as a Date or a string.\n\nRefs #3289\n\n* fix(expenses): classify a refused receipt insert from the error itself\n\nA refused receipt INSERT was told apart by re-reading for the same file.\nOn PostgreSQL the unique violation aborts a caller''s transaction, so the\nre-read failed and the race surfaced as the raw database error instead\nof DuplicateReceiptError; outside a transaction, a duplicate hidden from\nthe tenant-filtered read was misreported as an identity conflict. The\nviolation is now classified from the error first, by the\nexpense_receipts_expense_sha256_key name or the violated columns core\nreports, and the re-read is only the fallback for errors naming no key.\n\nRefs #3289\n\n* fix(expenses): let a fresh expense or receipt instance only insert\n\npinNaturalKey() skipped insert-only mode whenever a row already existed\nunder the id, even for a fresh, never-loaded instance. create() with an\nexisting expense''s id and unchanged slug then passed the guards and core\nadopted and upserted the row without a revision predicate, so a review\nlanding between the guard read and the write was overwritten (status\nreset, reviewed money replaced). Every fresh instance now may only\nINSERT: naming an existing id is EXPENSE_IDENTITY_CONFLICT, and an\nexisting row changes only through a loaded instance, which saves with\ncore''s revision compare-and-swap. The interleaving is reproduced with a\nbeforeSave interceptor that reviews the row mid-save.\n\nRefs #3289\n\n* fix(expenses): never let tenant population move a stored receipt or expense\n\nThe receipt''s immutable-tenant check compared the raw field, so saving\na stored global (NULL-tenant) receipt inside withTenant(A) passed it,\nand tenancy''s beforeSave interceptor then filled in tenant A, moving the\nreceipt away from its global expense. Expense had the same path for its\nown tenant (and so for its receipts and links). Both now compare the\ntenant a save will actually write, effectiveTenant(): the field, or the\nactive context the interceptor would fill an empty one from; a change is\nrefused (EXPENSE_RECEIPT_INVALID / EXPENSE_INVALID).\n\nRefs #3289\n\n* fix(expenses): treat an empty-string tenant as unset, never a tenant\n\neffectiveTenant() used ?? so '''' survived as the effective tenant and\ncompared equal to a stored NULL owner, while tenancy''s interceptor treats\n'''' as unset (truthiness) and filled in the active tenant: setting\ntenantId = '''' on a stored global expense or receipt and saving inside\nwithTenant(A) moved it. It now uses the interceptor''s falsy semantics,\nand both models normalize '''' to NULL before their checks, so '''' is\nstored as a global row, never as a '''' pseudo-tenant (core and tenancy\ntreat an empty tenant id as unset; real ids are UUIDs).\n\nRefs #3289","tree":{"sha":"5f151e547554615ef4f1da7394aedfb7fa799d2e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/git/trees/5f151e547554615ef4f1da7394aedfb7fa799d2e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/git/commits/d54f3970e2ec510f8d3fb9b31d95677a1178995c","verification":{"payload":"tree 5f151e547554615ef4f1da7394aedfb7fa799d2e\nparent 75459a05c49c78fd5080557b0545f0b0d90be112\nauthor Will Griffin <willgriffin@gmail.com> 1790926244 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790926244 +0000\n\nfeat(expenses): reviewed expense and deduplicated receipt models in smrt-expenses (#3339)\n\n* feat(expenses): add expense and receipt models in smrt-expenses\n\nNew workspace package @happyvertical/smrt-expenses for a cost someone\nincurred and the paper that proves it.\n\n- Expense: polymorphic cost object (qualified type + id, one per\n  expense), category, integer minor-unit amount with ISO currency,\n  incurredOn date apart from recordedAt, recorded-by and paid-by\n  profiles (company or a named person out of pocket), optional commerce\n  vendor and commitment (PurchaseOrder contract or one of its lines),\n  reimbursement recording, and a review state changed only by\n  review()/reject()/markDuplicate()/reopen(). A plain write to review\n  fields is refused on save; a reviewed expense''s money is frozen until\n  reopen().\n- ExpenseReceipt: expense-owned join to a smrt-assets Asset with\n  uploader, filename, MIME type, byte count and contentSha256. The same\n  file twice on one expense is refused (pre-insert check plus a unique\n  index on tenant, expense and hash, surfaced as DuplicateReceiptError);\n  the same file on two expenses is reported by findDuplicateReceipts().\n- ExpenseCollection.commitmentPosition(): reviewed, non-duplicate\n  actuals in the commitment''s currency reduce what remains open, each\n  once. totalsByCurrency() never sums across currencies; a commitment\n  match in another currency is refused.\n- Models and collections close their generated API, MCP and CLI\n  surface; consumers can require tenancy with a qualified\n  registerTenantScopedClass().\n\nThe behaviour suite runs on SQLite and, through test:postgres, against\na PostgreSQL schema created by migrateSmrtSchemas with live parity.\n\nRefs #3289\n\n* chore(expenses): register smrt-expenses in the release group and catalogs\n\nAdd the package to the changesets fixed group, the root README package\ncatalog, the CONTEXT-MAP business row, and the Biome noExplicitAny\nstrict list.\n\nRefs #3289\n\n* fix(expenses): check a commitment match only when it is made or changed\n\nValidating the commitment on every save meant a later edit to the\npurchase order (a currency change, a deletion) blocked unrelated saves\nof an already-matched expense, including recording its reimbursement.\nThe match, line and currency are now checked when set or changed; rows a\nlater commitment change leaves in another currency are reported in\notherCurrencies and never drawn.\n\nRefs #3289\n\n* chore(expenses): align smrt-expenses with the 0.52.0 release group\n\nEvery publishable smrt package carries the fixed group''s version; main\nreleased 0.52.0 while this branch was open.\n\nRefs #3289\n\n* fix(expenses): pin expense and receipt saves to the row their guards checked\n\nThe review lock and receipt immutability read the row stored under the\nobject''s id, but core''s natural-key save adopts any same-owner row on\n(tenant_id, slug, context). Both models derive their slug from the id,\nso create({ slug: <reviewed expense id>, amount }) found nothing by id,\npassed every guard, then upserted onto the reviewed expense: back to\nunreviewed with new money. The same overwrote a receipt''s hash.\n\nA new row''s first save is now a plain INSERT (requireInsertOnSave), so\na natural-key collision raises EXPENSE_IDENTITY_CONFLICT instead of\nadopting, and an existing row refuses a changed slug or context. A\nrefused receipt INSERT is re-read to report a racing duplicate file as\nDuplicateReceiptError and anything else as an identity conflict.\n\nRefs #3289\n\n* fix(expenses): refuse a vendor from another tenant\n\nvendorId is a crossPackageRef, which neither validates its target nor\ncreates a foreign key, so an expense in tenant A could name tenant B''s\nvendor. The vendor is now resolved through the commerce collection (so\ntenant interceptors apply) and must belong to the expense''s tenant\nwhenever it is set or changed, like the commitment check; otherwise\nEXPENSE_VENDOR_MISMATCH.\n\nRefs #3289\n\n* fix(expenses): enforce one copy of a receipt file per expense for every tenant\n\nThe unique index led with the nullable tenant_id, and NULLs are distinct\nin a unique index on PostgreSQL and SQLite, so two concurrent attaches of\nthe same file to a global (NULL-tenant) expense both committed. The key\nis now (expense_id, content_sha256): an expense belongs to exactly one\ntenant, so it is already tenant-scoped, and it holds for NULL tenants.\nCreated by smrt db:migrate; live parity stays clean.\n\nRefs #3289\n\n* fix(expenses): refuse inherited junction writers that would lose receipt evidence\n\nExpenseReceiptCollection inherited SmrtJunction.setLinks(), which deletes\nevery receipt of the expense and then re-attaches through attach() with\nno content hash; each attach failed EXPENSE_RECEIPT_INVALID after the\nevidence was already gone. attach() and setLinks() now throw before\ntouching anything and point to attachReceipt(). detach() stays: removing\na link is an explicit act and keeps the asset. The batch junction path\ncannot bypass save(): ExpenseReceipt overrides it, so\nhasBaseJunctionLifecycle() is false, which the test asserts.\n\nRefs #3289\n\n* fix(expenses): bind review transitions to their complete resulting state\n\nThe transition token authorized every review-field change once the\nstatus endpoints matched, so a caller could set duplicateOfId directly\nand then call review() or reject(): the marker was persisted without\nmarkDuplicate()''s same-tenant check, and review() could even store a\nreviewed duplicate. review() and reject() now clear duplicateOfId, every\ntransition assigns every review field, and the token carries that whole\nstate; save() refuses any review field that differs from it. A reviewed\nexpense with a duplicate marker is refused outright.\n\nRefs #3289\n\n* fix(expenses): keep a receipt''s tenant immutable after insert\n\nExisting receipts skip the link-target checks, so a save without tenant\ncontext (optional tenancy lets it through) could change a receipt''s\ntenantId while expenseId still pointed at the original tenant''s expense,\nbreaking receipt isolation. The tenant, derived from the expense on\ninsert, is now one of the receipt''s immutable columns.\n\nRefs #3289\n\n* fix(expenses): limit duplicate receipt groups after filtering, not before\n\nWith expenseId, findDuplicateReceipts() sliced the expense''s own hashes\nto the limit before grouping, and those include its unique receipts, so\nan expense with many older unique receipts hid a later shared one (100\nunique plus one shared returned nothing at the default limit). The\ntargeted path now groups every hash and limits the groups; only the\nfacet path, whose hashes are already shared, is limited up front.\n\nRefs #3289\n\n* fix(expenses): freeze recordedAt on a reviewed expense\n\nThe README promises a reviewed expense''s dates stay frozen until\nreopen(), but recordedAt was not in the reviewed-field lock, so it could\nbe rewritten on a reviewed expense. It is now locked and compared as an\ninstant, because drivers return the stored value as a Date or a string.\n\nRefs #3289\n\n* fix(expenses): classify a refused receipt insert from the error itself\n\nA refused receipt INSERT was told apart by re-reading for the same file.\nOn PostgreSQL the unique violation aborts a caller''s transaction, so the\nre-read failed and the race surfaced as the raw database error instead\nof DuplicateReceiptError; outside a transaction, a duplicate hidden from\nthe tenant-filtered read was misreported as an identity conflict. The\nviolation is now classified from the error first, by the\nexpense_receipts_expense_sha256_key name or the violated columns core\nreports, and the re-read is only the fallback for errors naming no key.\n\nRefs #3289\n\n* fix(expenses): let a fresh expense or receipt instance only insert\n\npinNaturalKey() skipped insert-only mode whenever a row already existed\nunder the id, even for a fresh, never-loaded instance. create() with an\nexisting expense''s id and unchanged slug then passed the guards and core\nadopted and upserted the row without a revision predicate, so a review\nlanding between the guard read and the write was overwritten (status\nreset, reviewed money replaced). Every fresh instance now may only\nINSERT: naming an existing id is EXPENSE_IDENTITY_CONFLICT, and an\nexisting row changes only through a loaded instance, which saves with\ncore''s revision compare-and-swap. The interleaving is reproduced with a\nbeforeSave interceptor that reviews the row mid-save.\n\nRefs #3289\n\n* fix(expenses): never let tenant population move a stored receipt or expense\n\nThe receipt''s immutable-tenant check compared the raw field, so saving\na stored global (NULL-tenant) receipt inside withTenant(A) passed it,\nand tenancy''s beforeSave interceptor then filled in tenant A, moving the\nreceipt away from its global expense. Expense had the same path for its\nown tenant (and so for its receipts and links). Both now compare the\ntenant a save will actually write, effectiveTenant(): the field, or the\nactive context the interceptor would fill an empty one from; a change is\nrefused (EXPENSE_RECEIPT_INVALID / EXPENSE_INVALID).\n\nRefs #3289\n\n* fix(expenses): treat an empty-string tenant as unset, never a tenant\n\neffectiveTenant() used ?? so '''' survived as the effective tenant and\ncompared equal to a stored NULL owner, while tenancy''s interceptor treats\n'''' as unset (truthiness) and filled in the active tenant: setting\ntenantId = '''' on a stored global expense or receipt and saving inside\nwithTenant(A) moved it. It now uses the interceptor''s falsy semantics,\nand both models normalize '''' to NULL before their checks, so '''' is\nstored as a global row, never as a '''' pseudo-tenant (core and tenancy\ntreat an empty tenant id as unset; real ids are UUIDs).\n\nRefs #3289","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqv12qCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQSAQAG6L3XilaydvoIFprG4NDFzP\nG+UNx+sUo/t4Ox0pN3IG+AeqLIWcUkqwqduN2VWiEfg+upXmyOBhJKUbi1wkkXGu\nLUBv4BVMBVBq76VYguwLVmlifvyht3iJL/DjXUfX/M0Q5Hwlxw7WcXltOU9V9aYT\nkjhwBbKyBfhGpWVqnzGQpDivHe8LSm2aGyTIKlqRNkEVUSuEPxiORK0vbC1pNpif\nvNvAeVXeFxAWvPue8PfJD8t9aVHviAjlwWnFt7pz4pu6S7CdLkoi1KapwF43JEIU\n+IMeh/UjbRtFb3zc9vofqE4Vz6oWHlOYUmoH/uNf0BFNpGn/wtMNhJpmrAiDLifx\n87Bej/m8zLmoDvJIFeNDvKLYrwKDTIQukTxFJS7OeLbk6Duk4yxyvfN9c2pNTWSj\nRn+noGYg7obyfTh7Th3wRXq7ECy+GA/GKq9bs35HnPSkdj+kbIQd4VG2CYes4PoP\n8zNYl6oZXyH1skG5OWXj/OYe7ReQ/QOlMtPIf3qjIpI8ODhZvevdcY8VLNWgsImL\nDCfgCwHOmc34ZyTCRVe+eMEhHlR1S85rq+bVA6RYXqCh92aJr1Z9RGVxGv69ml4g\nhCV6Yj0MuTQE5EsOVeEar739l0kiK3K3GQz6w9LSL3SvQ/YqEFu1+4idJ+MeZdIz\neOLB0vrA6pqNoogLEMIJ\n=ZTAv\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-02T07:30:51Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/happyvertical/smrt/commit/d54f3970e2ec510f8d3fb9b31d95677a1178995c","node_id":"C_kwDOQDruXtoAKGQ1NGYzOTcwZTJlYzUxMGY4ZDNmYjliMzFkOTU2NzdhMTE3ODk5NWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/happyvertical/smrt/commit/75459a05c49c78fd5080557b0545f0b0d90be112","sha":"75459a05c49c78fd5080557b0545f0b0d90be112","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/commits/75459a05c49c78fd5080557b0545f0b0d90be112"}],"sha":"d54f3970e2ec510f8d3fb9b31d95677a1178995c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/commits/d54f3970e2ec510f8d3fb9b31d95677a1178995c"}],"requestUrl":"https://api.github.com/repos/happyvertical/smrt/commits?per_page=100&page=1&sha=2cdde0ee0eb4e2051c3424d4e5d55c6c3cb7cc39&since=2025-03-31T23%3A59%3A59.000Z&until=2026-10-08T15%3A51%3A19.573Z"}');
