/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aitorosabrooktec/brooktec-claude-orchestration-test/commits/2ea9764178cde065ee1912a07e9145c5cf3d98a2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-10-22T15:06:50Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-10-22T15:06:50Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Add mobile-developer agent to orchestrator decision-making\n\nEnhanced the orchestrator to include mobile development support:\n\n1. Extended technology detection logic:\n   - Web frameworks: Angular, React, Next.js\n   - Mobile frameworks: React Native, Expo, Flutter, Ionic, Native iOS/Android\n   - Checks both package.json and project structure (pubspec.yaml, native dirs)\n\n2. Added mobile feature implementation section (3c):\n   - Routes to mobile-developer agent for mobile projects\n   - Platform detection (React Native, Flutter, Expo, Ionic, Native)\n   - State management and navigation detection\n   - Platform-specific design guidelines (HIG, Material Design)\n   - Offline-first capabilities and performance optimizations\n   - Native integrations and permissions handling\n\n3. Enhanced ambiguity handling:\n   - Detects if both web and mobile frameworks present\n   - STOPS and asks user which technology to use for the feature\n   - Provides clear options for all supported frameworks\n\n4. Updated Phase 2 success criteria:\n   - Added mobile-specific criteria (permissions, offline support, platform patterns)\n   - Platform-specific authentication (biometric, OAuth)\n   - App lifecycle and background state management\n\n5. Updated coordination notes:\n   - Documented mobile framework detection patterns\n   - Agent routing logic for mobile projects\n   - Platform-specific considerations\n\n6. Updated Phase 3 security audit:\n   - Added mobile-specific security checks (OWASP MASVS)\n   - Certificate pinning, secure storage, code obfuscation\n   - App store compliance and privacy considerations\n\nThe orchestrator now supports comprehensive web and mobile development\nwith intelligent agent selection based on detected project technology.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1aa6c0bf57183df5c4dd2a4b78c38a7c20c31c34","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aitorosabrooktec/brooktec-claude-orchestration-test/git/trees/1aa6c0bf57183df5c4dd2a4b78c38a7c20c31c34"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aitorosabrooktec/brooktec-claude-orchestration-test/git/commits/2ea9764178cde065ee1912a07e9145c5cf3d98a2","verification":{"payload":"tree 1aa6c0bf57183df5c4dd2a4b78c38a7c20c31c34\nparent 2db76ff652225156c754bfe6d499331ef9a01526\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1761145610 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1761145610 +0000\n\nAdd mobile-developer agent to orchestrator decision-making\n\nEnhanced the orchestrator to include mobile development support:\n\n1. Extended technology detection logic:\n   - Web frameworks: Angular, React, Next.js\n   - Mobile frameworks: React Native, Expo, Flutter, Ionic, Native iOS/Android\n   - Checks both package.json and project structure (pubspec.yaml, native dirs)\n\n2. Added mobile feature implementation section (3c):\n   - Routes to mobile-developer agent for mobile projects\n   - Platform detection (React Native, Flutter, Expo, Ionic, Native)\n   - State management and navigation detection\n   - Platform-specific design guidelines (HIG, Material Design)\n   - Offline-first capabilities and performance optimizations\n   - Native integrations and permissions handling\n\n3. Enhanced ambiguity handling:\n   - Detects if both web and mobile frameworks present\n   - STOPS and asks user which technology to use for the feature\n   - Provides clear options for all supported frameworks\n\n4. Updated Phase 2 success criteria:\n   - Added mobile-specific criteria (permissions, offline support, platform patterns)\n   - Platform-specific authentication (biometric, OAuth)\n   - App lifecycle and background state management\n\n5. Updated coordination notes:\n   - Documented mobile framework detection patterns\n   - Agent routing logic for mobile projects\n   - Platform-specific considerations\n\n6. Updated Phase 3 security audit:\n   - Added mobile-specific security checks (OWASP MASVS)\n   - Certificate pinning, secure storage, code obfuscation\n   - App store compliance and privacy considerations\n\nThe orchestrator now supports comprehensive web and mobile development\nwith intelligent agent selection based on detected project technology.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQPMIx9YY\nqw0eGJ+6G+TAHOUdJn4FSJ+Fif8VdePn/eex9pxdcuoMKCobx/MDa44VPQFSUMeO3BYl0PZoXTYj\nLQo=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2025-10-22T15:07:00Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/aitorosabrooktec/brooktec-claude-orchestration-test/commit/2ea9764178cde065ee1912a07e9145c5cf3d98a2","node_id":"C_kwDOQELQTNoAKDJlYTk3NjQxNzhjZGUwNjVlZTE5MTJhMDdlOTE0NWM1Y2YzZDk4YTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/aitorosabrooktec/brooktec-claude-orchestration-test/commit/2db76ff652225156c754bfe6d499331ef9a01526","sha":"2db76ff652225156c754bfe6d499331ef9a01526","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aitorosabrooktec/brooktec-claude-orchestration-test/commits/2db76ff652225156c754bfe6d499331ef9a01526"}],"sha":"2ea9764178cde065ee1912a07e9145c5cf3d98a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aitorosabrooktec/brooktec-claude-orchestration-test/commits/2ea9764178cde065ee1912a07e9145c5cf3d98a2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aitorosabrooktec/brooktec-claude-orchestration-test/commits/2db76ff652225156c754bfe6d499331ef9a01526/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-10-22T15:02:02Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-10-22T15:02:02Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Add Angular agent and intelligent technology detection to orchestrator\n\nThis commit adds Angular support to the frontend orchestration workflow:\n\n1. New angular-developer agent:\n   - Comprehensive Angular 14+ support with version-specific patterns\n   - Automatic detection of Angular version and architecture (standalone vs NgModule)\n   - Support for modern Angular features (signals, control flow, OnPush)\n   - RxJS reactive programming and state management\n   - Angular Material, CDK, and accessibility support\n   - Guards, interceptors, and HttpClient integration\n\n2. Enhanced orchestrator with intelligent agent selection:\n   - Detects project technology from package.json (@angular/core vs react/next)\n   - Routes to appropriate agent (angular-developer or frontend-developer)\n   - STOPS and asks user when technology is ambiguous or unclear\n   - Prevents proceeding with wrong framework when both detected\n\n3. Updated marketplace.json:\n   - Registered angular-developer agent\n   - Updated plugin description to include Angular\n\nChanges ensure the orchestrator intelligently selects the correct agent based\non the project''s frontend framework, with clear fallback to ask the user when\nthe technology cannot be determined with 100% certainty.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"436da1355574444d86a75e28b6270c936e004bef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aitorosabrooktec/brooktec-claude-orchestration-test/git/trees/436da1355574444d86a75e28b6270c936e004bef"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aitorosabrooktec/brooktec-claude-orchestration-test/git/commits/2db76ff652225156c754bfe6d499331ef9a01526","verification":{"payload":"tree 436da1355574444d86a75e28b6270c936e004bef\nparent fd5b72ba8216afe455810b0a33fbbe96d10b38b4\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1761145322 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1761145322 +0000\n\nAdd Angular agent and intelligent technology detection to orchestrator\n\nThis commit adds Angular support to the frontend orchestration workflow:\n\n1. New angular-developer agent:\n   - Comprehensive Angular 14+ support with version-specific patterns\n   - Automatic detection of Angular version and architecture (standalone vs NgModule)\n   - Support for modern Angular features (signals, control flow, OnPush)\n   - RxJS reactive programming and state management\n   - Angular Material, CDK, and accessibility support\n   - Guards, interceptors, and HttpClient integration\n\n2. Enhanced orchestrator with intelligent agent selection:\n   - Detects project technology from package.json (@angular/core vs react/next)\n   - Routes to appropriate agent (angular-developer or frontend-developer)\n   - STOPS and asks user when technology is ambiguous or unclear\n   - Prevents proceeding with wrong framework when both detected\n\n3. Updated marketplace.json:\n   - Registered angular-developer agent\n   - Updated plugin description to include Angular\n\nChanges ensure the orchestrator intelligently selects the correct agent based\non the project''s frontend framework, with clear fallback to ask the user when\nthe technology cannot be determined with 100% certainty.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE